t we can add it when\nit's more compelling.\n\nStacked on #27454.","tree":{"sha":"0b07badeca2dc3e0c17c1c2a0b683e9288a956b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/0b07badeca2dc3e0c17c1c2a0b683e9288a956b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4a05d3b282a73dc7baa67f5baae0eaa511ff8d78","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKv3ECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5mEQAAZp9etYQeUN3matwiX2Qo08\nSKZQ8xcbstYtadHZqK83/T335akxLrFjmakaKjwvVIZ/WtmCM1i/O2tI+L0QMdVG\nMA6pr4UY/ID/WRWWidxLsyjFem/EHcg4rVN0J4JNcxmR+8ZNNb6MVN9SRLrMy4ry\nY9jLfxc7logIkyXT9KAdDl0L5+/O3p3ERBXxXft9dVAP4Q/2Ni3jUN2cAxqDdDiY\n4EidwMNltvjLX8emuTh+sOjvVgMVm1ZEBgRDZvPPLAvXVfMLtvGhvBjxj+NcoqKx\nqvMuUMMVdMaNifND1jaoaSR/1+jmu3BxNWK1D3yeC6Q5+U71zomv3Wz2O5nNvkfY\n4jFoocdRk9PwmYIWPvOT6Hj6CSYynBUljcxroShXRtTFMSWs6dByiyRGli7cD3X4\n5yzXjdieNF8oNoBC32uWE1jX4MNVbtqtZMr3Bsoz09AZ0HkAitMudLuxGAQdGwy+\nGBAD+kRRpDUgYBTojKk+onqNeRlZMaSAaLMArh+hYJD2Qs8yplv2eJi2nr8YuEhT\nIKK/Q4rTi6/8eNsRwdsSRRHnPblGk8tJx4U1xDB63dosdugG6PEuTi/Fi7gfORxM\nwVCi1VdGtyblvXPbYW3fNLEUzMKcRu0CyivZ22xI2t/7B/I6gYY2F3olajhtfj1f\nt22sVTZHJ8+3moVTbzMG\n=oBVt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0b07badeca2dc3e0c17c1c2a0b683e9288a956b1\nparent 0b08bbb9d93c2e9ae1ad79fe156084dcebb855b7\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1781202372 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781202372 +0000\n\n[codex] remove EnvironmentPathRef (#27433)\n\nWe're switching to using a static encoding of the host path in\n`PathUri`. We may need a type like this again but we can add it when\nit's more compelling.\n\nStacked on #27454.","verified_at":"2026-06-11T18:26:13Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4a05d3b282a73dc7baa67f5baae0eaa511ff8d78","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4a05d3b282a73dc7baa67f5baae0eaa511ff8d78","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4a05d3b282a73dc7baa67f5baae0eaa511ff8d78/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0b08bbb9d93c2e9ae1ad79fe156084dcebb855b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0b08bbb9d93c2e9ae1ad79fe156084dcebb855b7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0b08bbb9d93c2e9ae1ad79fe156084dcebb855b7"}]},{"sha":"0b08bbb9d93c2e9ae1ad79fe156084dcebb855b7","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDBiMDhiYmI5ZDkzYzJlOWFlMWFkNzlmZTE1NjA4NGRjZWJiODU1Yjc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T18:21:47Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T18:21:47Z"},"message":"[codex] Provide ARM64 MinGW powl compatibility support (#27323)\n\n## Why\n\nWindows ARM64 uses 64-bit `long double`, but the LLVM MinGW Bazel\nconfiguration omits the upstream `powl` compatibility source and does\nnot link the `mingwex` archive that owns it. Cross-linking the release\nbinary therefore fails with an unresolved `powl` symbol.\n\n## What changed\n\nPatch the LLVM module to compile `math/arm-common/powl.c` into the ARM64\nMinGW extension sources and add `-lmingwex` to the Windows toolchain\ndefaults.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n\nStack: 3 of 6. Depends on #27322.","tree":{"sha":"8d4010d2ba9ee5718a190ca458f54a6a3ced3e34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/8d4010d2ba9ee5718a190ca458f54a6a3ced3e34"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/0b08bbb9d93c2e9ae1ad79fe156084dcebb855b7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKvy7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWRQQAA6IG2Dg1eyWthOKZG7bPH6N\nBm1Gj19nwn5PP5IY6YlV5x79dfGZDn7ctcyvr0qbFBW/a+eCm9Mw2JmYgT+aaFZt\n0zZprqJg4jzge49Lhu+H9y4mt8MtX7r5X2yEbqPljp9ON5urcQHX5yPQQxpntsWi\nH3pQH6rhJW43GI2BpZka20STPHlDqVn4klfCGa7nRQnAFWz3VYI4W3/gyXGwCpja\nm+COgQi7ewLlJw6r+A1p4W9oHFsTUBze3xsyACmynPqwFCPANTqkgzL46wHCS0dr\nb9MtcCL0e7iRkEF9v0gs90Hrz/qxz7QuxgFCaIFazYc1+LECsrbm5WuYTphc5xNC\nQgYsxVSNinzeh+kkkQ8f4M8tSnw4DJjSRCKNz56jBNitNk8waYoLocCrn/KrS7mM\nl7ILqXx3s3dF1WZ1srxKWBlhI5bnN0/TL2pP93r1OmZO/OHMwNLd8WaL3kTZzC+I\nbggRKAWZHmaTXfG73N4dxmLnI48tzipe9mCGSjjeFF3liSjp5Z6ZnwDWhvnTRfBl\nc75NyOWdKIF3ETUwGae7yPimE6OVmB5FsGKEdCg2KKRiGE745kV+rLcUbMYmfEp4\nVAO9cE0ITP2X6CRVa63evM8NfGOO/QOaCQVoBJkNhCNJrTa9iQMi73MgQ/Q6acKi\nFT2gbXqyYC1k0FxdudSm\n=MSkJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8d4010d2ba9ee5718a190ca458f54a6a3ced3e34\nparent 267232f3afdcab931376ae31c4375a95ac84566c\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1781202107 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781202107 -0700\n\n[codex] Provide ARM64 MinGW powl compatibility support (#27323)\n\n## Why\n\nWindows ARM64 uses 64-bit `long double`, but the LLVM MinGW Bazel\nconfiguration omits the upstream `powl` compatibility source and does\nnot link the `mingwex` archive that owns it. Cross-linking the release\nbinary therefore fails with an unresolved `powl` symbol.\n\n## What changed\n\nPatch the LLVM module to compile `math/arm-common/powl.c` into the ARM64\nMinGW extension sources and add `-lmingwex` to the Windows toolchain\ndefaults.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n\nStack: 3 of 6. Depends on #27322.","verified_at":"2026-06-11T18:21:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0b08bbb9d93c2e9ae1ad79fe156084dcebb855b7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/0b08bbb9d93c2e9ae1ad79fe156084dcebb855b7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/0b08bbb9d93c2e9ae1ad79fe156084dcebb855b7/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"267232f3afdcab931376ae31c4375a95ac84566c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/267232f3afdcab931376ae31c4375a95ac84566c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/267232f3afdcab931376ae31c4375a95ac84566c"}]},{"sha":"267232f3afdcab931376ae31c4375a95ac84566c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDI2NzIzMmYzYWZkY2FiOTMxMzc2YWUzMWM0Mzc1YTk1YWM4NDU2NmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T18:20:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T18:20:26Z"},"message":"feat: disable orchestrator skills for now (#27646)\n\nTemp disable orchestrator-only skills while waiting for the endpoint to\nbe fixed","tree":{"sha":"d7d69d863b55ba5dd9cf56c4adf3fa88334aca41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d7d69d863b55ba5dd9cf56c4adf3fa88334aca41"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/267232f3afdcab931376ae31c4375a95ac84566c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKvxqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAddUQAI6sGumfv7E1jbwJhpjniZeS\nnprJky2LBPubOiL6anWOunJxpGHNa3J6Zxz40jxcIuLVPzer7FJ3dtJjOb78IZ9s\nXCFYQwC0ywTgwWN2UjBwz/aptGQ74b6IbDG8r/r0Mag6+wrexEHApStA/GaQMniC\niv4cJpVLJuP5FkddDu+pagMAxLW6ArfYX22UD5/DRIoY20WLF2cTnbE4CTNQWQiM\nPfO9JCT9TVjWZT43+9KltgjMDGOAadYalA/su+g33DCiCCINVzj45H0aaJln79Lv\nT+6jdYC6k8hbm0kStFLvdx3iPap0ZkwKreJI2LhIp9WK/REAa/lZyuvYPuA3GxKv\nxDJ1kiwGp+WIuqx91/FmUc1NDOqVwC0CmnXHG0YJ80Wcc2MfJpnQ4l2cb05uKY9/\nD3sikifyXVeGffO11CrYCDfAqBK9HPvdeuP7Ccj57uuTXpRJWFE6DZH4mEmcLtyh\nYNruqUKHY7DBTDoAHOC7J1UDHZQPK+6pfrusBM4z4AS+RcOrGWVtayhTLMJlq/yN\nekYOsedHeekIBQ1BCEcdgBH5ROvO/ngCvhFRBDVUnRlHhE5guzD3y4DsFJZ9cwuf\nQU3sBPwCE7+ebh1SzIKh7vVk84TrHS4jfHQbgVCY3aWiHjzk6JJTh3VYoXCLvB3W\nRSmwZfzrHjQTxzjO9WXy\n=pZYo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d7d69d863b55ba5dd9cf56c4adf3fa88334aca41\nparent b42bff21bb366d11b374a69197f44f96c09e1851\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1781202026 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781202026 +0200\n\nfeat: disable orchestrator skills for now (#27646)\n\nTemp disable orchestrator-only skills while waiting for the endpoint to\nbe fixed","verified_at":"2026-06-11T18:20:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/267232f3afdcab931376ae31c4375a95ac84566c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/267232f3afdcab931376ae31c4375a95ac84566c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/267232f3afdcab931376ae31c4375a95ac84566c/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b42bff21bb366d11b374a69197f44f96c09e1851","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b42bff21bb366d11b374a69197f44f96c09e1851","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b42bff21bb366d11b374a69197f44f96c09e1851"}]},{"sha":"b42bff21bb366d11b374a69197f44f96c09e1851","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGI0MmJmZjIxYmIzNjZkMTFiMzc0YTY5MTk3ZjQ0Zjk2YzA5ZTE4NTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Tamir Duberstein","email":"tamird@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T18:04:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T18:04:24Z"},"message":"[codex] revert concurrent npm publishing (#27639)\n\nIn https://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/27354608310, the\nconcurrency introduced by\n\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5e50e7e639c9284ceac24a5498b73a5602fb6615\ncaused the npm publish job to fail.\n\nThe six platform tarballs contain different versions of the same\n`@openai/codex` package. Every publish updates the same packument, so\nonly two concurrent updates succeeded while four failed with HTTP 409.\n\nSerializing that group would leave only the responses API proxy running\nin parallel. Saving one publish does not justify the nested `xargs`\nmachinery needed to express those groups.\n\nRestore the serial publish loop and document why the platform variants\nmust not publish concurrently. Platform packages remain ahead of the\nroot CLI wrapper, and the SDK remains after its exact root dependency.","tree":{"sha":"38fd35cb550d21ef4e5f219e40d18e39ca9921b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/38fd35cb550d21ef4e5f219e40d18e39ca9921b2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/b42bff21bb366d11b374a69197f44f96c09e1851","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKvioCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwgkQAC34EsIwii77rAE5bK/k9k61\nlwumGL+oqDrOAA7lQrYWnDyApSPmOri0HCD405+ZvghtwVUjfIqss4WIcqpXZITX\n2q2ThsL8Zv2X1JWSnGd2LQfYqQTqMRU5ELFK92JokvS1tKsH5omJelQZs8F5mdob\nSE9DmKImurZWmy4kwkgX8vL9+dvxdBjSbgF0E4KNZcYEhHYq3OPM29nDs9ajrFOE\nV4CPxW7pGVWxenyRX9PM3CZCnX4sPND9I6vEdCQvXhZyEezUFibyIitUxSUm7ELm\nI+z9rQHBDYccaa4hfy686YYbT3m3GjGAplSiIyXp4p0j6PUM0Drs5pzghsFCgnjc\n/n2x6kWCub7VC6QR5TQmCZO+bARgfnBanc7CMbBNsM+tMyfyffs09Ibm6hEUEP/D\nPDH82MitH5t1alCh5DeiaepjlQ/tQOhd6vTRbmJ+5Ux6+BdDbJVHvikhhpw+z9JE\nFmwenG7QiQMlBgcVb+63Mw1m8CGcv8cxI+afioagjp1bsFiacgPkbDaDVPyzJx+x\n7G7NTX6bTnsYiphTP+3aTbg4cAfBTjqr8uCU8GoCo58ZXqbNCPkkS3gGVJzyad3Q\nAEEwyDU4X+9WcgMgio55hinEq/wO6aoYhvQzWUHY1qgk+XW5B2PFGQ9fzbGbKXkc\n23dskv3WBcR6tk20+JVG\n=m6+F\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 38fd35cb550d21ef4e5f219e40d18e39ca9921b2\nparent 7fbbc9f0333c14c84334c68c8d2c0d5feb4ab9fb\nauthor Tamir Duberstein <tamird@openai.com> 1781201064 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781201064 +0000\n\n[codex] revert concurrent npm publishing (#27639)\n\nIn https://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/27354608310, the\nconcurrency introduced by\n\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5e50e7e639c9284ceac24a5498b73a5602fb6615\ncaused the npm publish job to fail.\n\nThe six platform tarballs contain different versions of the same\n`@openai/codex` package. Every publish updates the same packument, so\nonly two concurrent updates succeeded while four failed with HTTP 409.\n\nSerializing that group would leave only the responses API proxy running\nin parallel. Saving one publish does not justify the nested `xargs`\nmachinery needed to express those groups.\n\nRestore the serial publish loop and document why the platform variants\nmust not publish concurrently. Platform packages remain ahead of the\nroot CLI wrapper, and the SDK remains after its exact root dependency.","verified_at":"2026-06-11T18:04:25Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b42bff21bb366d11b374a69197f44f96c09e1851","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b42bff21bb366d11b374a69197f44f96c09e1851","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b42bff21bb366d11b374a69197f44f96c09e1851/comments","author":{"login":"tamird","id":1535036,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MzUwMzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1535036?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird","html_url":"https://github.com/tamird","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7fbbc9f0333c14c84334c68c8d2c0d5feb4ab9fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7fbbc9f0333c14c84334c68c8d2c0d5feb4ab9fb","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7fbbc9f0333c14c84334c68c8d2c0d5feb4ab9fb"}]},{"sha":"7fbbc9f0333c14c84334c68c8d2c0d5feb4ab9fb","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDdmYmJjOWYwMzMzYzE0Yzg0MzM0YzY4YzhkMmMwZDVmZWI0YWI5ZmI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T18:01:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T18:01:16Z"},"message":"[codex] Surface runtime warnings in codex exec (#27415)\n\n## Why\n\n`codex exec` drops thread-scoped warning notifications. Warnings\ndiscovered while a thread starts, including unreadable or invalid UTF-8\nproject `AGENTS.md` files, therefore become silent.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Process global and primary-thread warning notifications while\ncontinuing to ignore warnings from unrelated threads.\n- Render runtime warnings in human output and expose them through the\nexisting non-fatal error item in JSONL output.\n- Add focused routing, rendering, and malformed project-instruction\ncoverage.","tree":{"sha":"832f49152510f15dff0dbf72e5f57f81cf96c2a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/832f49152510f15dff0dbf72e5f57f81cf96c2a2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/7fbbc9f0333c14c84334c68c8d2c0d5feb4ab9fb","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKvfsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJhoQAAhxWxKfPWnjldCnF2BVprJc\nS+KcjXSaDkjKPxsGH0UDFkLjkMKCLkws2eFA/egGn3TJmxREdKj0MGOWD1kOei27\nlfYN6iTATb4cr3bt2CaCdo2Afim0MgcqcpafnWra2dyGVJ7D7+kOJ1quy0ygNclO\nzWzBRgVL3dF4uz2N4PAfp81CauRp6+ZB3yxAKVGTNToOjZQQc23Rxq+GOT4iGKfN\nrNqsFwZ//4tJ4iXgkqURWxcbDPqh6ElzpKEEWugND0KfD2xYAvuFCtzBsBSyhMpy\n7+CNhDxvQz0xaFC1zyj5Isc42Q/MMOqySFJKZyWKfZ2fvVGg1Vq6nSY+QKK4BVpH\nfddMdG7e97u5i8OUL9ipG2UafUkmGN6ddskYZFXjxjMB3KhhEiTQWioZPq0O74vY\n2RBJpmMvL842DJQeAgyW71h7oj5k0eHKYPRw/301npZxGFgJXJ/HfI5phzZEE8w1\n65HlD5VvzxV3UmOh3R+GKtChsM5B/pH5LIsumAjc7u4g/eT8rQi7LJkCob8Ux3nr\nTts8cp0dL8ywkzi49nM6eMplr+BrgXSXq6F0QxS2B4kOgacIcWrWGmpft4EIioJP\nCZOJCMQfflweVhTC/eJLV8Y0xC4LRx3dyAPMi2gJkHjiYVsdgjr1KwfIZJduezF8\ny7XJaUzrroaVwoW4ukfm\n=zKYX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 832f49152510f15dff0dbf72e5f57f81cf96c2a2\nparent cc97839068fa92c9e8c3c050d91de6c61ce47f24\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1781200876 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781200876 -0400\n\n[codex] Surface runtime warnings in codex exec (#27415)\n\n## Why\n\n`codex exec` drops thread-scoped warning notifications. Warnings\ndiscovered while a thread starts, including unreadable or invalid UTF-8\nproject `AGENTS.md` files, therefore become silent.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Process global and primary-thread warning notifications while\ncontinuing to ignore warnings from unrelated threads.\n- Render runtime warnings in human output and expose them through the\nexisting non-fatal error item in JSONL output.\n- Add focused routing, rendering, and malformed project-instruction\ncoverage.","verified_at":"2026-06-11T18:01:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7fbbc9f0333c14c84334c68c8d2c0d5feb4ab9fb","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7fbbc9f0333c14c84334c68c8d2c0d5feb4ab9fb","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7fbbc9f0333c14c84334c68c8d2c0d5feb4ab9fb/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cc97839068fa92c9e8c3c050d91de6c61ce47f24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cc97839068fa92c9e8c3c050d91de6c61ce47f24","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/cc97839068fa92c9e8c3c050d91de6c61ce47f24"}]},{"sha":"cc97839068fa92c9e8c3c050d91de6c61ce47f24","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGNjOTc4MzkwNjhmYTkyYzllOGMzYzA1MGQ5MWRlNmM2MWNlNDdmMjQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T17:53:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T17:53:18Z"},"message":"[codex] add cross-platform filesystem adapter coverage (#27454)\n\n## Why\n\nThe exec-server's existing filesystem tests only run on `#[cfg(unix)]`.\nWe should be running the applicable ones on Windows, and also include\nthe basic filesystem operations that will be modified by migrating to\n`PathUri`.\n\n## What\n\nSplit platform-neutral local/remote tests into a shared Unix/Windows\nsuite while keeping the existing `AbsolutePathBuf` API, and add Windows\njunction canonicalization coverage.","tree":{"sha":"18b8d51a80af4d7fe99b7c309a62bc1fc8917785","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/18b8d51a80af4d7fe99b7c309a62bc1fc8917785"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/cc97839068fa92c9e8c3c050d91de6c61ce47f24","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKvYOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvmwQAItypcoRifxwwgp2GIGSCtJ+\n0cuchpYo/pmB49kyp8uOhMOi/4GcPeNWTZlA+VAisqbUyy7zs2RrPUzmQE56n0fE\n2ERgeA6EXxI85jdRLygSWgl3/aMQ4IMYBcFJt/LiOsexIsvnf60R0PeMojDIRC1/\nV0xbcbkW8mHJLITtHrRskiYXrGiZBShDBjPYbz6UZu85RePHGL83FI2X7k4wAlqT\nc+54qt8YR5ql3ylNxzm+JSuqr3qtIMpa9/srvLqYxqXeuXQimbPzOUYSsi17J5ae\nAbNIIs47uhzNHjIBOU+uBvd3GsKiQy7cwmjGWqu8Sl59h1mhJ460rKOZ4sgmKLg+\nLHSmIJcpoNcDnMrXndjMi+ucCR5TISc0/Btp2Z7Pjri1DTJLxTAvVdXnnm7YumwH\nyVmEUeGB8yuEDE2z55NXuNBpb0g3rjqcSorXH62FD9ATz/JYns35WCOQEUiXw+Eh\nLJOIF/RlAO+61DFAJmV+Wahs2E8eKzaaZe7tj+cBGD8eAGvHnyAa0o09MKnHCx3J\nWz6KE0Gr6N2RUf4kwWg2tcuxNoJW/O7oL3s6cVqpu9LxZgbPsYTDH/i59/hYXSJQ\nC02TCg89rxk0R5T6t/yb/St9e5vKqmj7SrQPzZaF6dIcbIUMKYk3cgqDvi40F/5k\nUCZMtQGspkn/1Qwd7KPE\n=pMeJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 18b8d51a80af4d7fe99b7c309a62bc1fc8917785\nparent eb76336f60a87ba4a94b31743bd741dd37cf7577\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1781200398 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781200398 +0000\n\n[codex] add cross-platform filesystem adapter coverage (#27454)\n\n## Why\n\nThe exec-server's existing filesystem tests only run on `#[cfg(unix)]`.\nWe should be running the applicable ones on Windows, and also include\nthe basic filesystem operations that will be modified by migrating to\n`PathUri`.\n\n## What\n\nSplit platform-neutral local/remote tests into a shared Unix/Windows\nsuite while keeping the existing `AbsolutePathBuf` API, and add Windows\njunction canonicalization coverage.","verified_at":"2026-06-11T17:53:19Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cc97839068fa92c9e8c3c050d91de6c61ce47f24","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/cc97839068fa92c9e8c3c050d91de6c61ce47f24","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cc97839068fa92c9e8c3c050d91de6c61ce47f24/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"eb76336f60a87ba4a94b31743bd741dd37cf7577","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/eb76336f60a87ba4a94b31743bd741dd37cf7577","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/eb76336f60a87ba4a94b31743bd741dd37cf7577"}]},{"sha":"eb76336f60a87ba4a94b31743bd741dd37cf7577","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGViNzYzMzZmNjBhODdiYTRhOTRiMzE3NDNiZDc0MWRkMzdjZjc1Nzc","commit":{"author":{"name":"charlesgong-openai","email":"charlesgong@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T17:34:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T17:34:41Z"},"message":"[codex] Propagate plugin app categories (#27420)\n\n## What\n- Parse optional `.app.json` `category` overrides for plugin apps.\n- Add nullable `category` to `AppSummary` and `AppTemplateSummary` in\nthe app-server protocol.\n- Fall back from `branding.category` to the first non-empty\n`app_metadata.categories` value when building app/template summaries.\n- Regenerate schema/type fixtures and update plugin read/install tests.\n\n## Why\nThe plugin details UI needs a normalized per-app category. Some apps\nonly provide their default category in metadata, while others need a\nlocal `.app.json` override.","tree":{"sha":"f0553df666cbc562e3ba7cc1a6172cd137c93cd4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f0553df666cbc562e3ba7cc1a6172cd137c93cd4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/eb76336f60a87ba4a94b31743bd741dd37cf7577","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKvGxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1zAQACPV3ntcREtKxTw/oqBqLqbT\nUzBhe/4izqHE/sYua0c7hbyPptZ2jrJ4y8PCRqbZuM93Hrg/Sf0LKEfjwFQV7vom\n5kimoOZGFqlVI/1NObE7snlYyWFRq31TEjeGZOaCECODMBxODjeABOxWR9cSsyxl\nV8pPAoDtn4WUvPw6k5UQK+A9yNP66Co0kojY5VGrF23uRPip4e3A/5IVjYZZrq4F\nVrjR/oDEo318anEfcRiuC+MkvWZ1/bemiKQJwVcxghnsk48ebg9sUlaAPBzyGuqC\nTr702MRTGRkdHb5jT5QD9fhvvYQYI9XwbjP8TP7XzYZMEcuLsXlJdCa/sm1CuecI\nCFqz2ogIlrS3MS5eBo/b1L4hVKls1NE/WpeK8ADtX1OIP1Rw+Mz/n+LvY2pJqtOp\nWu1k9pq4gG6KSczYyfSXmwr8655D6WBKlQBrOdouG8Q+IelEhxRUJwQedZjDM+RL\nQ+D0GaLbb2818Ty/4jWIrRisiiPBd+Q2JUVaPf0rZ9crkKj9VJurpuP6z2kdm0WU\nOZmJoeqaVtVXijHBstx/7giavUiorekO2ufcoZ2CyVhCku4UclZjczMYvYtX68p/\nSIo3i7YXw3n1UZSWDMDfh4Xp+Ue3hDt7csGTNWgopW4cZduSf8oSxoAsYe9CCBGa\nBlWF8BGBVU/2cS/Cycen\n=4t44\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f0553df666cbc562e3ba7cc1a6172cd137c93cd4\nparent 52db447c77d19606ee30e3d20cd2591f32f9e4f2\nauthor charlesgong-openai <charlesgong@openai.com> 1781199281 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781199281 -0700\n\n[codex] Propagate plugin app categories (#27420)\n\n## What\n- Parse optional `.app.json` `category` overrides for plugin apps.\n- Add nullable `category` to `AppSummary` and `AppTemplateSummary` in\nthe app-server protocol.\n- Fall back from `branding.category` to the first non-empty\n`app_metadata.categories` value when building app/template summaries.\n- Regenerate schema/type fixtures and update plugin read/install tests.\n\n## Why\nThe plugin details UI needs a normalized per-app category. Some apps\nonly provide their default category in metadata, while others need a\nlocal `.app.json` override.","verified_at":"2026-06-11T17:34:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/eb76336f60a87ba4a94b31743bd741dd37cf7577","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/eb76336f60a87ba4a94b31743bd741dd37cf7577","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/eb76336f60a87ba4a94b31743bd741dd37cf7577/comments","author":{"login":"charlesgong-openai","id":200841148,"node_id":"U_kgDOC_iXvA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200841148?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/charlesgong-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"52db447c77d19606ee30e3d20cd2591f32f9e4f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/52db447c77d19606ee30e3d20cd2591f32f9e4f2","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/52db447c77d19606ee30e3d20cd2591f32f9e4f2"}]},{"sha":"52db447c77d19606ee30e3d20cd2591f32f9e4f2","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDUyZGI0NDdjNzdkMTk2MDZlZTMwZTNkMjBjZDI1OTFmMzJmOWU0ZjI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T17:24:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T17:24:42Z"},"message":"lint: allow self-documenting builder arguments (#27507)\n\nBuilder-style setters often repeat the setting name in both the method\nand its sole argument. Calls such as `.enabled(false)` are already\nself-documenting, so requiring `/*enabled*/` adds noise without\nclarifying the call.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Exempt a method's sole non-self argument when its resolved parameter\nname matches the method name.\n- Continue validating any explicit argument comment against the resolved\nparameter name.\n- Continue requiring comments when method and parameter names differ or\nwhen a method has multiple non-self arguments.\n- Document the exception in `AGENTS.md` and the lint's own behavior\ndocumentation.\n\n## Examples\n\nBefore this change we'd need redundant comments like this:\n\n```rust\nbuilder.enabled(/*false*/ false);\nbuilder.retry_count(/*retry_count*/ 3);\nbuilder.base_url(/*base_url*/ None);\n```\n\nNow can be written like this:\n\n```rust\nbuilder.enabled(false);\nbuilder.retry_count(3);\nbuilder.base_url(None);\n```\n\nStill disallowed:\n\n```rust\nclient.set_flag(true); // Method name does not match parameter `enabled`.\noptions.enabled(false, /*retry_count*/ 3); // More than one non-self argument.\noptions.enabled(/*value*/ false); // Explicit comment does not match `enabled`.\n```\n\n## Validation\n\nAdded UI coverage for boolean, numeric, and `None` builder arguments,\nmulti-argument methods, and explicit comment mismatches. Ran `rustup run\nnightly-2025-09-18 cargo test` in `tools/argument-comment-lint`.","tree":{"sha":"da3c0f78a1275c23218e99b354fdc27bb52f1e46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/da3c0f78a1275c23218e99b354fdc27bb52f1e46"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/52db447c77d19606ee30e3d20cd2591f32f9e4f2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKu9aCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVg4QAKlQwZgKGPSHhYuOe8Cda2cf\nnBpDQtelRv78ZPnoa02RQLEVraU89IXgUCXXYP0QpUBBWDQJUElCAiZi2PvN/7PG\nnKTv6bNUWysJg+D3mchtxtFEdbr6d3u4T8NhcXGzsl4XuWwdnqCCGzlfTWCMEEUC\npBByJcuQiYmYZIl2uTua8VktQrxhsk5ZQ+U3G8wsz0b+tR2sPqayqbmVEcEcH4Ys\nc2nzeRhWrcNCRmqSEKD+u1gJh3wXDrVnlIf37gaOzl6udpmL2qpzrSCDFGg5oLd6\n6Q1LtSna31jpp3WDCo42xgwIin1AUs3lx06HSY3YUrO55IQMoIYz2Dv7DwMAQBOP\n4M1VUWxS7l5GsLCwuCNZTX1TFV7vhl8vjj4TYW566y40pCUOg/kGIzHGJqEGbPab\nCbqdpVdrE7DWf1+IColRvtccKT33yDUJpWaWuM5WK1yWt198TVnIVOZ19ucKonAP\nPpzEToDmugwCN9N7DTX5xDdZiry1jH35UiKI3Zq25dsPDmxWE4Jv5aZrnPLg3VQi\npWWNQSQ+e5aRMc1QlwdrMFz6cghA8bjbwOEPFuF1Xl7G7T8mAwevovq+kus/d+lL\nb6rG3O3BUMV520ql6FxsNZVCRqMedyyNxcDlV1soLUcY/DPCOQzCgE8Tb+JQreP6\nKK2Qmuf63EDAE4eNa1AP\n=XW6p\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree da3c0f78a1275c23218e99b354fdc27bb52f1e46\nparent 9d88e299a795a00c0e57498302d02fa28f37de0f\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1781198682 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781198682 -0700\n\nlint: allow self-documenting builder arguments (#27507)\n\nBuilder-style setters often repeat the setting name in both the method\nand its sole argument. Calls such as `.enabled(false)` are already\nself-documenting, so requiring `/*enabled*/` adds noise without\nclarifying the call.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Exempt a method's sole non-self argument when its resolved parameter\nname matches the method name.\n- Continue validating any explicit argument comment against the resolved\nparameter name.\n- Continue requiring comments when method and parameter names differ or\nwhen a method has multiple non-self arguments.\n- Document the exception in `AGENTS.md` and the lint's own behavior\ndocumentation.\n\n## Examples\n\nBefore this change we'd need redundant comments like this:\n\n```rust\nbuilder.enabled(/*false*/ false);\nbuilder.retry_count(/*retry_count*/ 3);\nbuilder.base_url(/*base_url*/ None);\n```\n\nNow can be written like this:\n\n```rust\nbuilder.enabled(false);\nbuilder.retry_count(3);\nbuilder.base_url(None);\n```\n\nStill disallowed:\n\n```rust\nclient.set_flag(true); // Method name does not match parameter `enabled`.\noptions.enabled(false, /*retry_count*/ 3); // More than one non-self argument.\noptions.enabled(/*value*/ false); // Explicit comment does not match `enabled`.\n```\n\n## Validation\n\nAdded UI coverage for boolean, numeric, and `None` builder arguments,\nmulti-argument methods, and explicit comment mismatches. Ran `rustup run\nnightly-2025-09-18 cargo test` in `tools/argument-comment-lint`.","verified_at":"2026-06-11T17:24:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/52db447c77d19606ee30e3d20cd2591f32f9e4f2","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/52db447c77d19606ee30e3d20cd2591f32f9e4f2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/52db447c77d19606ee30e3d20cd2591f32f9e4f2/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9d88e299a795a00c0e57498302d02fa28f37de0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9d88e299a795a00c0e57498302d02fa28f37de0f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9d88e299a795a00c0e57498302d02fa28f37de0f"}]},{"sha":"9d88e299a795a00c0e57498302d02fa28f37de0f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDlkODhlMjk5YTc5NWEwMGMwZTU3NDk4MzAyZDAyZmEyOGYzN2RlMGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T16:56:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T16:56:09Z"},"message":"Print TUI session info on fatal exits (#27417)\n\n## Summary\n\nTUI exits printed the resume/session summary only after checking the\nexit reason. On fatal exits, both CLI wrappers wrote the error and\ncalled `process::exit(1)` immediately, so an active session that ended\non a fatal error could skip the session information entirely.\n\nThis change prints the normal exit summary before returning the fatal\nnonzero exit code. If a fatal exit has a known thread id but no\nresumable rollout hint, it prints `Session ID: <id>` instead of staying\nsilent. It also flushes stdout before `process::exit(1)` so the summary\nline is not lost during process teardown.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Apply the fatal-exit ordering fix in both `codex` and standalone\n`codex-tui`.\n- Keep normal user-requested exit behavior unchanged.\n- Preserve the existing resume hint when a rollout is resumable, and use\nthe raw thread id only as a fatal-exit fallback.","tree":{"sha":"b9b49e23f3d60ed7f865596aabe7b0b4420fbeb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/b9b49e23f3d60ed7f865596aabe7b0b4420fbeb2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/9d88e299a795a00c0e57498302d02fa28f37de0f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKuipCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoFwQAHVPiNeDnnVTEnLyO4udrfpu\ntmciGqD/V+IZiAfXElxCAX9/XB90elQdKF3SjU2z4TkAFt+3rT0GmJ0MdrBhpHlo\nOnsEhLvaIgFd0oNc0k+8XVYJMGTpRy0c2SisEb4J36aPJHsBEO4LQ4/f/6sAJNql\njusXnfaodZUDdAT0HcZmu0UhSyDaorErBWbi2ku/+zqbA7iDaLcmYJ79xTnELUA9\nNSBJ7cXxZiIYQmSi3sv1PF79Io1WhcCktSGdQZ95xbQKY4dtHqC4X2IA/bMDMPvG\nDyK/t13OLLH9gWDRtka29tr39PfGEOWcADu/RozzeAPg2cPiAjbnBjiLNJXz2kPd\n1JKGefO6pzWn1T1CMER88HJrQI9fji6bF8oi2TdgOzMCN2xF3kbT7ZILC28edIsM\n1Mkf9Brf2epF2LuJaaH44oH2USY9l8ZsmtJbrEy46a7MzdXYK0IGbj8T26gaGZtP\n6GWp/Qha6ydtuVgRDYmInrmpP96Rty43cZWHRKQc+LHEawhy+2Big36EE3yyY8DA\nPChZIDzt9DYCPBK1ask7CRKuKT15yR4uoucQyJ/MN9a/o6l5NX1ygS8HFpTqoC7F\nuAtn0XgYADhPWQqtUad4m9x6HBoAm0GU5jSWyD3VdCh4+W0G1ehLyz/3nIflnHL+\nAlxg0wcqXB5ubEln31om\n=VBf1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b9b49e23f3d60ed7f865596aabe7b0b4420fbeb2\nparent df9dd22248934a9558630d4e37137ba7aa9445bd\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1781196969 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781196969 -0700\n\nPrint TUI session info on fatal exits (#27417)\n\n## Summary\n\nTUI exits printed the resume/session summary only after checking the\nexit reason. On fatal exits, both CLI wrappers wrote the error and\ncalled `process::exit(1)` immediately, so an active session that ended\non a fatal error could skip the session information entirely.\n\nThis change prints the normal exit summary before returning the fatal\nnonzero exit code. If a fatal exit has a known thread id but no\nresumable rollout hint, it prints `Session ID: <id>` instead of staying\nsilent. It also flushes stdout before `process::exit(1)` so the summary\nline is not lost during process teardown.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Apply the fatal-exit ordering fix in both `codex` and standalone\n`codex-tui`.\n- Keep normal user-requested exit behavior unchanged.\n- Preserve the existing resume hint when a rollout is resumable, and use\nthe raw thread id only as a fatal-exit fallback.","verified_at":"2026-06-11T16:56:09Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9d88e299a795a00c0e57498302d02fa28f37de0f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9d88e299a795a00c0e57498302d02fa28f37de0f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9d88e299a795a00c0e57498302d02fa28f37de0f/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"df9dd22248934a9558630d4e37137ba7aa9445bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/df9dd22248934a9558630d4e37137ba7aa9445bd","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/df9dd22248934a9558630d4e37137ba7aa9445bd"}]},{"sha":"df9dd22248934a9558630d4e37137ba7aa9445bd","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGRmOWRkMjIyNDg5MzRhOTU1ODYzMGQ0ZTM3MTM3YmE3YWE5NDQ1YmQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Chris Dong","email":"chrisdong@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T16:55:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T16:55:53Z"},"message":"Emit plugin ID on MCP tool call analytics events (#27483)\n\nMCP tool-call items already carry the runtime-resolved plugin owner, but\nthe analytics reducer dropped that field. Forwarding the existing value\nprovides direct attribution without downstream server-name inference.\n\n## Summary\n\n- emit `plugin_id` on `codex_mcp_tool_call_event` payloads\n- preserve `null` for MCP calls without a plugin owner\n- verify the serialized field through the MCP item lifecycle test\n\n## Test\n\n- `cd codex-rs && just test -p codex-analytics`\n- `cd codex-rs && just fix -p codex-analytics`\n- `cd codex-rs && just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"dc43844a6a5871340b661956d4727b22905177e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/dc43844a6a5871340b661956d4727b22905177e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/df9dd22248934a9558630d4e37137ba7aa9445bd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKuiZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiXwQACTBcde6/omf+UC8kDI69qx3\nBROSTNf6DKQXXTU75Bc+BBBp9v5iyg3+bREs+MuhxnMhvTNh2iTQJHTP1HYsZ71q\nN+xL25U4kRj2SfYHCf+f4/h9OiM8ldF1RqJ6vWCWOsoHh6Eqijdy7Lotbu1BDGWV\nAtLq5nRpU+z0zTX97fI3f6++hh65eiVT3hfScylgVCUPYRCm3YK/BIPUniiAzYDv\nu75v54x7/AlFfla537WB24Qy4dbAO+qOgPSI5ye2zkQEc9wk7FWWNLKIg4nOgTLG\n8P/ZknkAkU5Myvnv3Tt3H/F6wwJ6qmlkviahdVTw+vVFXdqt5i9mmNuAe1tBYkOm\nZjmd+qMKx3/b03/9LcA/buhrLP5db5784iMerqH1nijH4OkCPOkR729En+Ix/QFW\nE4SwOqQ10XjVlbPkcfL+4rX1UOa0iHckuO/2z5o42N/DK/vCLCL5n7v8BX86dpdI\noGfRDNey2FR8t37y5Zd4+sfzu8Mu7Rviy21+cl48akyhhT4NcYJXz8U4HvAtc9U3\ngi7CE8dOyXX+zFgJC9Bp2IMkrgBQFW8e6CSlDH6wSXRggVVmSiyr36+HAcLIzJDS\nSl0okz8ks/kpeb5HVXS48dlTEX/WIr7pdWjj1FiJ+i36WpV+PqM7dKStHdu1aNlF\nK7gCeg33Y7W3bZhh1X5h\n=5l+z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree dc43844a6a5871340b661956d4727b22905177e2\nparent 1e5b87b4d77e5de112d1a15562ffb6fd68c1e0f9\nauthor Chris Dong <chrisdong@openai.com> 1781196953 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781196953 -0700\n\nEmit plugin ID on MCP tool call analytics events (#27483)\n\nMCP tool-call items already carry the runtime-resolved plugin owner, but\nthe analytics reducer dropped that field. Forwarding the existing value\nprovides direct attribution without downstream server-name inference.\n\n## Summary\n\n- emit `plugin_id` on `codex_mcp_tool_call_event` payloads\n- preserve `null` for MCP calls without a plugin owner\n- verify the serialized field through the MCP item lifecycle test\n\n## Test\n\n- `cd codex-rs && just test -p codex-analytics`\n- `cd codex-rs && just fix -p codex-analytics`\n- `cd codex-rs && just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-11T16:55:54Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/df9dd22248934a9558630d4e37137ba7aa9445bd","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/df9dd22248934a9558630d4e37137ba7aa9445bd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/df9dd22248934a9558630d4e37137ba7aa9445bd/comments","author":{"login":"chrisdong-oai","id":256211597,"node_id":"U_kgDOD0V6jQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256211597?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisdong-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/chrisdong-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisdong-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisdong-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisdong-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisdong-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisdong-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisdong-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisdong-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisdong-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisdong-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1e5b87b4d77e5de112d1a15562ffb6fd68c1e0f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1e5b87b4d77e5de112d1a15562ffb6fd68c1e0f9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1e5b87b4d77e5de112d1a15562ffb6fd68c1e0f9"}]},{"sha":"1e5b87b4d77e5de112d1a15562ffb6fd68c1e0f9","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDFlNWI4N2I0ZDc3ZTVkZTExMmQxYTE1NTYyZmZiNmZkNjhjMWUwZjk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T16:23:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T16:23:08Z"},"message":"Remove TUI legacy Windows sandbox dependency (#27490)\n\n## Why\n\nThis is part of an ongoing attempt to eliminate the TUI's direct\ndependency on core features. When we moved the TUI to the app server, we\nleft a `legacy_core` shim that re-exported some remaining core symbols\nfor the TUI. The intent was to eventually remove all of these.\n\nIn this PR, we remove the symbols related to the Windows sandbox.\n\nThe change should be behavior-neutral and low risk because it's just\nrefactoring and removal of code that is now effectively dead.\n\nWhen working on this PR, I noticed a big existing problem that affects\nmixed-platform remoting. For example, if you run the TUI on a Linux box\nand remote into a Windows box, the TUI logic doesn't properly handle\nWindows sandbox setup properly. Fixing this is beyond the scope of this\nPR, but I've left a TODO comment in place so we don't forget.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Move the remaining TUI-specific sandbox level, setup, telemetry, and\nread-root helpers into `codex-tui`, calling `codex-windows-sandbox`\ndirectly.\n- Remove the Windows sandbox namespace and read-root grant re-exports\nfrom the client-side `legacy_core` facade.\n- Remove the dormant pre-elevation prompt fallback guarded by the\npermanently enabled `ELEVATED_SANDBOX_NUX_ENABLED` switch. The reachable\nelevated and non-elevated setup flows remain unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"e8413bf0346957fc0ad45fd89ea07ec1c1a61546","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e8413bf0346957fc0ad45fd89ea07ec1c1a61546"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/1e5b87b4d77e5de112d1a15562ffb6fd68c1e0f9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKuDsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAMkQAJ4UWYozPI4cWU2F3nQ8/LvA\nueT5gdKFXkAiZOZKiEju+ZLy8MNsV5DZ+gcbElXAdo6KlJFnNUFBwY0sfz8Mmq76\nSJ/mzg8xT495xMJXysl9A6IIxKjUa2OwIPc3HNwHihJs343qL+tqvFT+5Obh3uuz\nysfW/9LPxC1aOmu7hjTPeAmqtXy0z3jvrCsr0gvf9awnZaNJh0U4OTUwwj2l07yr\nnhqZjAqaOeeKpImflOtl6sHn2vWmDxc8XcQEAJn5eCBtPdID4BcDKfWohW9GxJOG\nsepWqOVFxQC8iVRkMFqLYL4tPX3cO0dWSiwfT3gxnOH2jV7mIXvRAofxFQVeOX71\nXTLoSO5YiBehKx1BOBe0HEKxWGEGd7sU79+DAZoxkSNgaD7ycgtrg9iNHKqQ8F+B\nlT7htCqiwuZieCpaPRJ47fktnAywGfhEfrMZxb406w41pltZPh2W8EvD2l5nEsPR\nEVddZbaDgAE/tcJHv0WIXBj6/9zx1eDADMJ+1GshYXZZLo8lv/2xW0h12Q1BAwSY\nlq2hDoU3kp0Ep8GaWnzIAauJR57FVAu9kauiCuoe1HRcD9xpOFGsuZFRDi++78Px\nn3VLvRNj26HZa2DFSVE6lEYpV9/rf0S6hFUSkGPpBAn9M1LZSgzj6hSXvGU9B1zU\nsupj7+dukEYaknXYPSe/\n=U2iB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e8413bf0346957fc0ad45fd89ea07ec1c1a61546\nparent f42780109c6646463f74eb8c8cf484437fedcca3\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1781194988 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781194988 -0700\n\nRemove TUI legacy Windows sandbox dependency (#27490)\n\n## Why\n\nThis is part of an ongoing attempt to eliminate the TUI's direct\ndependency on core features. When we moved the TUI to the app server, we\nleft a `legacy_core` shim that re-exported some remaining core symbols\nfor the TUI. The intent was to eventually remove all of these.\n\nIn this PR, we remove the symbols related to the Windows sandbox.\n\nThe change should be behavior-neutral and low risk because it's just\nrefactoring and removal of code that is now effectively dead.\n\nWhen working on this PR, I noticed a big existing problem that affects\nmixed-platform remoting. For example, if you run the TUI on a Linux box\nand remote into a Windows box, the TUI logic doesn't properly handle\nWindows sandbox setup properly. Fixing this is beyond the scope of this\nPR, but I've left a TODO comment in place so we don't forget.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Move the remaining TUI-specific sandbox level, setup, telemetry, and\nread-root helpers into `codex-tui`, calling `codex-windows-sandbox`\ndirectly.\n- Remove the Windows sandbox namespace and read-root grant re-exports\nfrom the client-side `legacy_core` facade.\n- Remove the dormant pre-elevation prompt fallback guarded by the\npermanently enabled `ELEVATED_SANDBOX_NUX_ENABLED` switch. The reachable\nelevated and non-elevated setup flows remain unchanged.","verified_at":"2026-06-11T16:23:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1e5b87b4d77e5de112d1a15562ffb6fd68c1e0f9","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1e5b87b4d77e5de112d1a15562ffb6fd68c1e0f9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1e5b87b4d77e5de112d1a15562ffb6fd68c1e0f9/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f42780109c6646463f74eb8c8cf484437fedcca3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f42780109c6646463f74eb8c8cf484437fedcca3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f42780109c6646463f74eb8c8cf484437fedcca3"}]},{"sha":"f42780109c6646463f74eb8c8cf484437fedcca3","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGY0Mjc4MDEwOWM2NjQ2NDYzZjc0ZWI4YzhjZjQ4NDQzN2ZlZGNjYTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Tamir Duberstein","email":"tamird@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T14:34:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T14:34:41Z"},"message":"[codex] download only release artifacts (#27529)\n\nIn https://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/27308011621, the\nrelease job downloaded 10.0 GiB of workflow artifacts in 87 seconds,\nthen discarded 42 artifacts accounting for 3.3 GiB.\n\nSelect target and supplemental release artifact patterns at download\ntime. This also excludes duplicate Cargo timing files without a cleanup\npass and should reduce total release time by about 30 seconds.","tree":{"sha":"620125e7bd3e06ab50296378c138f3e58881927b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/620125e7bd3e06ab50296378c138f3e58881927b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f42780109c6646463f74eb8c8cf484437fedcca3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKseBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1gMQAET8wb8a/xL68gb7tPPHxuRA\n8l+4d67BsvhafLXFHzf7BU0Iw2FKm71Eo1dz8sXH+W2i7skIPtnZSFlhO2GR9WCF\nyXT+No5Pgsin1yl87DD7g1ywA2zSMZRnShUTtAbCx53MFOOBMahQC49E26twjHUN\nHMSm7IbEyXLF0R4vPIjpeHcReLKOTUndyP2Q4lqNUFPuijrmju8qei2kZjT+lnbn\ngW+wSRBlfTe0+W8EMKW6Vb2JZecXExlQLJ+GJKQwmlNMXnfhSoKB1gXbUrS/Ux0W\nJOA2eY5msuay987S1+/18HV8N6V+I74WRvcKCcGw3+IowxuPlPXxK9AVJk6siFm4\nOzz768Wzl2MVnO2F5eBUcqbh9oNN54SZCQiuZ3f3YugDxulEQw+9ifIDeI6K2LgM\nnWIUY0mvARoB3uh2QSzmqY9umbwtHtN/Q/6rfLqb6jWruKXNuuj5bobhrNIgVHtj\n7vLm5QP7FRkkLjXQz+oyxrMPY+Z99SOTOGxoPxJTPmDJ9gAM+Mleh+b2o5dkdKh2\n9cagJY5Yinzk4frOJluTri2ayu7vDjLcw6xNNcvMoVr/aLxlkQcy4Hu1T98QuP3d\nzDuvUNYWlWSWdAP0In4xgZYXWzTUGW0Al0y5PsrLRWoDF/XPd5d3kXcgRwaTW6EN\nmnP0Nz0+uak4Tmc91U3j\n=oinW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 620125e7bd3e06ab50296378c138f3e58881927b\nparent 9163c0a3351e21c39d5fd0ec6df79c6ad16415bf\nauthor Tamir Duberstein <tamird@openai.com> 1781188481 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781188481 -0400\n\n[codex] download only release artifacts (#27529)\n\nIn https://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/27308011621, the\nrelease job downloaded 10.0 GiB of workflow artifacts in 87 seconds,\nthen discarded 42 artifacts accounting for 3.3 GiB.\n\nSelect target and supplemental release artifact patterns at download\ntime. This also excludes duplicate Cargo timing files without a cleanup\npass and should reduce total release time by about 30 seconds.","verified_at":"2026-06-11T14:34:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f42780109c6646463f74eb8c8cf484437fedcca3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f42780109c6646463f74eb8c8cf484437fedcca3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f42780109c6646463f74eb8c8cf484437fedcca3/comments","author":{"login":"tamird","id":1535036,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MzUwMzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1535036?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird","html_url":"https://github.com/tamird","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9163c0a3351e21c39d5fd0ec6df79c6ad16415bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9163c0a3351e21c39d5fd0ec6df79c6ad16415bf","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9163c0a3351e21c39d5fd0ec6df79c6ad16415bf"}]},{"sha":"9163c0a3351e21c39d5fd0ec6df79c6ad16415bf","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDkxNjNjMGEzMzUxZTIxYzM5ZDVmZDBlYzZkZjc5YzZhZDE2NDE1YmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Tamir Duberstein","email":"tamird@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T14:23:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T14:23:46Z"},"message":"[codex] publish DotSlash alongside npm (#27528)\n\nIn https://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/27308011621,\npreparing and publishing the three DotSlash configurations took 72\nseconds after creating the GitHub release. npm publication could not\nstart until those independent steps finished.\n\nMove DotSlash publication to a sibling job that starts after the GitHub\nrelease. npm and DotSlash can then proceed concurrently, reducing total\nrelease time by about one minute.","tree":{"sha":"8ae68d583a50d77fa61512302f00fed0f0675997","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/8ae68d583a50d77fa61512302f00fed0f0675997"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/9163c0a3351e21c39d5fd0ec6df79c6ad16415bf","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKsTyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvAMQAJ47BB9sj3PeGsYnZOuapb9e\nljwCFnjCpv7oHtLWTNR8AtxzgeYrxeHTwVn5MkTJbjZ7pvVdum0SjooeHNySgN43\ne44YbqW+PPM9aps3AguXbf7jniAaRoHL8dcBunkvWKFVcwGkDtlAV2omFNZ2jtN0\nveglUNf98Lw3ehbkFEDC891a+77iiOdbYGecH0mhrkWXFzQRRVebLOf7GMoS134c\nuOLl2W4XFDRLEUnNg4Hm1pjZA7gRIvJTFZfNaFAoLdmRiMrzGWA3kWSspE2hDXVF\n1L4UnUS0UTPE974TCwdNDffGlUF+ODFjLggtSx0Lq30IL8ASJ48IWGpjJrcni477\n+iFNpB0pdPitKhqxJqD9OCAvoIl5VeJDhv+phgywBg92mzp3N9GPq4Pk1osVW0xQ\nMsqjBJhsbHNwMdoFASx78xJVzSPbl1YO2zWF9d1DpM6n+nixvdiPt0BNPWCxedbv\nB6prqmcm5bhhxRkTzopFivFJbqSwQ9gpPNaDFOWAa/YUBeTphJdC8XXCzHm45Hr3\ntt1Xe+kT66A7c+K+oxa0Zxek6s8mQu4D/4RxnB9EXLQCf1TPkY73497tGlY2aTOC\nqqQPw7oUfUuPPPR4cbtsjG8T4NHzUpgjLLCp1ORc+bjBXrclsFjh6Rrlsdzw8l01\nQzrFsZxL4j8fCIOSwLUa\n=LT0G\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8ae68d583a50d77fa61512302f00fed0f0675997\nparent 5e50e7e639c9284ceac24a5498b73a5602fb6615\nauthor Tamir Duberstein <tamird@openai.com> 1781187826 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781187826 -0400\n\n[codex] publish DotSlash alongside npm (#27528)\n\nIn https://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/27308011621,\npreparing and publishing the three DotSlash configurations took 72\nseconds after creating the GitHub release. npm publication could not\nstart until those independent steps finished.\n\nMove DotSlash publication to a sibling job that starts after the GitHub\nrelease. npm and DotSlash can then proceed concurrently, reducing total\nrelease time by about one minute.","verified_at":"2026-06-11T14:23:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9163c0a3351e21c39d5fd0ec6df79c6ad16415bf","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9163c0a3351e21c39d5fd0ec6df79c6ad16415bf","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9163c0a3351e21c39d5fd0ec6df79c6ad16415bf/comments","author":{"login":"tamird","id":1535036,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MzUwMzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1535036?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird","html_url":"https://github.com/tamird","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5e50e7e639c9284ceac24a5498b73a5602fb6615","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5e50e7e639c9284ceac24a5498b73a5602fb6615","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5e50e7e639c9284ceac24a5498b73a5602fb6615"}]},{"sha":"5e50e7e639c9284ceac24a5498b73a5602fb6615","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDVlNTBlN2U2MzljOTI4NGNlYWMyNGE1NDk4YjczYTU2MDJmYjY2MTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Tamir Duberstein","email":"tamird@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T14:19:27Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T14:19:27Z"},"message":"[codex] publish npm packages concurrently (#27527)\n\nIn https://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/27308011621,\npublishing the npm tarballs serially took 147 seconds. Six platform\npackages and the responses API proxy are independent.\n\nPublish those packages concurrently, then publish the root CLI wrapper\nand SDK in dependency order. Individual platform publishes took 19 to\n23 seconds, so this should reduce total release time by nearly two\nminutes.","tree":{"sha":"eeb3616d8f01ac8ef9152fc37ea5b69be73c5da1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/eeb3616d8f01ac8ef9152fc37ea5b69be73c5da1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/5e50e7e639c9284ceac24a5498b73a5602fb6615","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKsPvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1oAQAD5lyNgLUIFV5sbEprYLR1Ke\nUVE/y27FiZEh4v71/gBInZSopGsQ7MWRYt4SO6HxLY+pnzD/VCtq3Q1GtFYzC6D0\nKf22ObxFH3qJ+nwEgHlv9E3UVYSN0zK5TbITuQtDi0rtPyRbP4QOfuoDa5NJFnAW\nfLOrHk5Nj04RdM2NK8qpsyQZVLX/0KF6MGaSkmqe4/0cy1a9e5eZHtssiR/SiKyD\nNmrAuGUVZ3hBktVC3S+ZJtbf/FA8zlx3DoscQeOUR/Nc5TfdoAk/HWrnbHhWkKkT\n5EaEIMKvGoQWQ6Lx2z1swFq+kjYac6ATs1CKWtaxRTIUzvC05dbMOE0vy2kSQzRF\nZmjXNT4yRv+Koa4jtueRK/dmTJg7alQ73BVooHwExJvYFw0qguVaRD0RXqlse6xQ\n93NRShtnkHAc87pZGsP3ikAIBwO6oVL0f5Dn2ABUQvMfihXBXFb8KOiat0Q8fsFE\n3zrpQabuNgSxHbev50fAJSQN4VGNovPecz67pYvJK7NGnpjoqgmHGKCxOZypIINd\nVp9Z+VVx+MvRkZI7xr44/7+65jWsRtL/aMWfq1vaQBCD8Cu5/Zl53cJvffaKm/bh\n4B0p1NsHz+jVbkP+gADK/11PM6TlQEaXkmiV3FD/yppgRfxqSibxwAZWBOxPc8Nx\ntbVe1V6BdixWNkgDswHO\n=GXJx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree eeb3616d8f01ac8ef9152fc37ea5b69be73c5da1\nparent 7c2394808ed09b1e3aae254f12c027ff657e8f20\nauthor Tamir Duberstein <tamird@openai.com> 1781187567 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781187567 -0700\n\n[codex] publish npm packages concurrently (#27527)\n\nIn https://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/27308011621,\npublishing the npm tarballs serially took 147 seconds. Six platform\npackages and the responses API proxy are independent.\n\nPublish those packages concurrently, then publish the root CLI wrapper\nand SDK in dependency order. Individual platform publishes took 19 to\n23 seconds, so this should reduce total release time by nearly two\nminutes.","verified_at":"2026-06-11T14:19:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5e50e7e639c9284ceac24a5498b73a5602fb6615","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5e50e7e639c9284ceac24a5498b73a5602fb6615","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5e50e7e639c9284ceac24a5498b73a5602fb6615/comments","author":{"login":"tamird","id":1535036,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MzUwMzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1535036?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird","html_url":"https://github.com/tamird","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7c2394808ed09b1e3aae254f12c027ff657e8f20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7c2394808ed09b1e3aae254f12c027ff657e8f20","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7c2394808ed09b1e3aae254f12c027ff657e8f20"}]},{"sha":"7c2394808ed09b1e3aae254f12c027ff657e8f20","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDdjMjM5NDgwOGVkMDliMWUzYWFlMjU0ZjEyYzAyN2ZmNjU3ZThmMjA","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T12:03:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T12:03:53Z"},"message":"skills: decouple the skills extension from core (#27413)\n\n## Why\n\n`ext/skills` currently depends on `codex-core` for two host concerns:\nreading the concrete `Config` type and borrowing core-owned\nmodel-context fragment types. That coupling prevents the extension from\nbeing assembled independently above core and leaves context that belongs\nto the skills feature owned by core.\n\nThis stacked PR introduces the host boundary needed for the broader\nextension migration while intentionally preserving existing skills\nbehavior. It is stacked on #27404.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Adds a small public `SkillsExtensionConfig` view and makes skills\ninstallation generic over the host config type.\n- Requires the host to map its config into that view; app-server\nsupplies the current `Config` values.\n- Moves the available-skills and selected-skill context fragment\nimplementations into `ext/skills`, preserving their roles, markers, and\nrendered bytes.\n- Removes the direct `codex-core` dependency from\n`codex-skills-extension`.\n- Keeps local discovery, invocation, side effects, and the\n`codex-core-skills` compatibility types unchanged for later staged PRs.\n\n## Behavior\n\nThis adds no capability and is intended to have no user-visible or\nmodel-visible behavior change. The install API and ownership boundary\nchange internally; emitted skills context remains byte-for-byte\ncompatible.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Updates the skills extension integration coverage to use a host-owned\ntest config.\n- Asserts the complete rendered catalog and selected-skill fragments,\nincluding their roles and markers.\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n- Rust tests and Clippy were not run locally per request; CI will run\nthem.","tree":{"sha":"656977208752dc9f8978d0c315234babcdb55c3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/656977208752dc9f8978d0c315234babcdb55c3e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/7c2394808ed09b1e3aae254f12c027ff657e8f20","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKqQpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWMcQAEg2BcUElV2Bl/hxnHWequJA\nn3zkTl26hyybaT+Nf/ZXuvBHMDbqfP/4btNgR2j6AF3xatsGvG8ZtLqQkEbgUi3E\nCsx3CTdwUBomx3srldVsyhqy0NrBYEiZBhUfrmLQNqtq7IgWGF/+oHdItHEfdLZs\n0UyDFeHVDsMqKF5rGEZj73g5tBn/GSSI2zm9hvB2yejpPdYng+j5Z950jDpMdlkm\nOyXqkJjMvUgBErmlBeYFYnylU+6iEyEovlmTxOI6bSWNjvqJGJKqmckJCRthuf8u\nKRoDztxHVxWlmYfya9vHQoo+xGnrn6ogkbCZ7nSnVF7XcWz6JvStR9Fdyj+3RvZe\nBa9QFKw2W4sbgQb/YzsG9uKPu7cq4T6N9c7CESZN1U85Ll89e0+F6abUD9Oxp/50\nCFCYP7wuTwSn2u19yf1EYUaBlGSnPcPA2uGl17og3enS2W875lQFJXUDDEAuQTdo\nfdcrB+fEIih3Rq+Fpw5K6/Eb4Xr/1elO1+7Ru4leFvacX2E1dUMcevmxXdKAnV0v\nCHgnl/hcuL/2CdV4uzzza24dw6vMlYoZx32GQjcl/UEAoS4Iqo/oFjbpK2wJ2u9x\nk2/teu0+lKRwnuOISSl9mc/9XtkuLTUdUbJYK/ufMn5kqchWwrOeMaWGeqYwsAW+\njqgdriXgdqyPcmIufcFv\n=dDp0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 656977208752dc9f8978d0c315234babcdb55c3e\nparent 4322e01d2bef7b52b0ea91fe31d1a9c6de2dba71\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1781179433 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781179433 +0200\n\nskills: decouple the skills extension from core (#27413)\n\n## Why\n\n`ext/skills` currently depends on `codex-core` for two host concerns:\nreading the concrete `Config` type and borrowing core-owned\nmodel-context fragment types. That coupling prevents the extension from\nbeing assembled independently above core and leaves context that belongs\nto the skills feature owned by core.\n\nThis stacked PR introduces the host boundary needed for the broader\nextension migration while intentionally preserving existing skills\nbehavior. It is stacked on #27404.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Adds a small public `SkillsExtensionConfig` view and makes skills\ninstallation generic over the host config type.\n- Requires the host to map its config into that view; app-server\nsupplies the current `Config` values.\n- Moves the available-skills and selected-skill context fragment\nimplementations into `ext/skills`, preserving their roles, markers, and\nrendered bytes.\n- Removes the direct `codex-core` dependency from\n`codex-skills-extension`.\n- Keeps local discovery, invocation, side effects, and the\n`codex-core-skills` compatibility types unchanged for later staged PRs.\n\n## Behavior\n\nThis adds no capability and is intended to have no user-visible or\nmodel-visible behavior change. The install API and ownership boundary\nchange internally; emitted skills context remains byte-for-byte\ncompatible.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Updates the skills extension integration coverage to use a host-owned\ntest config.\n- Asserts the complete rendered catalog and selected-skill fragments,\nincluding their roles and markers.\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n- Rust tests and Clippy were not run locally per request; CI will run\nthem.","verified_at":"2026-06-11T12:03:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7c2394808ed09b1e3aae254f12c027ff657e8f20","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7c2394808ed09b1e3aae254f12c027ff657e8f20","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7c2394808ed09b1e3aae254f12c027ff657e8f20/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4322e01d2bef7b52b0ea91fe31d1a9c6de2dba71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4322e01d2bef7b52b0ea91fe31d1a9c6de2dba71","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4322e01d2bef7b52b0ea91fe31d1a9c6de2dba71"}]},{"sha":"4322e01d2bef7b52b0ea91fe31d1a9c6de2dba71","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDQzMjJlMDFkMmJlZjdiNTJiMGVhOTFmZTMxZDFhOWM2ZGUyZGJhNzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T11:51:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T11:51:04Z"},"message":"skills: render catalog locators by authority (#27591)\n\n## Why\n\nHosted skills introduced by #27388 use opaque `skill://` resource\nidentifiers, but the skills catalog rendered every locator as a `file`\nand told the model that every skill body lived on disk. That can send\nthe model toward filesystem tools for a resource that must instead be\nread through its owning authority.\n\nThe catalog should describe how each source is accessed without changing\nthe underlying discovery or invocation behavior.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Render host skills as `file`, executor-owned skills as `environment\nresource`, orchestrator-owned skills as `orchestrator resource`, and\ncustom-provider skills as `custom resource`.\n- Update the shared no-alias guidance to describe source locators rather\nthan assuming every skill is stored on the host filesystem.\n- Direct orchestrator resources through `skills.list` and `skills.read`,\nand explicitly tell the model not to treat `skill://` identifiers as\nfilesystem paths.\n- Preserve the existing filesystem and alias behavior for local skills.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis PR changes only model-visible catalog rendering and guidance. It\ndoes not change skill discovery, selection, prompt injection, provider\nrouting, catalog caching or refresh behavior, resource validation, or\nthe `skills.*` tool contract.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Extended skills-extension coverage for host-file and executor-resource\nlabels.\n- Extended the no-executor app-server flow to assert\norchestrator-resource wording and non-filesystem guidance.","tree":{"sha":"accf14680d2e4dd537773c8641f1268e995b2957","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/accf14680d2e4dd537773c8641f1268e995b2957"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4322e01d2bef7b52b0ea91fe31d1a9c6de2dba71","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKqEoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmk8QAHcyeL/JSNR4n7RklA34q0qc\nRLKci9Ct9gMoyPc6DNRzJqimxjZv57i2ox8Ln7V0LrgVLLwNYMX2E2IDH3INic+K\nAL2Mf36DbmjsEWFqoC1jMBg7RiJZKE7kCMBc86K57Do60gcy0sa6kCu3RNQuEDWb\nqjBrqy0ZIzbem2t40Ln7hDEkr1KhCvYaW8SkOhQZU3xdlno3ILAkDGMYELF5Z9Fi\nX7jglLmygJ+Nce+gQfJZNMFbvPdpbgEew+80oArTVb0CfhX1omMTXlpug2+iHRj7\nm8M1WTqQ+Wz/X1GoY9kR6JQzWD9A0qgA3He9bFJomem4fQzGm5Tn1oSaTR1qglvE\nzusO8pkc+IBLJ7N29Vn/kgWwipMwlud8MM0O4yhJXnasvGEiL/f+8dfGPC1MzJA2\nQKRoriXTk1Bzz7UZ73nWybJV/pYSaV0Sm4icw1M3KuslgsV4H8A4FwBNrVEw/89s\ne+R98JGOHybbH+djSkQQU0ptsK/5Qi24ctsGSfls+QAtA60UA3aBKOrlqCoJSU7a\n8q5EqPnIKLJIxQ7j+yDy9nGJLhYi79OG7H1sI1F9tZjy2fqS6d78S+04uGY9X1Q/\nKc2anjqDPyAV9M7UkJmRh8TTB1TfCE6zr4xfll2PYiHPx/Mo6H1ZYZTB0t59oC3P\nfWpFEID6eCkn6luJqQ+g\n=cPz5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree accf14680d2e4dd537773c8641f1268e995b2957\nparent dd46ef1aac689d6ab6aa6a73c4358bff07d70a87\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1781178664 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781178664 +0200\n\nskills: render catalog locators by authority (#27591)\n\n## Why\n\nHosted skills introduced by #27388 use opaque `skill://` resource\nidentifiers, but the skills catalog rendered every locator as a `file`\nand told the model that every skill body lived on disk. That can send\nthe model toward filesystem tools for a resource that must instead be\nread through its owning authority.\n\nThe catalog should describe how each source is accessed without changing\nthe underlying discovery or invocation behavior.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Render host skills as `file`, executor-owned skills as `environment\nresource`, orchestrator-owned skills as `orchestrator resource`, and\ncustom-provider skills as `custom resource`.\n- Update the shared no-alias guidance to describe source locators rather\nthan assuming every skill is stored on the host filesystem.\n- Direct orchestrator resources through `skills.list` and `skills.read`,\nand explicitly tell the model not to treat `skill://` identifiers as\nfilesystem paths.\n- Preserve the existing filesystem and alias behavior for local skills.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis PR changes only model-visible catalog rendering and guidance. It\ndoes not change skill discovery, selection, prompt injection, provider\nrouting, catalog caching or refresh behavior, resource validation, or\nthe `skills.*` tool contract.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Extended skills-extension coverage for host-file and executor-resource\nlabels.\n- Extended the no-executor app-server flow to assert\norchestrator-resource wording and non-filesystem guidance.","verified_at":"2026-06-11T11:51:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4322e01d2bef7b52b0ea91fe31d1a9c6de2dba71","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4322e01d2bef7b52b0ea91fe31d1a9c6de2dba71","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4322e01d2bef7b52b0ea91fe31d1a9c6de2dba71/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"dd46ef1aac689d6ab6aa6a73c4358bff07d70a87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/dd46ef1aac689d6ab6aa6a73c4358bff07d70a87","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/dd46ef1aac689d6ab6aa6a73c4358bff07d70a87"}]},{"sha":"dd46ef1aac689d6ab6aa6a73c4358bff07d70a87","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGRkNDZlZjFhYWM2ODlkNmFiNmFhNmE3M2M0MzU4YmZmMDdkNzBhODc","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T10:55:58Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T10:55:58Z"},"message":"test: cover referenced backend skill reads without an executor (#27404)\n\n## Why\n\nPR #27388 lets models read child resources referenced by backend plugin\nskills without an executor. The integration fixture should prove that\nreal flow: the injected `SKILL.md` advertises a child `skill://`\nresource, and `skills.read` resolves that exact resource through the\nbackend provider.\n\nThis is stacked on #27388.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Adds a child-resource link to the backend skill fixture and asserts\nthat it reaches model context.\n- Tightens the end-to-end skills test around `skills.list` followed by\n`skills.read` for the referenced resource.\n- Splits the existing app-server `mcpResource/read` coverage into a\nfocused test so the generic RPC path remains covered independently.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Adds app-server integration coverage for both the referenced backend\nskill resource and the generic MCP resource read path.","tree":{"sha":"5628dc19e6d37fe7432fee9bf30228f5929d95a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/5628dc19e6d37fe7432fee9bf30228f5929d95a9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/dd46ef1aac689d6ab6aa6a73c4358bff07d70a87","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKpQ+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnaAQAC44RubBITwkwXgxoQUJdn2J\nyjswcj4r3Dk91R9TwZ79US4KmDf78A3gFG95aaYwKL/VF/ayE3fUXktn1VtfCoYy\nin1Cepy8j1oSg0CykL9WchNMZR6M0VG1MMzSPtZyQ4LUyHEPuzlXpaEmr1AlbmEb\nEgtRLSUJAHd0pNj5hFm1XPwe6XKzInsKLCs+mvcrmrQavRL2WF4jBmSMP2g8qe7n\nheEuBj3cRcXu7CDo/v4rPYQ+qIZHXgo4RYExeifIsGQGfZt/uIKehylRykUMVG+C\nBqNTHori4RX+elF4YcBxnAyz7bfCdZmRuIXA+bvOmcbaUOxPIcgNYITpOJGC0NGO\nYur7ZqDgku2Wh6aKGzbJcFQB4ki9Fun3nH6LotW00+cZi7vEHQkwnNmskYdpLsiS\nWCoG9r6GNE5Rg/fH+LyTJvBQkvRx26qLwk/+UIv8asyYTu1lJQqVHAl/gWRQ91Kr\nGGoIVry0yEBqZiagZu66c8UZyHh9c5L2/rFbo40ltesvTLWQeHbg2VgWc4TrRr9R\nD6D6+oBWnmyVLGQH5WHzed/DHcY1xLrYhyHA4QCuL5rKg1IRbhEj2fn6HifvKm8x\nhlQj7OXeGES3Nf6pejp2KyHMTzl9evErOV7RrK87eV/g9x2WWNEy/cwWJLJCAHUQ\nIzlXCmb94WqmCnjMxs/W\n=cDWM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5628dc19e6d37fe7432fee9bf30228f5929d95a9\nparent e6757bba91f5cfb6c19c7e8ee383bea950d661f0\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1781175358 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781175358 +0200\n\ntest: cover referenced backend skill reads without an executor (#27404)\n\n## Why\n\nPR #27388 lets models read child resources referenced by backend plugin\nskills without an executor. The integration fixture should prove that\nreal flow: the injected `SKILL.md` advertises a child `skill://`\nresource, and `skills.read` resolves that exact resource through the\nbackend provider.\n\nThis is stacked on #27388.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Adds a child-resource link to the backend skill fixture and asserts\nthat it reaches model context.\n- Tightens the end-to-end skills test around `skills.list` followed by\n`skills.read` for the referenced resource.\n- Splits the existing app-server `mcpResource/read` coverage into a\nfocused test so the generic RPC path remains covered independently.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Adds app-server integration coverage for both the referenced backend\nskill resource and the generic MCP resource read path.","verified_at":"2026-06-11T10:55:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/dd46ef1aac689d6ab6aa6a73c4358bff07d70a87","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/dd46ef1aac689d6ab6aa6a73c4358bff07d70a87","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/dd46ef1aac689d6ab6aa6a73c4358bff07d70a87/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e6757bba91f5cfb6c19c7e8ee383bea950d661f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e6757bba91f5cfb6c19c7e8ee383bea950d661f0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e6757bba91f5cfb6c19c7e8ee383bea950d661f0"}]},{"sha":"e6757bba91f5cfb6c19c7e8ee383bea950d661f0","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGU2NzU3YmJhOTFmNWNmYjZjMTljN2U4ZWUzODNiZWE5NTBkNjYxZjA","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T10:52:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T10:52:46Z"},"message":"nit: cap error (#27585)\n\nJust cap an error that could end up in the model context","tree":{"sha":"59d3cea697831dbeee2565e4bceeb3654596cf9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/59d3cea697831dbeee2565e4bceeb3654596cf9a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e6757bba91f5cfb6c19c7e8ee383bea950d661f0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKpN+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsFQQACBrPS+n5EUSD2pJFT5wNg1v\nNI0n1jOd6OhhasmcLb7XfQpE1ytDqnlr/Y2iEOb0U6U2Jh3Ms9aBywKZeBkfsPVS\nfC8unHtU6BhmC1mFdoDO/iEISkLZfAypVDXM0hcp2yHMMVE6hNLhvhapk6oFeDHd\nZCvfEh7/Y75LCbVrCLNt/uM4NRKs0EAL3mcuUnx0r4UEtWS+iZOdQvDpQuz6dDmB\nEGuY4PlOLTD02946Api4QRq1eafwSniWF4eq+03VLhk+dMZhGU6X34Ien2tZc4VX\njJcIwLQekV8WtUFFcJ0nLDjgOjeg9aHU9a9vJkZ0W5RfJh2cbNun1b5r2bMcHQ2k\nuKttL1vCJjxccnX1hbD7UFq53nJpn+/UiFSOD9W/J3hg69sjhzfe9WSnBj5uoWcU\nL2QUJ/I6oUDLxwVnP+874Y7S/D3nD0uuTX/n3EaW9LPIuPt1GUZiqI5Okn3/1wnD\n1+53raZOEQptKXGsCzmx92rBClade5Vtrt0jfchUdTtjbi4LEv/VM7afaI9I03eq\nmdNm93bA6haHLsSm2cvLIrek5Hew7AnLhWEW49zAn6uaxKn2NO/o8JJN/r/lZ9or\n/8PlmJ5wiZlsez2aHXtOaLTxF6NGCA6KGptxPDlXjwVJtuNMFonV36F4YUSsx9Yg\nOpb3gM2m4Z2I4VT+3F6C\n=hc7Z\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 59d3cea697831dbeee2565e4bceeb3654596cf9a\nparent 087035224123977defc7fda6e684088395b1d0a0\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1781175166 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781175166 +0200\n\nnit: cap error (#27585)\n\nJust cap an error that could end up in the model context","verified_at":"2026-06-11T10:52:46Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e6757bba91f5cfb6c19c7e8ee383bea950d661f0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e6757bba91f5cfb6c19c7e8ee383bea950d661f0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e6757bba91f5cfb6c19c7e8ee383bea950d661f0/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"087035224123977defc7fda6e684088395b1d0a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/087035224123977defc7fda6e684088395b1d0a0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/087035224123977defc7fda6e684088395b1d0a0"}]},{"sha":"087035224123977defc7fda6e684088395b1d0a0","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDA4NzAzNTIyNDEyMzk3N2RlZmM3ZmRhNmU2ODQwODgzOTViMWQwYTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T10:41:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T10:41:44Z"},"message":"multi-agent: move concurrency guidance into v2 usage hints (#27569)\n\n## Why\n\nNative Codex currently teaches multi-agent concurrency through the\n`spawn_agent` tool description, while bridge-driven evals frame the same\nlimit as a shared pool of active agent slots. That mismatch makes the\nmodel-facing story harder to reason about, especially because the\ntool-level wording does not make it explicit that the limit covers the\nwhole agent team, including the current agent.\n\nThis change gives native Codex the same mental model: tell the root\nagent and subagents how many active slots exist, and remove the separate\n`spawn_agent` limit wording.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Extend the built-in `multi_agent_v2` root and subagent usage hints\nwith shared-slot guidance derived from the resolved\n`max_concurrent_threads_per_session` value.\n- Keep the complete default hints in `MultiAgentV2Config` so initial\ncontext and forked histories consume the same canonical strings.\n- Drop the redundant `spawn_agent` description text and remove the\nnow-unused limit plumbing from the tool spec path.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core usage_hint`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nmulti_agent_v2_default_session_thread_cap_counts_root`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nmulti_agent_v2_default_usage_hints_use_configured_thread_cap`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nspawn_agent_tool_v2_requires_task_name_and_lists_visible_models`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nmulti_agent_feature_selects_one_agent_tool_family`","tree":{"sha":"b35ec03d1eb2544fc8560f2db463a2b35e7df236","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/b35ec03d1eb2544fc8560f2db463a2b35e7df236"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/087035224123977defc7fda6e684088395b1d0a0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKpDoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFfAQABM0J5Z2AoBEqkLOnpmLSSfU\nRfJsurBMv3UaL60s9oihSlK/slynigQbOz2lhCuFwT6vVHk9HZsDbKscgVIGOeNu\nOxENaKLXVlwyenHzS6grt2RnZf/ajlIUDMHRI65I0iOnTIjZEqZPNStwn34cl+ly\noZ2paCQxCZ4agHVTfMKbQ7OF8qXRlX5F7kpI/OkjAWfk/Tjlkxpux1/9XuPvuq3p\nN18kucTImF7EtSF+Euql9n7A1rA68NpNuN5xCmT0clufZaegYryp/ZMKm9YhaVLT\np4BBMZ2n3GvyIZ1v74352GG4FJtnBFW0bUEzQSyaLrYual6Vo75VYsnyZGjGwIoe\nph77ihgpr9QHljwiqWl7CbjM6aJ475TH6//l2D2GEL8wuroZYabHQ6GhYW/hksWU\n3J3KQ38YSV1gA3mnUNO7OU40gFM7+GDonKRjgq9WDqa0Dcaktno0jtceT3HIB6cx\npaYenkaoQImebY9zPEbCJwSSuAetFTWhB3OGsXFpyPbO3es6K4qblUe7uOLLb1zG\nC9kforrBb6uUNGZ2mTIkRVcbia4/tv4VNktLtZQJHO2GDdW3jF1HytbbW4Cf8/8B\nk5ikBUm5YaE08tWPYGizxJb0YpU4hY/foFotyOpvM2GDU5mWRbHEwUPq6vHdDfJ+\nUg6DyWtv9dfHn5uEyd0h\n=7spI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b35ec03d1eb2544fc8560f2db463a2b35e7df236\nparent 7b3eb8e4bcacc55cda6d5fb4d31a06b36351749b\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1781174504 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781174504 +0200\n\nmulti-agent: move concurrency guidance into v2 usage hints (#27569)\n\n## Why\n\nNative Codex currently teaches multi-agent concurrency through the\n`spawn_agent` tool description, while bridge-driven evals frame the same\nlimit as a shared pool of active agent slots. That mismatch makes the\nmodel-facing story harder to reason about, especially because the\ntool-level wording does not make it explicit that the limit covers the\nwhole agent team, including the current agent.\n\nThis change gives native Codex the same mental model: tell the root\nagent and subagents how many active slots exist, and remove the separate\n`spawn_agent` limit wording.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Extend the built-in `multi_agent_v2` root and subagent usage hints\nwith shared-slot guidance derived from the resolved\n`max_concurrent_threads_per_session` value.\n- Keep the complete default hints in `MultiAgentV2Config` so initial\ncontext and forked histories consume the same canonical strings.\n- Drop the redundant `spawn_agent` description text and remove the\nnow-unused limit plumbing from the tool spec path.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core usage_hint`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nmulti_agent_v2_default_session_thread_cap_counts_root`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nmulti_agent_v2_default_usage_hints_use_configured_thread_cap`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nspawn_agent_tool_v2_requires_task_name_and_lists_visible_models`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nmulti_agent_feature_selects_one_agent_tool_family`","verified_at":"2026-06-11T10:41:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/087035224123977defc7fda6e684088395b1d0a0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/087035224123977defc7fda6e684088395b1d0a0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/087035224123977defc7fda6e684088395b1d0a0/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7b3eb8e4bcacc55cda6d5fb4d31a06b36351749b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7b3eb8e4bcacc55cda6d5fb4d31a06b36351749b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7b3eb8e4bcacc55cda6d5fb4d31a06b36351749b"}]},{"sha":"7b3eb8e4bcacc55cda6d5fb4d31a06b36351749b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDdiM2ViOGU0YmNhY2M1NWNkYTZkNWZiNGQzMWEwNmIzNjM1MTc0OWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T10:38:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T10:38:04Z"},"message":"skills: expose remote skill resource tools (#27388)\n\n## Why\n\nPR #27387 makes backend plugin skills discoverable and invocable without\nan executor, but resources referenced by those skills still sit behind\nthe generic MCP resource surface. The model needs a skills-owned API\nthat preserves the provider authority and package boundary instead of\ntreating remote resources like local files.\n\nThis is stacked on #27387.\n\n## What\n\n- Adds one `skills` namespace with bounded `list` and `read` tools for\nremote skill providers.\n- Revalidates `authority + package` against the live remote catalog on\nevery read, then routes the opaque resource ID back through that\nprovider.\n- Allows the backend provider to read canonical child `skill://`\nresources while rejecting cross-package, non-canonical, query, fragment,\nand traversal-shaped URIs.\n- Caps each serialized tool result at 8 KB. Lists are paginated; reads\nreturn an opaque continuation cursor.\n- Marks the JSON output as external context so memory generation can\napply its normal suppression policy.\n- Deliberately does not add `skills.search`; that waits for a bounded\nplugin-service search contract.\n\n## Tool contract\n\nPseudo-Python matching the wire shape:\n\n```python\nfrom typing import Literal, NotRequired, TypedDict\n\n\nclass RemoteSkillAuthority(TypedDict):\n    kind: Literal[\"remote\"]\n    id: str  # e.g. \"codex_apps\"\n\n\nclass RemoteSkill(TypedDict):\n    authority: RemoteSkillAuthority\n    package: str  # opaque provider-owned package ID\n    name: str\n    description: str\n    main_resource: str  # opaque provider-owned SKILL.md ID\n\n\nclass SkillsListParams(TypedDict):\n    cursor: NotRequired[str]\n\n\nclass SkillsListResult(TypedDict):\n    skills: list[RemoteSkill]\n    next_cursor: str | None\n    warnings: list[str]\n    truncated: bool\n\n\nclass SkillsReadParams(TypedDict):\n    authority: RemoteSkillAuthority  # copied from skills.list\n    package: str  # copied from skills.list\n    resource: str  # provider-owned child resource ID\n    cursor: NotRequired[str]  # copy next_cursor to continue\n\n\nclass SkillsReadResult(TypedDict):\n    resource: str\n    contents: str\n    next_cursor: str | None\n    truncated: bool\n\n\nclass Skills:\n    def list(self, params: SkillsListParams) -> SkillsListResult: ...\n    def read(self, params: SkillsReadParams) -> SkillsReadResult: ...\n```\n\nThere is one namespace for all remote skills, not one tool or MCP server\nper skill. No resource ID is converted into a filesystem path.\n\n## Backend dependency\n\n`/ps/mcp` must support direct reads of child resources such as\n`skill://plugin_demo/deploy/references/deploy.md`. This PR implements\nand tests the Codex side of that contract; production child reads remain\ndependent on the corresponding plugin-service support. Search remains\nout of scope until that service exposes a bounded search/resource API.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Added an app-server integration test covering `skills.list` followed\nby `skills.read` with no executor.\n- Ran `just fmt`.\n- Ran `just bazel-lock-update` and `just bazel-lock-check`.\n- Did not run Rust tests or Clippy locally, per request; CI will run\nthem.","tree":{"sha":"0a76502dd9d4ae56b6c632991f18015d16644469","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/0a76502dd9d4ae56b6c632991f18015d16644469"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/7b3eb8e4bcacc55cda6d5fb4d31a06b36351749b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKpAMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWnQQAAe8guujXY7TBu6haYmYV0cu\nt4wYC5dCWSkJ0KSzU6Lp1hmjEJO2CMLg1sXIIThk0lNNFfhRmvFbKsTzW+HfatTF\n4ceIX60bMZzROLe1xvGM16KqHMff4eLyE5YAJjALTqnEXtq5ox9iS5fTFyhlu4YE\na5rKe2x78C3dLwBUPrK4SAT64C6gW5Qr79/HgRmxosEtLKBvHpRa4HTsGaUlwfuI\nDxKBLh/fB/LDSyu7X2NBoXoArJGjAnplAEtWNjYBxaW5o3PkZ/bUqnGHpYnMF3vU\nMKRcUMJX4BUOvIta0G1CDx+hW8PpVEKbmsSwuaqxzpjo295E8/oRTraXRE5iN2dC\n6KPxAXVtQGnL70J3QWk6fMwOFb7hFMCD68EjtXQpAgXIOK2NAADvD2dZbuP5Ddgx\nTO7/xjXmV223VBMSfCio4NjFUM8aBelNZk8atKSMHHJfpbSaxWM0RkmN5xvDugvD\natBFtv+vgVuwtwTGB0jOumJ80RI+7WJ7PD91xSWqnpp5N/0CNEGK6jvsodwxRP5W\nBt7x0KkUycKgDOm7DaPqS6/c5cGVIPdJCLMg3tPsBZs6Rj0s/45d94Uge3Y6vfA2\npimwIiAiXdT/xAFn6FnZJ4BqJQXevL9cv8qUZI1ppywtPztkuLGRsRlylqDmM5O5\nL0iBbzL0GoRzxzaqem1l\n=7JHz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0a76502dd9d4ae56b6c632991f18015d16644469\nparent 273a4aa4f2474b9d27a2654f5803d51f65ce3f43\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1781174284 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781174284 +0200\n\nskills: expose remote skill resource tools (#27388)\n\n## Why\n\nPR #27387 makes backend plugin skills discoverable and invocable without\nan executor, but resources referenced by those skills still sit behind\nthe generic MCP resource surface. The model needs a skills-owned API\nthat preserves the provider authority and package boundary instead of\ntreating remote resources like local files.\n\nThis is stacked on #27387.\n\n## What\n\n- Adds one `skills` namespace with bounded `list` and `read` tools for\nremote skill providers.\n- Revalidates `authority + package` against the live remote catalog on\nevery read, then routes the opaque resource ID back through that\nprovider.\n- Allows the backend provider to read canonical child `skill://`\nresources while rejecting cross-package, non-canonical, query, fragment,\nand traversal-shaped URIs.\n- Caps each serialized tool result at 8 KB. Lists are paginated; reads\nreturn an opaque continuation cursor.\n- Marks the JSON output as external context so memory generation can\napply its normal suppression policy.\n- Deliberately does not add `skills.search`; that waits for a bounded\nplugin-service search contract.\n\n## Tool contract\n\nPseudo-Python matching the wire shape:\n\n```python\nfrom typing import Literal, NotRequired, TypedDict\n\n\nclass RemoteSkillAuthority(TypedDict):\n    kind: Literal[\"remote\"]\n    id: str  # e.g. \"codex_apps\"\n\n\nclass RemoteSkill(TypedDict):\n    authority: RemoteSkillAuthority\n    package: str  # opaque provider-owned package ID\n    name: str\n    description: str\n    main_resource: str  # opaque provider-owned SKILL.md ID\n\n\nclass SkillsListParams(TypedDict):\n    cursor: NotRequired[str]\n\n\nclass SkillsListResult(TypedDict):\n    skills: list[RemoteSkill]\n    next_cursor: str | None\n    warnings: list[str]\n    truncated: bool\n\n\nclass SkillsReadParams(TypedDict):\n    authority: RemoteSkillAuthority  # copied from skills.list\n    package: str  # copied from skills.list\n    resource: str  # provider-owned child resource ID\n    cursor: NotRequired[str]  # copy next_cursor to continue\n\n\nclass SkillsReadResult(TypedDict):\n    resource: str\n    contents: str\n    next_cursor: str | None\n    truncated: bool\n\n\nclass Skills:\n    def list(self, params: SkillsListParams) -> SkillsListResult: ...\n    def read(self, params: SkillsReadParams) -> SkillsReadResult: ...\n```\n\nThere is one namespace for all remote skills, not one tool or MCP server\nper skill. No resource ID is converted into a filesystem path.\n\n## Backend dependency\n\n`/ps/mcp` must support direct reads of child resources such as\n`skill://plugin_demo/deploy/references/deploy.md`. This PR implements\nand tests the Codex side of that contract; production child reads remain\ndependent on the corresponding plugin-service support. Search remains\nout of scope until that service exposes a bounded search/resource API.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Added an app-server integration test covering `skills.list` followed\nby `skills.read` with no executor.\n- Ran `just fmt`.\n- Ran `just bazel-lock-update` and `just bazel-lock-check`.\n- Did not run Rust tests or Clippy locally, per request; CI will run\nthem.","verified_at":"2026-06-11T10:38:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7b3eb8e4bcacc55cda6d5fb4d31a06b36351749b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7b3eb8e4bcacc55cda6d5fb4d31a06b36351749b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7b3eb8e4bcacc55cda6d5fb4d31a06b36351749b/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"273a4aa4f2474b9d27a2654f5803d51f65ce3f43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/273a4aa4f2474b9d27a2654f5803d51f65ce3f43","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/273a4aa4f2474b9d27a2654f5803d51f65ce3f43"}]},{"sha":"273a4aa4f2474b9d27a2654f5803d51f65ce3f43","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDI3M2E0YWE0ZjI0NzRiOWQyN2EyNjU0ZjU4MDNkNTFmNjVjZTNmNDM","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T10:07:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T10:07:19Z"},"message":"core: enable remote compaction v2 by default (#27573)\n\n## Why\n\nRemote compaction v2 is ready to become the default for providers that\nalready support remote compaction. Leaving it behind an\nunder-development opt-in keeps eligible sessions on the legacy\nremote-compaction path.\n\nThis does not broaden provider eligibility: OpenAI and Azure move to v2,\nwhile Bedrock and OSS providers retain their existing local-compaction\nbehavior.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Mark `remote_compaction_v2` stable and enable it by default.\n- Make tests that intentionally cover legacy remote compaction\nexplicitly disable v2.\n- Update parity coverage so v2 exercises the production default and only\nlegacy mode opts out.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\nauto_compact_runs_after_resume_when_token_usage_is_over_limit\nauto_compact_counts_encrypted_reasoning_before_last_user\nauto_compact_runs_when_reasoning_header_clears_between_turns\nresponses_lite_compact_request_uses_lite_transport_contract`","tree":{"sha":"bd934cc16f069d443dc29913c6ef082d53b2b871","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/bd934cc16f069d443dc29913c6ef082d53b2b871"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/273a4aa4f2474b9d27a2654f5803d51f65ce3f43","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKojXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIVQQAAS1vuaNgp34Mbf6bDGO4qF1\njx76HoRdVeFmlIOHxBz+MzoEW4WxjVVxzPsSJglwcgc+LbPCAswn40SQQiQ/zaEg\nvmbRLtPa8Kb+vvNXS2JBDn9JKH6vSTQo8Sjbeb7lDLCahZoCfUPRB6MwNXtMLoWa\nONuDeSmgXBkpLTLqN80z9ImESlDouv/t7dIlyebNpru9mJfrPsyfnw5bVeOBZFky\nK2uY5qgEtlFH72eHNRJTBVE9CqZG0TBUHrpAn0jG8/as8neRtD41BplP1zpIRYCb\nYRCexu7DoDqVrPkyAAvSOovweCo2O4b4dbTNBQ3Rqr40D524cs57HnLkDPIbNNYg\nDYPkNVpI8bbvHqzOs1xpT8Kjp0mrovHhGo+krGJ1iCS5XD5/PtVEEW5GT/RhSpV2\nDKkgqAIbPqVUZTCiHZBtZX+xJDkDTvwmQWcyVStwBNNpQIgWLpnInATtTQpfJ4y0\nktqyxX7BGZVZKo06xPrXeI2brfIcPR4rrA3WIjnoUWHZWycNSz4Ut6EMXRLhtWgD\ngt901y2OmaMaOwaRNbHmQQnBVCfXLecY0M8V1Sbd4MpBFh3d57lohpAIRcIo5xht\nUOQ8sy+APN2J7OlLYp2hPfs/zDA1Af6vT1eyXJ2rcjszrGTaM1iJo/vj3KGCNNH7\nrSrGBntZKXO2hSrIo04e\n=oLnC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree bd934cc16f069d443dc29913c6ef082d53b2b871\nparent 6754e77792e5cb788a8ef2b4f3c3b51d0324482a\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1781172439 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781172439 +0000\n\ncore: enable remote compaction v2 by default (#27573)\n\n## Why\n\nRemote compaction v2 is ready to become the default for providers that\nalready support remote compaction. Leaving it behind an\nunder-development opt-in keeps eligible sessions on the legacy\nremote-compaction path.\n\nThis does not broaden provider eligibility: OpenAI and Azure move to v2,\nwhile Bedrock and OSS providers retain their existing local-compaction\nbehavior.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Mark `remote_compaction_v2` stable and enable it by default.\n- Make tests that intentionally cover legacy remote compaction\nexplicitly disable v2.\n- Update parity coverage so v2 exercises the production default and only\nlegacy mode opts out.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\nauto_compact_runs_after_resume_when_token_usage_is_over_limit\nauto_compact_counts_encrypted_reasoning_before_last_user\nauto_compact_runs_when_reasoning_header_clears_between_turns\nresponses_lite_compact_request_uses_lite_transport_contract`","verified_at":"2026-06-11T10:07:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/273a4aa4f2474b9d27a2654f5803d51f65ce3f43","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/273a4aa4f2474b9d27a2654f5803d51f65ce3f43","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/273a4aa4f2474b9d27a2654f5803d51f65ce3f43/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6754e77792e5cb788a8ef2b4f3c3b51d0324482a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6754e77792e5cb788a8ef2b4f3c3b51d0324482a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6754e77792e5cb788a8ef2b4f3c3b51d0324482a"}]},{"sha":"6754e77792e5cb788a8ef2b4f3c3b51d0324482a","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDY3NTRlNzc3OTJlNWNiNzg4YThlZjJiNGYzYzNiNTFkMDMyNDQ4MmE","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T09:46:47Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T09:46:47Z"},"message":"skills: cache remote catalog failures per thread (#27403)\n\n## Summary\n\n- cache the first remote skill catalog outcome per thread, including\nfailures\n- preserve discovery errors as catalog warnings\n- update the existing cache regression test to verify failed discovery\nis attempted once\n\n## Why\n\nA failed or hanging `codex_apps` `resources/list` call could run once\nwhile building initial context and immediately again while contributing\nfirst-turn input. With the discovery timeout, an ordinary Apps turn\ncould wait up to 20 seconds before inference and retry again on later\nturns even when no remote skill was mentioned.\n\nCaching a warning-only empty catalog preserves graceful degradation\nwhile preventing repeated synchronous discovery attempts.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just fmt`\n- Tests and Clippy not run per request; CI will validate the change.","tree":{"sha":"38cf957f8158de16026da5b3d17275b77bf2a04e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/38cf957f8158de16026da5b3d17275b77bf2a04e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6754e77792e5cb788a8ef2b4f3c3b51d0324482a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKoQHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAArV4QAKkc6uYBThgUXvIG7MXWjgAu\nRzNSzOFaZVWhZi+4k6HxeiZf2ZyaC2vdiZl+89xDoHc5l3qIzZSY/pjibsx3P49v\nXKxaXWvUpPXCJOnFDYEwS3mAafqT+L8FAX/LjUEdvoUmTBv6aJfArpJhmm5JCkgw\n/041VD9d1WxHEBwjrGM7WkMH4j2cz/WdcoIJLDynrNHn0nppLn+1FHIY9jOVKIsh\nVd+DOcpeh9dF7ZiEyb91XqJVIxM6tPXWApjqEiylUNdFwYJ8uzasfmi/FJMnAEiu\niPzEOBsudajM/Jq1N70yzP5E7z87Zah8htDCaZIZ5izV89deRfNlkQ4infMa5uKv\nKaXRHtW71GQXLblUJVmZKMnfbEefxImwQ+a0CaP8tK+r3buuVAUPL2eSlDbp7mA4\nekw9t46TVbAgm8WkL+gcKa69mFtI54V8BtfwoV6zTtdTK2khe8yCJctjeTfhs8Iv\n0NJrDfXVBlqqN4wXY3XIE/xE+e7tG+jjSO3KenBfYxWOIcE6DNe6sqyTj1MrWDEu\n81FSyGQYXvC+LwGmSb0Fpc1/YuzKLIBPUssNvSMXP9hlBHmvkiKeizThoIJOr8Q6\nzBvYUHsyCSIiaIr1nr/3DIHixl/90b1Vi6wylqxr+7dXrNbMTM3nTiN9hOLIePlu\nOBPulY7cGU3zntqxC+Cr\n=FOM6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 38cf957f8158de16026da5b3d17275b77bf2a04e\nparent a287c5dffdc96855e61a75526e86428fee6663e4\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1781171207 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781171207 +0200\n\nskills: cache remote catalog failures per thread (#27403)\n\n## Summary\n\n- cache the first remote skill catalog outcome per thread, including\nfailures\n- preserve discovery errors as catalog warnings\n- update the existing cache regression test to verify failed discovery\nis attempted once\n\n## Why\n\nA failed or hanging `codex_apps` `resources/list` call could run once\nwhile building initial context and immediately again while contributing\nfirst-turn input. With the discovery timeout, an ordinary Apps turn\ncould wait up to 20 seconds before inference and retry again on later\nturns even when no remote skill was mentioned.\n\nCaching a warning-only empty catalog preserves graceful degradation\nwhile preventing repeated synchronous discovery attempts.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just fmt`\n- Tests and Clippy not run per request; CI will validate the change.","verified_at":"2026-06-11T09:46:48Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6754e77792e5cb788a8ef2b4f3c3b51d0324482a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6754e77792e5cb788a8ef2b4f3c3b51d0324482a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6754e77792e5cb788a8ef2b4f3c3b51d0324482a/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a287c5dffdc96855e61a75526e86428fee6663e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a287c5dffdc96855e61a75526e86428fee6663e4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a287c5dffdc96855e61a75526e86428fee6663e4"}]},{"sha":"a287c5dffdc96855e61a75526e86428fee6663e4","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGEyODdjNWRmZmRjOTY4NTVlNjFhNzU1MjZlODY0MjhmZWU2NjYzZTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T09:28:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T09:28:16Z"},"message":"skills: make backend plugin skills invocable without an executor (#27387)\n\n## Why\n\n#27198 made the extension-owned `codex_apps` MCP connection the hosted\nplugin runtime, but its `mcp/skill` resources still bypassed the skills\nextension. App-server could list and read those resources through\ngeneric MCP APIs, but a thread with no selected environment did not\nexpose them in the model's skills catalog or load their `SKILL.md`\nthrough `$skill`.\n\nHosted skills should stay remote while using the same typed catalog,\nsource authority, deduplication, bounded contextual catalog, and\nselected-skill prompt injection as host and executor skills. They should\nnot be downloaded or exposed as ambient filesystem paths.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add a session-scoped `McpResourceClient` over the replaceable MCP\nconnection manager so resource list/read calls follow startup and\nrefresh replacements.\n- Add a `BackendSkillProvider` that pages `codex_apps` resources,\naccepts bounded and validated `mcp/skill` entries, and reads a selected\nskill's `SKILL.md` through the same MCP connection.\n- Register the remote provider in app-server and include it in the\nskills catalog even when a thread has no selected capability roots or\nexecutor.\n- Contribute hosted skill metadata through the bounded\n`AvailableSkillsInstructions` developer-context path, exclude remote\nentries from per-turn catalog injection, and classify `<skills>`\nmessages as contextual developer content so rollback can trim and\nrebuild them correctly.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Extend the app-server MCP resource integration test with\n`environments: []` to exercise two-page discovery, filter a\nnon-`mcp/skill` resource, verify the escaped developer catalog entry and\nuser-role `<skill>` fragment containing the fetched `SKILL.md`, and\npreserve generic MCP resource reads.\n- Add core event-mapping coverage that classifies `<skills>` developer\nmessages as contextual history.","tree":{"sha":"91c8148f7880095cdc6a2e0641a229016f7000a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/91c8148f7880095cdc6a2e0641a229016f7000a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a287c5dffdc96855e61a75526e86428fee6663e4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKn+wCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtcUQAKQU+cUxS6LBOUEr4NKPIZK+\nrdU6M+FENxqv2vLRXY8athUuvAgIkxhaAbMYnzich4ydXbgIZrv7bawb314C2t1Q\nqX+jhHoEmQbfhvN+Bw0ifieWm6ixG7lbYMmEJuYPMJSTr6fEiFKNC466mMHD9OZZ\nCvNfArMz8SRfrfO4QDsxLAPo0IYJgAeZiONctmrirQNlH67utTJDaPhHuwf9u417\niKr+6lXuvzqzyR4XVWosmli/ZuTgb02RV/kbc11oyz3Vbs+gdRMiMtTjH1U10uVT\nPU2CyWGKfFTH4FzSDwb+hoqywJQgEUFl8nGsMqxoexbDVf80fM+3ikCinayRczsl\nP2ro6V64JkDuQ4yQnLGoTwbXWtQ2p79DETY7SlpyH6p5FbtTW222F3hmGk3Oul5Q\n66FkPT6N5Ew7Y008+gNjgx9SbDn3CvpHi9GzdY/0dKnsof0WtpPEn2FBW8grjGQS\n0ZBFCoAm8GH25rBVBvfZoqRQT++SKEPJxDCmwBk7JXS19/oN7wm0+uTAY/luPNGl\nM+aIxcva3ogCa5xjxi2t5k/d2k9kwX1EiAj9mt16GeLBJ0YLHCO5cJwkSUXorkxw\nRPQEPJVmvWGgFu/1dxzlM9O7BCwiiQ0oGB6KXs6a/UNc23ps1z4oeNKsjceuKCtT\n6OLfAfLVABz9+RAnUi7s\n=KQT9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 91c8148f7880095cdc6a2e0641a229016f7000a3\nparent 53b501974545547b26680b40ba2bb03903b2da44\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1781170096 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781170096 +0200\n\nskills: make backend plugin skills invocable without an executor (#27387)\n\n## Why\n\n#27198 made the extension-owned `codex_apps` MCP connection the hosted\nplugin runtime, but its `mcp/skill` resources still bypassed the skills\nextension. App-server could list and read those resources through\ngeneric MCP APIs, but a thread with no selected environment did not\nexpose them in the model's skills catalog or load their `SKILL.md`\nthrough `$skill`.\n\nHosted skills should stay remote while using the same typed catalog,\nsource authority, deduplication, bounded contextual catalog, and\nselected-skill prompt injection as host and executor skills. They should\nnot be downloaded or exposed as ambient filesystem paths.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add a session-scoped `McpResourceClient` over the replaceable MCP\nconnection manager so resource list/read calls follow startup and\nrefresh replacements.\n- Add a `BackendSkillProvider` that pages `codex_apps` resources,\naccepts bounded and validated `mcp/skill` entries, and reads a selected\nskill's `SKILL.md` through the same MCP connection.\n- Register the remote provider in app-server and include it in the\nskills catalog even when a thread has no selected capability roots or\nexecutor.\n- Contribute hosted skill metadata through the bounded\n`AvailableSkillsInstructions` developer-context path, exclude remote\nentries from per-turn catalog injection, and classify `<skills>`\nmessages as contextual developer content so rollback can trim and\nrebuild them correctly.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Extend the app-server MCP resource integration test with\n`environments: []` to exercise two-page discovery, filter a\nnon-`mcp/skill` resource, verify the escaped developer catalog entry and\nuser-role `<skill>` fragment containing the fetched `SKILL.md`, and\npreserve generic MCP resource reads.\n- Add core event-mapping coverage that classifies `<skills>` developer\nmessages as contextual history.","verified_at":"2026-06-11T09:28:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a287c5dffdc96855e61a75526e86428fee6663e4","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a287c5dffdc96855e61a75526e86428fee6663e4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a287c5dffdc96855e61a75526e86428fee6663e4/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"53b501974545547b26680b40ba2bb03903b2da44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/53b501974545547b26680b40ba2bb03903b2da44","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/53b501974545547b26680b40ba2bb03903b2da44"}]},{"sha":"53b501974545547b26680b40ba2bb03903b2da44","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDUzYjUwMTk3NDU0NTU0N2IyNjY4MGI0MGJhMmJiMDM5MDNiMmRhNDQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"alexsong-oai","email":"alexsong@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T06:42:15Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T06:42:15Z"},"message":"[codex] Tune cloud config cache intervals (#26513)\n\n## Summary\n- Increase the cloud config bundle background refresh interval from 5\nminutes to 15 minutes.\n- Increase the local cloud config bundle cache TTL from 30 minutes to 1\nhour.\n\n## Why\n- Reduce background cloud config fetch frequency while keeping cached\nworkspace-managed policies available longer between refreshes.\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `cargo test -p codex-cloud-config`","tree":{"sha":"2bb4bc374ed89d97c09604b28a61a28aa670702b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2bb4bc374ed89d97c09604b28a61a28aa670702b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/53b501974545547b26680b40ba2bb03903b2da44","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKljHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtb8QAIF9nYIdeJYWTYlhhCgEKLLl\nT/9KhiMCE9RDtNA2lumXgTokzuWJAOMT2w9Bj+0a9h9L5io3ykJkTfAQUHB/THgp\nBaQmcE3ogPakLz16WLEKMp5IUIbJQVOcFj+qTrHCEtqEexM+jGtUiLS77iN/puZO\nBVnNO9OvDqc8a3UHYTkO3Srbv/p0+9auStzJsHmHWVjhg1h0LesPhW2ykSjzR8J3\nnHFsGiRoC3tOMsnTrsfsFmxPioU6rgCUeo0uZDPyVLj0rQWTdq3OuWbYUUwwZUNA\nShW5xNvpMP0yp67k2U2OzKdAMLHyoS1LtKIKSkZSbZk8dvzrEJkYwzQfnM2j7Sdq\n+A715ee7L7c4lkqC0oFEx9tgyaJPGKB04ywNu5l6ENrNvtaGDdkLCV6gypmRuBKA\nE7FerLibAyt6EVyUglQ/pAWEStseEgbVbgzd3xD4CtVPaLyGziow43tNoA/jHGAA\nUpLbLjgiufXM8FUywfEs5zA+ZlmeArbOrWPgNTD8dVkclzzbUejcOvKI8d2o7FNz\nJg/UAflIlWa5QRgv7oKhaCnovMdWoY2noFOTtRsamgD4Y1tznhW9fVD0pcqVpMUC\nFtf9vpSao14tEo+MTpH9Hix3Zs6WvTu2jmrsJwiNIPcd7Z4eQN7Y69Wsyv3NFzUG\nhKVSt8R8QO2wND4ZedI0\n=gScV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2bb4bc374ed89d97c09604b28a61a28aa670702b\nparent 8d9f33c87ca2e7cb89490703fb03f74c9a26578b\nauthor alexsong-oai <alexsong@openai.com> 1781160135 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781160135 -0700\n\n[codex] Tune cloud config cache intervals (#26513)\n\n## Summary\n- Increase the cloud config bundle background refresh interval from 5\nminutes to 15 minutes.\n- Increase the local cloud config bundle cache TTL from 30 minutes to 1\nhour.\n\n## Why\n- Reduce background cloud config fetch frequency while keeping cached\nworkspace-managed policies available longer between refreshes.\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `cargo test -p codex-cloud-config`","verified_at":"2026-06-11T06:42:16Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/53b501974545547b26680b40ba2bb03903b2da44","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/53b501974545547b26680b40ba2bb03903b2da44","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/53b501974545547b26680b40ba2bb03903b2da44/comments","author":{"login":"alexsong-oai","id":256201575,"node_id":"U_kgDOD0VTZw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256201575?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/alexsong-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8d9f33c87ca2e7cb89490703fb03f74c9a26578b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8d9f33c87ca2e7cb89490703fb03f74c9a26578b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8d9f33c87ca2e7cb89490703fb03f74c9a26578b"}]},{"sha":"8d9f33c87ca2e7cb89490703fb03f74c9a26578b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhkOWYzM2M4N2NhMmU3Y2I4OTQ5MDcwM2ZiMDNmNzRjOWEyNjU3OGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"rhan-oai","email":"rhan@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T06:07:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T06:07:06Z"},"message":"[codex-analytics] Emit structured compaction codex errors (#27082)\n\n## Summary\n- replace raw compaction `error` analytics with `codex_error_kind` and\n`codex_error_http_status_code`\n- derive compaction error telemetry from `CodexErr` using the same\n`CodexErrKind` mapping and HTTP status helper used by turn events\n- remove the pre-compact hook stop reason from the internal compaction\noutcome now that it is no longer emitted as raw analytics text\n\n## Why\nCompaction `error` was a raw `CodexErr::to_string()` value, which can\ncarry free-form provider or user-derived text. Structured Codex error\nfields preserve useful low-cardinality telemetry without sending the raw\nstring.\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-analytics`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ncompact::tests::build_token_limited_compacted_history_appends_summary_message`\n\nAttempted `just test -p codex-core`; the changed crate compiled, but the\nfull target failed in unrelated environment-dependent tests such as\nmissing helper binaries and shell snapshot timeouts.","tree":{"sha":"3371df81ae904f395d05495b6446674aafbae037","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/3371df81ae904f395d05495b6446674aafbae037"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8d9f33c87ca2e7cb89490703fb03f74c9a26578b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKlCKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqgcQADiOJ8bE7ScV594zfBCluFL2\np85hdrEvUmX58isTC3oE9a1KSA9XsVmXuMK/pcfjopmRFlOsvXQFzXwWaBg2e7E0\nAR1jq9WaXF75RCS0ClC9a9A94jFLhOetPrsl9qeAwhzJm5kr3BVx4vwxpq4ZTo9a\njwssvvzJepkqQoDxtJ8I2Kvxgpm2L85Q3y+gyolo1C267kb/Bnk8GYLxPivEsIUO\nCp/Ph+U9cEkd6m80bf6Ztp8kli0xOQDVK/Ex5UcDqpqeIjQH3QVxKqYEBOD96YzU\ncXTwF7cnwCNZyAL4bBLRscQ91nzxTiBZgY7+FRm4oaqvrcUBcf0ZBwpAIfnE/4Lf\nq0u6kj2tRxN6tQl1kqotgcQ9JKwTvFIX8Lu/7MQ4Y2Yp3pyvU3ERPxjfSetpOP/k\n92vgNKtjbtMxGi7IdcHF0TGD0qEl0bFHHwiMzOZC3KqJu19dzXgNP0boz/SBR+nS\nMMOyIbPEPNH+eiBiBkMdNs5L3ErKWTgcPKuAxeaRjSGO/1ZbMlmdXBeRFI6pfFgN\nQDfyJBoXg64TEbj+Got0PeyH2WAk3gFgcNxCBPyZoyWIe1l2cwq09ZPSrMfPDdwf\nH37IrirNmEOKFYmk2gYhYCVKs28gai8scw/ZcPwdlMO8oa3wdcD9XNQ5KOAociWJ\nEHUn5brPhpbG3Xepbcp8\n=Jr5m\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3371df81ae904f395d05495b6446674aafbae037\nparent b5a718ef6742af051857ab5d3e20920dfbe66af3\nauthor rhan-oai <rhan@openai.com> 1781158026 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781158026 +0000\n\n[codex-analytics] Emit structured compaction codex errors (#27082)\n\n## Summary\n- replace raw compaction `error` analytics with `codex_error_kind` and\n`codex_error_http_status_code`\n- derive compaction error telemetry from `CodexErr` using the same\n`CodexErrKind` mapping and HTTP status helper used by turn events\n- remove the pre-compact hook stop reason from the internal compaction\noutcome now that it is no longer emitted as raw analytics text\n\n## Why\nCompaction `error` was a raw `CodexErr::to_string()` value, which can\ncarry free-form provider or user-derived text. Structured Codex error\nfields preserve useful low-cardinality telemetry without sending the raw\nstring.\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-analytics`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ncompact::tests::build_token_limited_compacted_history_appends_summary_message`\n\nAttempted `just test -p codex-core`; the changed crate compiled, but the\nfull target failed in unrelated environment-dependent tests such as\nmissing helper binaries and shell snapshot timeouts.","verified_at":"2026-06-11T06:07:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8d9f33c87ca2e7cb89490703fb03f74c9a26578b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8d9f33c87ca2e7cb89490703fb03f74c9a26578b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8d9f33c87ca2e7cb89490703fb03f74c9a26578b/comments","author":{"login":"rhan-oai","id":214716640,"node_id":"U_kgDODMxQ4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214716640?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rhan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b5a718ef6742af051857ab5d3e20920dfbe66af3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b5a718ef6742af051857ab5d3e20920dfbe66af3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b5a718ef6742af051857ab5d3e20920dfbe66af3"}]},{"sha":"b5a718ef6742af051857ab5d3e20920dfbe66af3","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGI1YTcxOGVmNjc0MmFmMDUxODU3YWI1ZDNlMjA5MjBkZmJlNjZhZjM","commit":{"author":{"name":"sayan-oai","email":"sayan@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T06:06:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T06:06:34Z"},"message":"Use generic search metadata for dynamic tools (#27356)\n\n## Why\n\nDynamic tools maintained a separate search-text builder even though the\nshared tool search path already derives the same metadata from\n`ToolSpec`. Using the shared path removes duplicate behavior before\nadding explicit namespaces.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Build dynamic-tool search entries with\n`ToolSearchInfo::from_tool_spec`.\n- Remove the custom search-text state and its implementation-only unit\ntest.\n\nThe old search text included the tool name, its space-separated form,\ndescription, namespace, and top-level parameter names. The shared\nbuilder preserves all of those terms and also indexes namespace\ndescriptions and nested schema metadata.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\ntool_search_returns_deferred_dynamic_tool_and_routes_follow_up_call`","tree":{"sha":"6d084eb0898d417da5aec91e46870ca4679f3fc7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6d084eb0898d417da5aec91e46870ca4679f3fc7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/b5a718ef6742af051857ab5d3e20920dfbe66af3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKlBqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3hEQADK4ex2Vh27g1wqmDoI/d2H2\nPzdJVNJEdFRMxJ9JSHS1zdwLLHm5HAtYWENhiz5ZtZ7PjUT9sniFKJucI6Bh6Gf9\nxLzrSVxwJEqGjdAJ/mucFZfALVkEiNOVtelVi0VAbPDuoyYU7kXQB5vRk3/GjAdm\nNSPxjZ75ij2u+60ChVdKuiYRLOstaCxrAkOR9CWr+Lm2adDC0WY9a6AGFipUrvKW\nOJ2gQlgMqk3J+5aewW2psj/n2N2rTvUp20cncuPAcN6MXkZQsTArb/Mgah/Gxj3L\nA0Xbjxc6dfdWyLocokGy0hXEqJI2K0LkD7TsCHPd2FociYJx2jJUSNmQsdeQKGIH\nw2MrxX7ts0OkeqNBPiz6D219f8TXFM2SfORR679fCzv672VStVcR1ScSDLpIorcI\nXphr09gfT380MDW6cLEwHbU8cI0Ifjj3TJxgg5rPcpKoEHtw0GmSLWdziRBMsxu7\nnQbeSWQs4x9dwksGx2Sl79LgeYl3K9nBSTl6LgoY4OAuSY0EMKs6Gp8Rd2JmYrE1\nqYpvkrcAlKBMzU+2cBkh5nremLSWFhLOdhQVKlVW2cxJhOu19Pky5LdxasiD5IsG\nfPNVq/tirsxCOsrW2DZEC1hhzrFhjyF6IjfOFFpLrUpfBI6v/x9dMp3EaoCRxAHi\nzQx+pADafhLEi13bM4vD\n=kiIt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6d084eb0898d417da5aec91e46870ca4679f3fc7\nparent 383708e74e42ac09b473633019d5f1498c18fbea\nauthor sayan-oai <sayan@openai.com> 1781157994 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781157994 -0700\n\nUse generic search metadata for dynamic tools (#27356)\n\n## Why\n\nDynamic tools maintained a separate search-text builder even though the\nshared tool search path already derives the same metadata from\n`ToolSpec`. Using the shared path removes duplicate behavior before\nadding explicit namespaces.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Build dynamic-tool search entries with\n`ToolSearchInfo::from_tool_spec`.\n- Remove the custom search-text state and its implementation-only unit\ntest.\n\nThe old search text included the tool name, its space-separated form,\ndescription, namespace, and top-level parameter names. The shared\nbuilder preserves all of those terms and also indexes namespace\ndescriptions and nested schema metadata.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\ntool_search_returns_deferred_dynamic_tool_and_routes_follow_up_call`","verified_at":"2026-06-11T06:06:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b5a718ef6742af051857ab5d3e20920dfbe66af3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b5a718ef6742af051857ab5d3e20920dfbe66af3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b5a718ef6742af051857ab5d3e20920dfbe66af3/comments","author":{"login":"sayan-oai","id":244841968,"node_id":"U_kgDODpf98A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244841968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/sayan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"383708e74e42ac09b473633019d5f1498c18fbea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/383708e74e42ac09b473633019d5f1498c18fbea","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/383708e74e42ac09b473633019d5f1498c18fbea"}]},{"sha":"383708e74e42ac09b473633019d5f1498c18fbea","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDM4MzcwOGU3NGU0MmFjMDliNDczNjMzMDE5ZDVmMTQ5OGMxOGZiZWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"rhan-oai","email":"rhan@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T05:47:22Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T05:47:22Z"},"message":"[codex-analytics] report cached input tokens for v2 compaction (#27103)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add nullable `cached_input_tokens` to the compaction analytics event\n- populate it from response usage for compaction v2\n- leave it `null` for other compaction implementations\n\nThis adds visibility into prompt-cache usage for v2 compaction without\nchanging compaction behavior.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-analytics`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ncollect_compaction_output_accepts_additional_output_items`","tree":{"sha":"6468fcc7273b9ae0a0a0565e74ff92a400b48d4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6468fcc7273b9ae0a0a0565e74ff92a400b48d4d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/383708e74e42ac09b473633019d5f1498c18fbea","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKkvqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATzkQABfid6CpuoEoGW6goeDc7dVB\n/ZjorJifA1e+KxqHQhlJSogpNwCnqI6MYOs6vk6cqgFA3TTXjoVtfvdnZh2x+Ssp\nq1n+0B2TWb7yIO/CrxYpku1xAiggJuh/jhyqYRk4XN8cZLUAGOWZHtDRPE3txvHq\nEJt1ene1o03dUv0oZGsuBszaak+XLex8LYTXOqaJwWdujbu8wey827Jt0nMnA4c6\nu0P2lK4KLRLT7rTewDlo7GK5ENzBjvZqaq+HNh9vdi/IiDaYTAWYEoSO8QEkaA53\nwXEIPleFx9MmlNu5MTkulAtrQRD/TZDQgioX91B6HSbk9TDFXVGxkxkkKwxABeSF\nXi+zFaw9V/V5DsQClkdsrrgfd6/RvUuV36ZmGTFfLlj3DT66LgrF9PJpDfvR3C9w\nmyypogeFdWufx6aGG0yVdLbaX+XqAYjM2STi8VZt+BcAXgxm7coXF/VE90bpHV5a\nYZL66dKZrCy3O8y04oB8Si0scWNwy0LoQLf3y2DRDSA4Ij46c4KrOD4ZG0AjAfZe\nd28DQUP52GGLgxHWgxkzGnxbYdxfW1LV4KeVVBgjUFY+1GqWxlCQqBeh/qnrLtE4\np1JKwExpsC2+3PaUaLg3EifFZDLSdyVpmjPik4IklGDFHa1kUGhvEqYz69YS2DOI\nI7lioyWlyE11q/0IehD/\n=zt/I\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6468fcc7273b9ae0a0a0565e74ff92a400b48d4d\nparent 598125109dd2e098486884d8fb563ebe90bc24da\nauthor rhan-oai <rhan@openai.com> 1781156842 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781156842 -0700\n\n[codex-analytics] report cached input tokens for v2 compaction (#27103)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add nullable `cached_input_tokens` to the compaction analytics event\n- populate it from response usage for compaction v2\n- leave it `null` for other compaction implementations\n\nThis adds visibility into prompt-cache usage for v2 compaction without\nchanging compaction behavior.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-analytics`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ncollect_compaction_output_accepts_additional_output_items`","verified_at":"2026-06-11T05:47:23Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/383708e74e42ac09b473633019d5f1498c18fbea","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/383708e74e42ac09b473633019d5f1498c18fbea","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/383708e74e42ac09b473633019d5f1498c18fbea/comments","author":{"login":"rhan-oai","id":214716640,"node_id":"U_kgDODMxQ4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214716640?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rhan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"598125109dd2e098486884d8fb563ebe90bc24da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/598125109dd2e098486884d8fb563ebe90bc24da","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/598125109dd2e098486884d8fb563ebe90bc24da"}]},{"sha":"598125109dd2e098486884d8fb563ebe90bc24da","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDU5ODEyNTEwOWRkMmUwOTg0ODY4ODRkOGZiNTYzZWJlOTBiYzI0ZGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Curtis 'Fjord' Hawthorne","email":"fjord@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T04:17:32Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T04:17:32Z"},"message":"image: preserve metadata when resizing prompt images (#27266)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Preserve ICC profiles and EXIF metadata when resizing and re-encoding\nprompt images.\n- Retain EXIF orientation metadata without rotating or otherwise\nmodifying the pixel data locally.\n- Support metadata preservation for PNG, JPEG, and WebP outputs.\n- Continue returning the original bytes when an image does not require\nre-encoding.\n\nThis intentionally preserves the metadata most important for rendering\nprompt images faithfully. Other format-specific metadata is not copied.\n\n## Motivation\n\nClient-side resizing previously discarded image metadata during\nre-encoding. This could lose color-profile information and EXIF\norientation needed by downstream image consumers.\n\n\n#### [git stack](https://github.com/magus/git-stack-cli)\n- ✅ `1` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27245\n- ✅ `2` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27247\n- ✅ `3` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27246\n- 👉 `4` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27266","tree":{"sha":"ad4526d576092805b36001bdeba429f768907229","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/ad4526d576092805b36001bdeba429f768907229"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/598125109dd2e098486884d8fb563ebe90bc24da","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKjbcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPVsQAI1mRymwghOOROyxeK9qFO+D\nmDjG76aJ/rU4T+b3aDWwzQrehvOqHmwvbmct/5VdiuNG81SZ/4c85BLnGr1F/Haz\nrOhPhmhf61PIa6XdWM0KHRvdd19H+s8OY4awOPek4nPucAU7zS3H4EwWTn6C6Sji\nU6CqKqlv8Nf8WsDYhtEIe46Db+46Ssgl9cgt699b0xmC5nO7ZEms/A91QWd0dYM7\n79/EUF2PY3BKjtIQGz85NlvAn3TnrEhqOAeMe9RgS3npgRzr5Cwhl6Fgre1NfhnW\nj2K+gWoeRTFgtxbs/oajReRTlgII0SiZYS3hWUf8SVsheDONvXEVV86A45vlTzXm\nxLPUN5KeEvAvfk0LuO+n+hs0WatOAvqeWzFuHlIZLmPT7dyhftO8C0yrRQnTuy7I\nPb4cz91fEVvuXUtXA/F83Et4sunFQdm8hSzxaA0dTzON2o2/y5jUTJfTlLYlyjP9\nKA3fcOH0hAWc5wDppT+GQb3x+pRDHxHVkUM/dXjEExnUPUH/NasfjI8GSC2E/2KR\nDXo5zC6aHuggVTgYd0KQcim54udpN/RawscElfGxC23xqbmyJB0JEv3UZ0dNwm3w\nTtD9/H8mSPPw7v1lbwbq+kp+mdqTv85L0aY4dJAGJ3hSgGV5g9YsxT8HCJxyeH2W\nsVekFj9b0NIOtHblRisb\n=IZ7E\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ad4526d576092805b36001bdeba429f768907229\nparent dac5f07403e048544cad6e9f9fbd52b91cb47a15\nauthor Curtis 'Fjord' Hawthorne <fjord@openai.com> 1781151452 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781151452 -0700\n\nimage: preserve metadata when resizing prompt images (#27266)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Preserve ICC profiles and EXIF metadata when resizing and re-encoding\nprompt images.\n- Retain EXIF orientation metadata without rotating or otherwise\nmodifying the pixel data locally.\n- Support metadata preservation for PNG, JPEG, and WebP outputs.\n- Continue returning the original bytes when an image does not require\nre-encoding.\n\nThis intentionally preserves the metadata most important for rendering\nprompt images faithfully. Other format-specific metadata is not copied.\n\n## Motivation\n\nClient-side resizing previously discarded image metadata during\nre-encoding. This could lose color-profile information and EXIF\norientation needed by downstream image consumers.\n\n\n#### [git stack](https://github.com/magus/git-stack-cli)\n- ✅ `1` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27245\n- ✅ `2` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27247\n- ✅ `3` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27246\n- 👉 `4` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27266","verified_at":"2026-06-11T04:17:32Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/598125109dd2e098486884d8fb563ebe90bc24da","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/598125109dd2e098486884d8fb563ebe90bc24da","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/598125109dd2e098486884d8fb563ebe90bc24da/comments","author":{"login":"fjord-oai","id":240979671,"node_id":"U_kgDODl0O1w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240979671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/fjord-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"dac5f07403e048544cad6e9f9fbd52b91cb47a15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/dac5f07403e048544cad6e9f9fbd52b91cb47a15","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/dac5f07403e048544cad6e9f9fbd52b91cb47a15"}]},{"sha":"dac5f07403e048544cad6e9f9fbd52b91cb47a15","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGRhYzVmMDc0MDNlMDQ4NTQ0Y2FkNmU5ZjlmYmQ1MmI5MWNiNDdhMTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T04:17:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T04:17:10Z"},"message":"[codex] Add context remaining tool (#27518)\n\n## Why\n\nThe token budget feature can inject remaining-context notices into\nmodel-visible context, but the model does not have a direct way to ask\nfor that same remaining-token fragment on demand.\n\nThis PR adds a small model tool for the token budget feature so the\nmodel can request the current remaining context window message without\nduplicating the fragment format.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Adds a `get_context_remaining` direct-model tool behind\n`Feature::TokenBudget`.\n- Renders the tool output through `TokenBudgetRemainingContext`,\nmatching the existing budget message shape.\n- Registers the tool alongside `new_context` in the token budget tool\nset.\n- Adds integration coverage that verifies the tool is exposed and\nreturns the same `<token_budget>` remaining fragment already present in\ncontext.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core token_budget`","tree":{"sha":"6112690fbc1adad9889fc7871e81cb914d3ea4fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6112690fbc1adad9889fc7871e81cb914d3ea4fb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/dac5f07403e048544cad6e9f9fbd52b91cb47a15","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKjbGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAh7YQAHVpJWtMk6GsO1wkHgZYk10Q\nUeSYn2nfv5s6L763HUkpiUtrilUmAh6p+q5BYCzEvwU1lDQbqhFwnsI0OXpmgFud\nSgef5G5s/z75pi6MOJ0kd2zEdZIe7mngOvRLNRRGn/GxDJ+B6re9aQMLamm50sik\nm5TeOqw7+QFw5xWiXP52H0Y1Jo9aQ02NkI0z2k2K2YWFvL7f29RO464MP6T0936E\n0wHkEJMGnsWWPrmatN8/9O2aR1Hu389FoLf9wVEAeNPiT/nvSQ4Op9uR18Md3BIX\nkq8Cx/HR1gJZ2rvl8jEL5Uc+2UWXVKzLqiBvELf2HLs8CFwKe9efQEBWIxAj/zv+\ny54iV+5O5JDatlww8gLPuebIr8VTws/T2yQazzA6akvLxY48Mp73ESdnoKvfn0fm\nPOrUogHUX7qPAs+f+5Gg/yFylwtVdI5I6gL32CezJG5f7kQVc0Gowy13K/7Qo1BO\n/hWrfCTp9AG7t+9k6SOEmxBxCdFczub2ns0RM2Nz7USlOhjbDyWNG69hcJUVXfJv\n2vNP1Lv7bid7hLsod0kumh2Z9o8eoJyX2VdgqBEK4QPtuQ0Uy9Ghqa4aIit0H/rN\nH9jcnSQCH0WrRHyOG0ycn7a1u8EBtReSai3dF08mmr1fHOebauqxRJPfI2odaWMs\nHTGrcGUNqONUgcjYz2VL\n=6WHx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6112690fbc1adad9889fc7871e81cb914d3ea4fb\nparent ba4925b3c2240718888989664097f503ed062f80\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1781151430 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781151430 +0000\n\n[codex] Add context remaining tool (#27518)\n\n## Why\n\nThe token budget feature can inject remaining-context notices into\nmodel-visible context, but the model does not have a direct way to ask\nfor that same remaining-token fragment on demand.\n\nThis PR adds a small model tool for the token budget feature so the\nmodel can request the current remaining context window message without\nduplicating the fragment format.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Adds a `get_context_remaining` direct-model tool behind\n`Feature::TokenBudget`.\n- Renders the tool output through `TokenBudgetRemainingContext`,\nmatching the existing budget message shape.\n- Registers the tool alongside `new_context` in the token budget tool\nset.\n- Adds integration coverage that verifies the tool is exposed and\nreturns the same `<token_budget>` remaining fragment already present in\ncontext.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core token_budget`","verified_at":"2026-06-11T04:17:11Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/dac5f07403e048544cad6e9f9fbd52b91cb47a15","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/dac5f07403e048544cad6e9f9fbd52b91cb47a15","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/dac5f07403e048544cad6e9f9fbd52b91cb47a15/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ba4925b3c2240718888989664097f503ed062f80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ba4925b3c2240718888989664097f503ed062f80","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ba4925b3c2240718888989664097f503ed062f80"}]},{"sha":"ba4925b3c2240718888989664097f503ed062f80","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGJhNDkyNWIzYzIyNDA3MTg4ODg5ODk2NjQwOTdmNTAzZWQwNjJmODA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ahmed Ibrahim","email":"aibrahim@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T04:11:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T04:11:26Z"},"message":"[codex] Compact when comp_hash changes (#27520)\n\n## Summary\n- snapshot `comp_hash` into `TurnContext` when the turn is created and\nuse that snapshot as the downstream source of truth\n- persist the turn hash in rollout context and recover it into\nprevious-turn settings during resume and fork replay\n- compact existing history with the previous model only when both\nadjacent turns provide hashes and the values differ\n- record `comp_hash_changed` as the compaction reason\n- cover ordinary transitions, resume, and missing-hash compatibility\nwith end-to-end tests\n\n## Why\nHistory produced under one compaction-compatible model configuration may\nnot be safe to carry directly into another. Compacting at the turn\nboundary converts that history before context updates and the new user\nmessage are added. Persisting the turn snapshot in `TurnContextItem`\nmakes the same protection work after resuming a rollout.\n\nA missing hash is not treated as evidence of incompatibility. `None →\nSome`, `Some → None`, and `None → None` do not trigger compaction; only\n`Some(previous) → Some(current)` with unequal values does.\n\n## Stack\n- depends on #27532\n- #27532 is based directly on `main`\n\n## Testing\n- `just test -p codex-core pre_sampling_compact_` — 6 passed\n- `just test -p codex-core\nturn_context_item_uses_turn_context_comp_hash_snapshot` — passed\n- `just fix -p codex-core -p codex-protocol -p codex-analytics -p\ncodex-models-manager`","tree":{"sha":"0a25e258bdd2de44a4b406dc5f41f12e46eccb07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/0a25e258bdd2de44a4b406dc5f41f12e46eccb07"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/ba4925b3c2240718888989664097f503ed062f80","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKjVuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAb74QAFTcdsx1cnmPAxubeYVPcsnn\nXee8HHPLcH7UpPPT3a85VE4VLLH6+kKtxHr6vRfJoApaWWJzLrnCydHVagQVcMuU\nmOjvMXNlYMuJ0XcHVyRpfB4eNJ1Bp0tsqQyRGMz4tX+GjXBnaXgnFoIY9pQp2RQ3\njJ5PELVnmkEajwLQ80OFIOpHPRIi5XAvO1Kwg8zCJ50mUZAMYH8cG5JqzQL2ue8n\nrxXkiaMnY/eXlxiBQvhIE1n2L+uT5d9B2PwaXAdwclCQLqD2it/BSRpC2VNGHtu4\nKVQh2r1vZjASBy74mjO4X/BR0FvHWna6HstYCtQX1mr873w65umQL8fsKA9biaHC\nlq4Yffx59C0DGIZQXhCmS5S7ia5t8j/W/Y7gXZoZ9KWryZCO4QUxvLt042kEld8R\nbJvajcHv3pnFbkWud/r3YV4K5t2UCAWrlZFz707XQ7s95X7jwU4L9O3bB5QmrmrM\nHrbdgjpWK/I2Ell0K6ePm2WKVOrM7k7TZXIc2Fw9mhFMtBkozYNo3S8CxHiXrG3w\nP2rLQ2Qg3d34xDOWybrxPyJ0BTgW/M+qt0dQ8rb/6H6NiuvnD1I22Xq7f/DpWqVD\nQo4BlR48Bs0HruBZgHreDIJFIQFkCFfz+91uwsrCYUbMS/AX/8M7My2ZXqw/FVRb\nUxQgCxsNTqbsmZOhHXVp\n=uF5F\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0a25e258bdd2de44a4b406dc5f41f12e46eccb07\nparent 856855914f516b4fed91bb7eec032925ef6e7ba3\nauthor Ahmed Ibrahim <aibrahim@openai.com> 1781151086 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781151086 +0000\n\n[codex] Compact when comp_hash changes (#27520)\n\n## Summary\n- snapshot `comp_hash` into `TurnContext` when the turn is created and\nuse that snapshot as the downstream source of truth\n- persist the turn hash in rollout context and recover it into\nprevious-turn settings during resume and fork replay\n- compact existing history with the previous model only when both\nadjacent turns provide hashes and the values differ\n- record `comp_hash_changed` as the compaction reason\n- cover ordinary transitions, resume, and missing-hash compatibility\nwith end-to-end tests\n\n## Why\nHistory produced under one compaction-compatible model configuration may\nnot be safe to carry directly into another. Compacting at the turn\nboundary converts that history before context updates and the new user\nmessage are added. Persisting the turn snapshot in `TurnContextItem`\nmakes the same protection work after resuming a rollout.\n\nA missing hash is not treated as evidence of incompatibility. `None →\nSome`, `Some → None`, and `None → None` do not trigger compaction; only\n`Some(previous) → Some(current)` with unequal values does.\n\n## Stack\n- depends on #27532\n- #27532 is based directly on `main`\n\n## Testing\n- `just test -p codex-core pre_sampling_compact_` — 6 passed\n- `just test -p codex-core\nturn_context_item_uses_turn_context_comp_hash_snapshot` — passed\n- `just fix -p codex-core -p codex-protocol -p codex-analytics -p\ncodex-models-manager`","verified_at":"2026-06-11T04:11:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ba4925b3c2240718888989664097f503ed062f80","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ba4925b3c2240718888989664097f503ed062f80","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ba4925b3c2240718888989664097f503ed062f80/comments","author":{"login":"aibrahim-oai","id":219906144,"node_id":"U_kgDODRuAYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219906144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/aibrahim-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"856855914f516b4fed91bb7eec032925ef6e7ba3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/856855914f516b4fed91bb7eec032925ef6e7ba3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/856855914f516b4fed91bb7eec032925ef6e7ba3"}]},{"sha":"856855914f516b4fed91bb7eec032925ef6e7ba3","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDg1Njg1NTkxNGY1MTZiNGZlZDkxYmI3ZWVjMDMyOTI1ZWY2ZTdiYTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"xl-openai","email":"xl@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T03:57:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T03:57:35Z"},"message":"[codex] Pass auth mode to plugin manager (#27517)\n\n## Summary\n- Add auth mode state to `PluginsManager`.\n- Sync the plugin manager auth mode when `ThreadManager` is created and\nwhen account auth changes.\n- Route plugin load outcomes through an auth-aware projection hook so\nfollow-up plugin filtering can stay inside `core-plugins`.\n\n## Motivation\nThis prepares plugin capability loading to be configured by auth mode,\nsuch as hiding or exposing app/MCP-backed plugin surfaces based on\nwhether the user is using ChatGPT auth or API-key auth, without leaking\nthose details outside the plugin manager.\n\n## Tests\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins`\n- `env -u CODEX_SANDBOX_NETWORK_DISABLED -u CODEX_SANDBOX just test -p\ncodex-core thread_manager::tests`\n- `env -u CODEX_SANDBOX_NETWORK_DISABLED -u CODEX_SANDBOX just test -p\ncodex-app-server`","tree":{"sha":"13dd19a3e4c8409636363a82cc217849f2aa7a19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/13dd19a3e4c8409636363a82cc217849f2aa7a19"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/856855914f516b4fed91bb7eec032925ef6e7ba3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKjIvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJzsQAG+Oo2dV/hJVkboUBtMEig5Y\n3Qu7V1cjw3ScK60GhTq2E9/gcIt/xALL2TjO141DrJuJyt8JN9edkUZstix2eAp5\nXRs9jjiaZuIwT98HpfpaHr4vHVqp2yuKT/OR9L+N8F+BfHw6FzbDS7VYG9LXNKmr\nRexZ61vthcPuO08WULhnxEST4z54yPS2zPwdCbRHUMoOAAc1pMG1Z2NmPaJQgsOX\nuyksFyAf8gtZX+shP61ZadC+dM+TIAM2wCxEJ2TDWp/ImTs3rt+gHn1uVdywA7Pc\nBvOaKqDYauoEjgRIZXuxUwJFtcS4cU5vY61sTg3aruX+4ZczYhYuMk2i+zm5x59J\nXxsUhitWON1velonKPieDRwiBL7OzVvPLD26vxZABOUdBmfzPG5NC8ADmhm9YPct\n1tRasI9QqTNuHw81XgDsJN7dj81nzZ9pfJaDPQANopbT7Q/LeBrZPk68pEz7yQYU\n0nmuGYpMQiiauCHhDGjv5SFRL2wIrF64lGhNsyvlQZnIon9DrGa9gJuwN8oehurd\nLlEAu1cG7+8kQbap7blg/L997xX/ftmIW4H2V1ziRbjF981H0ojPTxe3TI/aZnNT\ndDiKQ65NIHq+g3026bFCe3KSZ6SIsUjqGytfzxeZk4/87r3EU3xdMhTQKkYdEipo\nAwXBUAwo3ISyfpFew3hu\n=lGg2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 13dd19a3e4c8409636363a82cc217849f2aa7a19\nparent 4435ff28109bcef17b66c76a80c8478fddc2d541\nauthor xl-openai <xl@openai.com> 1781150255 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781150255 -0700\n\n[codex] Pass auth mode to plugin manager (#27517)\n\n## Summary\n- Add auth mode state to `PluginsManager`.\n- Sync the plugin manager auth mode when `ThreadManager` is created and\nwhen account auth changes.\n- Route plugin load outcomes through an auth-aware projection hook so\nfollow-up plugin filtering can stay inside `core-plugins`.\n\n## Motivation\nThis prepares plugin capability loading to be configured by auth mode,\nsuch as hiding or exposing app/MCP-backed plugin surfaces based on\nwhether the user is using ChatGPT auth or API-key auth, without leaking\nthose details outside the plugin manager.\n\n## Tests\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins`\n- `env -u CODEX_SANDBOX_NETWORK_DISABLED -u CODEX_SANDBOX just test -p\ncodex-core thread_manager::tests`\n- `env -u CODEX_SANDBOX_NETWORK_DISABLED -u CODEX_SANDBOX just test -p\ncodex-app-server`","verified_at":"2026-06-11T03:57:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/856855914f516b4fed91bb7eec032925ef6e7ba3","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/856855914f516b4fed91bb7eec032925ef6e7ba3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/856855914f516b4fed91bb7eec032925ef6e7ba3/comments","author":{"login":"xl-openai","id":184293535,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvwYnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184293535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/xl-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4435ff28109bcef17b66c76a80c8478fddc2d541","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4435ff28109bcef17b66c76a80c8478fddc2d541","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4435ff28109bcef17b66c76a80c8478fddc2d541"}]},{"sha":"4435ff28109bcef17b66c76a80c8478fddc2d541","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDQ0MzVmZjI4MTA5YmNlZjE3YjY2Yzc2YTgwYzg0NzhmZGRjMmQ1NDE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Curtis 'Fjord' Hawthorne","email":"fjord@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T03:43:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T03:43:03Z"},"message":"core: strip image detail from Responses Lite requests (#27246)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Strip image `detail` fields from every Responses Lite request.\n- Apply stripping to message images and function/custom tool-output\nimages.\n- Transform only the formatted request copy without mutating stored\nhistory.\n- Preserve image URLs byte-for-byte, including HTTP(S) URLs, without\ndownloading, validating, or resizing them.\n- Preserve all image `detail` fields for non-Responses-Lite models.\n\n## Motivation\n\nResponses Lite does not support image `detail` tags, so Codex must omit\nthem whenever `model_info.use_responses_lite` is enabled. This transport\nrequirement is independent of the `resize_all_images` feature.\n\nStored history retains the original detail values. This keeps\nrequest-specific formatting isolated from conversation state and\npreserves the information for local image preparation and\nnon-Responses-Lite requests.\n\n\n#### [git stack](https://github.com/magus/git-stack-cli)\n- ✅ `1` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27245\n- ✅ `2` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27247\n- 👉 `3` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27246\n- ⏳ `4` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27266","tree":{"sha":"0376604b0039d8bfc8f94400b489b16dda26f639","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/0376604b0039d8bfc8f94400b489b16dda26f639"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4435ff28109bcef17b66c76a80c8478fddc2d541","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKi7HCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADF8QAIkHnddYuvfWovQfn3ZSEZO1\n93HztrJPSNRHV8jU0JNO21VCXJQE5Jzt5rXgrQVowX2L7LyaDdS9qzEBb8WJyyw1\nsveG29aanNjjt74RMEymprVi7um5aZxIXF3HSmEJIAZozvm4d9ahxxFVxP7zkzP8\nX8k6ATPUTYVGgmot2UCHyleE5xaFVhK4RFZnJ3F+uQNTiq5sHKV4Vgc+7hyAT8zA\n+wowd4c3nPNVKYtMY1maU6oAgFDZ5qoQ7gxn5K0+b8Vy9Ty/vDGIXsOer8aOeA9l\nwHy6tYeT8g/EUpKOKwOlqRFcjOu1UdMSBBXhoO9mQ8AKOsro6J3DEW+pKQCEPtET\nnSeypcT+PvS/YgJQB69mRPdeL1oSsA0k7O8VwxCFQbXdUru0SLQzaOSCfGULtkaj\nBQB6P/cuUVMOLNIm5fGZGREX4v9RTvnco8PuyrFC8HDIjh/HBLBeSuwkfdKMoWKB\nJPGH0uX2k8jNj1Aa8xIHi4VhiUsaoalL2GfZ9wM3d5Drw1axjIp2wSlGpSwFvgsD\n6/KoIw9u/BLJmdtPLjk8ThAct95ZYFS6PJR2IVROJcO2tCOvYVjD5wJUGPOdgEO7\nN1JLDJO+w5RElUBCy8q2tchpJGgNvcoz59VP21bVzU/k6M4SG9FhCGkAd9d60vhR\nup3ytX/nVpJpOv/J9R48\n=7z2j\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0376604b0039d8bfc8f94400b489b16dda26f639\nparent e614fad02e2ac2d3acf6513c7aa29d180de028cd\nauthor Curtis 'Fjord' Hawthorne <fjord@openai.com> 1781149383 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781149383 -0700\n\ncore: strip image detail from Responses Lite requests (#27246)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Strip image `detail` fields from every Responses Lite request.\n- Apply stripping to message images and function/custom tool-output\nimages.\n- Transform only the formatted request copy without mutating stored\nhistory.\n- Preserve image URLs byte-for-byte, including HTTP(S) URLs, without\ndownloading, validating, or resizing them.\n- Preserve all image `detail` fields for non-Responses-Lite models.\n\n## Motivation\n\nResponses Lite does not support image `detail` tags, so Codex must omit\nthem whenever `model_info.use_responses_lite` is enabled. This transport\nrequirement is independent of the `resize_all_images` feature.\n\nStored history retains the original detail values. This keeps\nrequest-specific formatting isolated from conversation state and\npreserves the information for local image preparation and\nnon-Responses-Lite requests.\n\n\n#### [git stack](https://github.com/magus/git-stack-cli)\n- ✅ `1` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27245\n- ✅ `2` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27247\n- 👉 `3` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27246\n- ⏳ `4` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27266","verified_at":"2026-06-11T03:43:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4435ff28109bcef17b66c76a80c8478fddc2d541","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4435ff28109bcef17b66c76a80c8478fddc2d541","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4435ff28109bcef17b66c76a80c8478fddc2d541/comments","author":{"login":"fjord-oai","id":240979671,"node_id":"U_kgDODl0O1w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240979671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/fjord-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e614fad02e2ac2d3acf6513c7aa29d180de028cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e614fad02e2ac2d3acf6513c7aa29d180de028cd","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e614fad02e2ac2d3acf6513c7aa29d180de028cd"}]},{"sha":"e614fad02e2ac2d3acf6513c7aa29d180de028cd","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGU2MTRmYWQwMmUyYWMyZDNhY2Y2NTEzYzdhYTI5ZDE4MGRlMDI4Y2Q","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ahmed Ibrahim","email":"aibrahim@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T03:42:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T03:42:55Z"},"message":"[codex] Add comp_hash to model metadata (#27532)\n\n## Summary\n- add optional `comp_hash` metadata to `ModelInfo`\n- update `ModelInfo` fixtures for the shared schema change\n- keep older model responses compatible by defaulting the field to\n`None`\n\n## Why\nThe models endpoint needs an opaque identifier for compaction-compatible\nmodel configurations. This PR only exposes that value in model metadata;\nit does not add it to turn context or change runtime behavior.\n\nFollow-up #27520 carries the value through turn context and rollouts,\nthen uses it to trigger compaction.\n\n## Stack\n- based directly on `main`\n- replaces #27519, which was accidentally merged into the wrong base\nbranch\n- functionality follow-up: #27520\n\n## Testing\n- `just test -p codex-protocol\nmodel_info_defaults_availability_nux_to_none_when_omitted`\n- `just fix -p codex-core -p codex-protocol -p codex-analytics -p\ncodex-models-manager`","tree":{"sha":"29290aaf29c7b71570ac2f303c70895f5a62aa77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/29290aaf29c7b71570ac2f303c70895f5a62aa77"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e614fad02e2ac2d3acf6513c7aa29d180de028cd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKi6/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYc4QAD5htT4OWenbBIyjvVbn5YsH\npsuQ+uYAlZjMc5AlGCTP82Ly8X9MDpjQaFbPs2kTk3zZZeR4AD0IT1T7NutD1dqr\nfAy2MofR9CrrnrI3gppG6vfjQ0Qku1sk2PKLVn7i3So/Rf7CwBwUpLaOBZo4WbO4\nCqBF3BfSSUL4eJKK2dF4zwmj+PYA9X6TQmOl/rSLUXIoSyFy3UVa7SjJ+QqY2Ih5\nrssQr3QwZ+UDwx5LKO2sanR4tsEoFmf/GUOpSsykYoTKDJkGfYlWZ/d9JWetE9Pz\ndaAl4bIfVu3wyFVoDRCA3PkYVkE+yvHGOXJoAXKKBXknOkGDVjQoxzRUuaiXnL3R\nIrtCWmw3uz7UxY7eugTpjLPl62+o5ThfvIEzB9sFfPZP9L53cSpXLfYBP+R+aoev\nS49SJz5KLu/1hKXTbkYCIhBGbCm6IbALFFb15kep+3u44k4fJ9ZYirbT5LWyaVS3\niGpBN2BnVeFSYm1Vb5j57yXofsUSfYv2t/dTS/fm2dlyKad0v9Vz3u1NYiex9mgi\ncLa707ZiIrz2ESBLAr0f5L94LKRGRO5/tx4Qttz9oPop3o9bgG08h0K5j2+nFdxY\n68C/JkJ5PyhKNC1M52k24AMOpbBfGXz1Kf8UwBe0kQSciVI4gzkaS/ovbjDt96oM\nswob6mwcKz4X9ldIXtMr\n=aLyj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 29290aaf29c7b71570ac2f303c70895f5a62aa77\nparent 06afd63f4ae72e1b59ec761f0801bce71e1e742b\nauthor Ahmed Ibrahim <aibrahim@openai.com> 1781149375 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781149375 -0700\n\n[codex] Add comp_hash to model metadata (#27532)\n\n## Summary\n- add optional `comp_hash` metadata to `ModelInfo`\n- update `ModelInfo` fixtures for the shared schema change\n- keep older model responses compatible by defaulting the field to\n`None`\n\n## Why\nThe models endpoint needs an opaque identifier for compaction-compatible\nmodel configurations. This PR only exposes that value in model metadata;\nit does not add it to turn context or change runtime behavior.\n\nFollow-up #27520 carries the value through turn context and rollouts,\nthen uses it to trigger compaction.\n\n## Stack\n- based directly on `main`\n- replaces #27519, which was accidentally merged into the wrong base\nbranch\n- functionality follow-up: #27520\n\n## Testing\n- `just test -p codex-protocol\nmodel_info_defaults_availability_nux_to_none_when_omitted`\n- `just fix -p codex-core -p codex-protocol -p codex-analytics -p\ncodex-models-manager`","verified_at":"2026-06-11T03:42:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e614fad02e2ac2d3acf6513c7aa29d180de028cd","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e614fad02e2ac2d3acf6513c7aa29d180de028cd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e614fad02e2ac2d3acf6513c7aa29d180de028cd/comments","author":{"login":"aibrahim-oai","id":219906144,"node_id":"U_kgDODRuAYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219906144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/aibrahim-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"06afd63f4ae72e1b59ec761f0801bce71e1e742b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/06afd63f4ae72e1b59ec761f0801bce71e1e742b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/06afd63f4ae72e1b59ec761f0801bce71e1e742b"}]},{"sha":"06afd63f4ae72e1b59ec761f0801bce71e1e742b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDA2YWZkNjNmNGFlNzJlMWI1OWVjNzYxZjA4MDFiY2U3MWUxZTc0MmI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Celia Chen","email":"celia@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T03:42:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T03:42:38Z"},"message":"feat: add Bedrock API key as a managed auth mode (#27443)\n\n## Why\n\nCodex needs to manage Amazon Bedrock API key credentials through the\nexisting auth lifecycle instead of introducing a separate auth manager\nor provider-specific credential file. Treating Bedrock API key login as\na primary auth mode gives it the same persistence, keyring, reload, and\nlogout behavior as the existing OpenAI API key and ChatGPT modes.\n\nThe credential is valid only for the `amazon-bedrock` model provider.\nOpenAI-compatible providers must reject this auth mode rather than\ntreating the Bedrock key as an OpenAI bearer token.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added `bedrockApiKey` as an app-server `AuthMode` and\n`CodexAuth::BedrockApiKey` as a primary `AuthManager` mode.\n- Added `BedrockApiKeyAuth`, containing the API key and AWS region, to\nthe existing `AuthDotJson` payload stored in `$CODEX_HOME/auth.json` or\nthe configured keyring backend.\n- Added `login_with_bedrock_api_key(...)`, parallel to\n`login_with_api_key(...)`, which replaces the current stored login with\nBedrock credentials.\n- Reused generic auth reload and logout behavior instead of adding a\nBedrock-specific auth manager or logout path.\n- Updated login restrictions, status reporting, diagnostics, telemetry\nclassification, generated app-server schemas, and auth fixtures for the\nnew mode.\n- Added explicit errors when Bedrock API key auth is selected with an\nOpenAI-compatible model provider.\n\nThis PR establishes managed storage and auth-mode behavior. Routing the\nmanaged key and region into Amazon Bedrock requests will be in follow-up\nPRs.","tree":{"sha":"15d9bbf2e652a0e1cf94f225f691284b9886eb8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/15d9bbf2e652a0e1cf94f225f691284b9886eb8c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/06afd63f4ae72e1b59ec761f0801bce71e1e742b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKi6uCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATuYQAIKyjVn98SjWFqTtPtwOzF9r\nDtDQ6qtwRhFIMcth1AL3VEuTiPPGQBgn6gtFwrofcIB7+2O7nOwbLwcVmWptCjAs\n5Nf627T+nlhWHqtTREPnABnJ5562SZwyMILaeEBZm2YVHnmXezusjTXpTIpWYfRI\nUOUl05fJcBRVJkNMQLmZJ3ehODSCxbY7S+7t9fON8fp4E+G/1tQ+GNQAY9XBBEHv\ntj/XKSTGzgJmyuHHxZjO9KwQQBjZkn4pXj1L+ScRT4TbEJE1lIvoph6b7v+VTOKV\nIjaERH/ZhqQB8oMcOFIHoc+V7xvDsfxQFzNGAxF1B2NjqCcmbda9gz3l82LEIH17\n9dSGXvEbPvbAm3Id4vOJ4N3CzDZbxTQB9G1g5llfkaVY/vZeQJH/yCLQWnIXzBcE\n/Rg9Hle/Jqm1cd+UUL29GTx++QB60xfQHScD1ESsTqbvx55zyQZm7ohCoBgAghuT\ngUPfiveStZCG54T3hehmBwNE94JZk4r0iRWOzU2CBjl3aTb32/SPCwIRKAt9rG7P\nuCNfYbVT9kMEZQbtCAUHOMumoPVqEmCZvkvixISbGK9DtHOMSniHVJCCApKMg2A8\nL2CToeKENe0f93Q1DzaXFsDPGqK6snd+HK3fbeYyAyC+9zoZ2QmkFj1NLm9eXSaC\n+nG25Hjt69XKptu0tQVN\n=TvDr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 15d9bbf2e652a0e1cf94f225f691284b9886eb8c\nparent 87ab01834af30cfae99014ca93035d3068716b3f\nauthor Celia Chen <celia@openai.com> 1781149358 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781149358 -0700\n\nfeat: add Bedrock API key as a managed auth mode (#27443)\n\n## Why\n\nCodex needs to manage Amazon Bedrock API key credentials through the\nexisting auth lifecycle instead of introducing a separate auth manager\nor provider-specific credential file. Treating Bedrock API key login as\na primary auth mode gives it the same persistence, keyring, reload, and\nlogout behavior as the existing OpenAI API key and ChatGPT modes.\n\nThe credential is valid only for the `amazon-bedrock` model provider.\nOpenAI-compatible providers must reject this auth mode rather than\ntreating the Bedrock key as an OpenAI bearer token.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added `bedrockApiKey` as an app-server `AuthMode` and\n`CodexAuth::BedrockApiKey` as a primary `AuthManager` mode.\n- Added `BedrockApiKeyAuth`, containing the API key and AWS region, to\nthe existing `AuthDotJson` payload stored in `$CODEX_HOME/auth.json` or\nthe configured keyring backend.\n- Added `login_with_bedrock_api_key(...)`, parallel to\n`login_with_api_key(...)`, which replaces the current stored login with\nBedrock credentials.\n- Reused generic auth reload and logout behavior instead of adding a\nBedrock-specific auth manager or logout path.\n- Updated login restrictions, status reporting, diagnostics, telemetry\nclassification, generated app-server schemas, and auth fixtures for the\nnew mode.\n- Added explicit errors when Bedrock API key auth is selected with an\nOpenAI-compatible model provider.\n\nThis PR establishes managed storage and auth-mode behavior. Routing the\nmanaged key and region into Amazon Bedrock requests will be in follow-up\nPRs.","verified_at":"2026-06-11T03:42:39Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/06afd63f4ae72e1b59ec761f0801bce71e1e742b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/06afd63f4ae72e1b59ec761f0801bce71e1e742b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/06afd63f4ae72e1b59ec761f0801bce71e1e742b/comments","author":{"login":"celia-oai","id":209693228,"node_id":"U_kgDODH-qLA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/209693228?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/celia-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"87ab01834af30cfae99014ca93035d3068716b3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/87ab01834af30cfae99014ca93035d3068716b3f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/87ab01834af30cfae99014ca93035d3068716b3f"}]},{"sha":"87ab01834af30cfae99014ca93035d3068716b3f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDg3YWIwMTgzNGFmMzBjZmFlOTkwMTRjYTkzMDM1ZDMwNjg3MTZiM2Y","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T03:39:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T03:39:07Z"},"message":"[codex] Add new context window tool (#27488)\n\n## Why\n\nThe token budget feature tells the model how much room remains in the\ncurrent context window. When the model decides the current window is no\nlonger useful, it needs a way to ask Codex to start over with a fresh\ncontext window without spending tokens on a compaction summary.\n\nThis PR adds that model-requestable escape hatch on top of #27438.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added a direct-model-only `new_context` tool behind\n`Feature::TokenBudget`.\n- Stores the tool request on `AutoCompactWindow` and consumes it after\nsampling so the next follow-up request in the same turn starts in the\nnew window.\n- Starts the new window as a no-summary compaction checkpoint that\ncontains only fresh initial context, not preserved conversation history.\n- Keeps the new window aligned with token-budget startup context,\nincluding the `Current context window Z` message.\n- Added integration coverage and a snapshot showing the same-turn\n`new_context` flow into a fresh full-context follow-up request.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core token_budget`","tree":{"sha":"abf4fd341dd4c4af2194e15127cd78e384a66f8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/abf4fd341dd4c4af2194e15127cd78e384a66f8b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/87ab01834af30cfae99014ca93035d3068716b3f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKi3bCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASpwQAGWsIK85ApYo1BD1M6pG0z7U\nw2BG0IvoQ1IKJVUqFC9s1c8zyz/ZhIOLFya/Pk9nICoIULTaxzWyBJvA/xElWRpW\ns8QaL6QG5YQxg74qVu8YrKCp5pK+uJnN8pNBeBiauOVUB/qAHR47AIoztJWiEVSn\npgktHAXaTNP8vUHaxoGQkmvrck4YCkpkY2MeziiNEI3AWxkFJgDGglJNeB2raSB7\nt7tmdP7FIaja1E9RvMfBat8DoeSj3kR7l4JKzm/lUZKunIPGm82Vj3TEWnavl5n6\nJPquRcpdk8TuowIzqW+i8hbv8O2DwZ9CQA6FIun4XAOQL0j7Y8a+HsyZQeM+t9t5\nyc513vDc6XYS+aNlzssmuWBHFU3TkFUJMQOU+0KFwhKdHHTIt4bbWxTGK9ZES0PP\n3DOXJll281pDcgJ2JuXuu5Jyf4BD5fWNZ4uP+oZrH0Q08qRL8Kg6Q0RNRVkXanh+\n+WJhrG0PXJ+ubFLdbVLQhawbBfy2m7PJIjTB2GEIXZ3mOmXrnpj3Blxmyjg/Qn3+\npzVyOFlKyvwXBRyIlNbGqqPAdiUShTXexyF/EpgUSVK89ZL5LCOrpL48ni+0FMfV\nRBpegPkgmtSeKHp4pmRqELZt/2o6+f5+mm2Zy941W+I7n/ZNI71D/OuZFysAN7Cq\n0fUAMmG+qidh3mxbcugR\n=e75J\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree abf4fd341dd4c4af2194e15127cd78e384a66f8b\nparent 728b8243a9d74f437d8651b44995c0ccd8cae88e\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1781149147 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781149147 +0000\n\n[codex] Add new context window tool (#27488)\n\n## Why\n\nThe token budget feature tells the model how much room remains in the\ncurrent context window. When the model decides the current window is no\nlonger useful, it needs a way to ask Codex to start over with a fresh\ncontext window without spending tokens on a compaction summary.\n\nThis PR adds that model-requestable escape hatch on top of #27438.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added a direct-model-only `new_context` tool behind\n`Feature::TokenBudget`.\n- Stores the tool request on `AutoCompactWindow` and consumes it after\nsampling so the next follow-up request in the same turn starts in the\nnew window.\n- Starts the new window as a no-summary compaction checkpoint that\ncontains only fresh initial context, not preserved conversation history.\n- Keeps the new window aligned with token-budget startup context,\nincluding the `Current context window Z` message.\n- Added integration coverage and a snapshot showing the same-turn\n`new_context` flow into a fresh full-context follow-up request.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core token_budget`","verified_at":"2026-06-11T03:39:07Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/87ab01834af30cfae99014ca93035d3068716b3f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/87ab01834af30cfae99014ca93035d3068716b3f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/87ab01834af30cfae99014ca93035d3068716b3f/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"728b8243a9d74f437d8651b44995c0ccd8cae88e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/728b8243a9d74f437d8651b44995c0ccd8cae88e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/728b8243a9d74f437d8651b44995c0ccd8cae88e"}]},{"sha":"728b8243a9d74f437d8651b44995c0ccd8cae88e","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDcyOGI4MjQzYTlkNzRmNDM3ZDg2NTFiNDQ5OTVjMGNjZDhjYWU4OGU","commit":{"author":{"name":"sayan-oai","email":"sayan@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T03:37:25Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T03:37:25Z"},"message":"tools: simplify default tool search text (#27526)\n\n## Why\n\nDefault tool search text currently derives identity from both `ToolName`\nand `ToolSpec`. For function and namespace specs, this indexes the same\nnames more than once and also adds a flattened `{namespace}{name}` token\nthat is not model-visible.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Derive default search text entirely from `ToolSpec` while preserving\nnames, descriptions, namespace metadata, and recursive schema metadata.\n- Keep the default search-text builder private and remove the unused\n`ToolName` argument.\n- Add coverage for the exact search text generated for a namespaced tool\nwith nested schema metadata.\n\n## Example\n\nFor the `codex_app` namespace and `automation_update` tool (schema terms\nomitted):\n\n- Before: `codex_appautomation_update automation update codex_app\ncodex_app Manage Codex automations. automation_update automation update\n...`\n- After: `codex_app Manage Codex automations. automation_update\nautomation update ...`\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-tools`","tree":{"sha":"57c75b2776022cfbdf1eb9684fa395986818e164","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/57c75b2776022cfbdf1eb9684fa395986818e164"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/728b8243a9d74f437d8651b44995c0ccd8cae88e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKi11CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAouIQAD3lLuilRgzqvWe8A3MWclGo\nDf4JM2YBy1g5vkTzEK7e4EZErB+iD4iPGQg6YnCbIIouwuUHnIr9iOQRtc5+kuZH\noY2fe7Fi/0U/hUzIDK7Yq5OsKJ90sn/tFa3HdoPFyRRQCEckG85ursP2VaEa76Wl\nf84LcAqobDYki4kmT50sFvYM/+CKzEwhOb1Qt3xVyt95lKxb1/c9p0IV39V4wmCH\nadY0j1cIuTDnQ0l2q2mBomqNf6vqwGjOoe6DinOlg1MMZ6+vszZOet1MkWfsMaAU\nVqHrx3andYVs/au0bCmnZQK7QW5VkML0PZdRboNoQ1wmT3NeMTX1Dioon8e5S4p/\n3+i1wcTSeJA54kPYMPocdfgvtE/pVF3LVDYJrv2f/XQI/o4jR0wGu6q13HUmUbxc\nAv+Zpad1MsD23IKhPa8mymbOAHDqhYVU00M0EOmO1+Or1OWr9pgcBe45gzoXSnIJ\nA6KfK/OW1wRlEi9PFJMWhG/O+x8UScLZ7Ey+jEHa9nN8Xi6j/LvQv5gH0nePJgm0\nWHqJOK+gaIw8QBw8ymSJ3IdUXHCbf5JjKMQxmPL0xRnjbGENHatD79C5kDNeYFz5\njj72lX25wBJQehxco/N5JGzgZLMuNAc5Kob7PqywS+c56o+QF8jCKZz3WieoagDb\nq4EtiPut1PBrCpxQnb8k\n=2nQt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 57c75b2776022cfbdf1eb9684fa395986818e164\nparent f1f9d0c3b5606d8da1c7f7839fc6e0cb85dd5d04\nauthor sayan-oai <sayan@openai.com> 1781149045 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781149045 +0000\n\ntools: simplify default tool search text (#27526)\n\n## Why\n\nDefault tool search text currently derives identity from both `ToolName`\nand `ToolSpec`. For function and namespace specs, this indexes the same\nnames more than once and also adds a flattened `{namespace}{name}` token\nthat is not model-visible.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Derive default search text entirely from `ToolSpec` while preserving\nnames, descriptions, namespace metadata, and recursive schema metadata.\n- Keep the default search-text builder private and remove the unused\n`ToolName` argument.\n- Add coverage for the exact search text generated for a namespaced tool\nwith nested schema metadata.\n\n## Example\n\nFor the `codex_app` namespace and `automation_update` tool (schema terms\nomitted):\n\n- Before: `codex_appautomation_update automation update codex_app\ncodex_app Manage Codex automations. automation_update automation update\n...`\n- After: `codex_app Manage Codex automations. automation_update\nautomation update ...`\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-tools`","verified_at":"2026-06-11T03:37:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/728b8243a9d74f437d8651b44995c0ccd8cae88e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/728b8243a9d74f437d8651b44995c0ccd8cae88e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/728b8243a9d74f437d8651b44995c0ccd8cae88e/comments","author":{"login":"sayan-oai","id":244841968,"node_id":"U_kgDODpf98A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244841968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/sayan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f1f9d0c3b5606d8da1c7f7839fc6e0cb85dd5d04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f1f9d0c3b5606d8da1c7f7839fc6e0cb85dd5d04","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f1f9d0c3b5606d8da1c7f7839fc6e0cb85dd5d04"}]},{"sha":"f1f9d0c3b5606d8da1c7f7839fc6e0cb85dd5d04","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGYxZjlkMGMzYjU2MDZkOGRhMWM3Zjc4MzlmYzZlMGNiODVkZDVkMDQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"yuning-oai","email":"yuning@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T03:30:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T03:30:44Z"},"message":"[codex] Expand hosted web search citation guidance (#27501)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Expand the hosted web search prompt with explicit Markdown-link\ncitation guidance.\n- Keep internal `turnX` reference IDs out of final responses and place\ncitations next to supported claims.\n\n## Context\n\n\nhttps://openai.slack.com/archives/C0AU83S0ZQU/p1781133381448499?thread_ts=1780352049.512299&cid=C0AU83S0ZQU\n\n## Test plan\n\n- Confirmed `codex-rs/ext/web-search/web_run_description.md` exactly\nmatches the supplied target prompt.\n- `UV_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/codex-uv-cache\nPATH=/tmp/codex-just/bin:/home/dev-user/.rustup/toolchains/1.95.0-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/bin:$PATH\npython3 scripts/format.py --check`\n- `git diff --check`","tree":{"sha":"61fed0835a95b0545f496c1b035c1739b415f142","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/61fed0835a95b0545f496c1b035c1739b415f142"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f1f9d0c3b5606d8da1c7f7839fc6e0cb85dd5d04","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKivkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYQYQALHKp9Cn7pQKV/MGCm/gKqZP\nUB8bL4Cmcy4TrgFISHMQGbcci/lOX60SO/N/JpYbquLk7zgRoB6XIqHOGT5Nt0F8\n00VBkc/aPynHSLCfcgSUREQBGulJjK3hwKVB5MIrLLsmckdqmKP62VllMxRnsgzW\n3NsUP7LnctA/G7h/KWo7FZjqpSyl1q6tW74ANlYbYbbJRKXLmauZ/EyoWNoyVviU\nGYHsf95qVZhAXiIRjYPeNxIpveUiQ1xb5276LSmhokz0Gj6xXx7QGSiKpsEMZQ6M\nzdZe5JnMXs9lZkKANrR895Xj+At4YN5CcrRIa+FN34b5ooEKjx1iYv3HkrSuagxK\nSzyU0UYgLv81TxCDorVBcIuaJNBx2nXPFrdqiSng+YnL0o9lLLJ+Zu9fsYIBadT+\n5V1VMC7Zplz+G55ZmOSgpGG3o7a/YPq5bgYmSMD4TBwkrVnDdOPtTP4dUZiqzWrV\n6gzpUk/qfnPV3baXjWwCcNI51I84HnYWdMw/Ez0V7NLGX3BBzkCg8zFU9HV2299j\nEng8/OUSv+186hP8qIZu4s0STuynCi/3fidejo0z0y3yGc3CXb2BmHxHVQ60+DBS\nSUxz3r+U13NGCSoyZnqLN1GYhjeT/V3ERmC05so8OqZb2d9Rgj0AfVZcw9Jszbe0\n8na6dXMEhnwHTK3egOY9\n=5Zd6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 61fed0835a95b0545f496c1b035c1739b415f142\nparent 658af936fdd04cd2661e253b4fe78d769aef8534\nauthor yuning-oai <yuning@openai.com> 1781148644 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781148644 +0000\n\n[codex] Expand hosted web search citation guidance (#27501)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Expand the hosted web search prompt with explicit Markdown-link\ncitation guidance.\n- Keep internal `turnX` reference IDs out of final responses and place\ncitations next to supported claims.\n\n## Context\n\n\nhttps://openai.slack.com/archives/C0AU83S0ZQU/p1781133381448499?thread_ts=1780352049.512299&cid=C0AU83S0ZQU\n\n## Test plan\n\n- Confirmed `codex-rs/ext/web-search/web_run_description.md` exactly\nmatches the supplied target prompt.\n- `UV_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/codex-uv-cache\nPATH=/tmp/codex-just/bin:/home/dev-user/.rustup/toolchains/1.95.0-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/bin:$PATH\npython3 scripts/format.py --check`\n- `git diff --check`","verified_at":"2026-06-11T03:30:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f1f9d0c3b5606d8da1c7f7839fc6e0cb85dd5d04","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f1f9d0c3b5606d8da1c7f7839fc6e0cb85dd5d04","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f1f9d0c3b5606d8da1c7f7839fc6e0cb85dd5d04/comments","author":{"login":"yuning-oai","id":257628876,"node_id":"U_kgDOD1sazA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257628876?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuning-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/yuning-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuning-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuning-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuning-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuning-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuning-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuning-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuning-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuning-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yuning-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"658af936fdd04cd2661e253b4fe78d769aef8534","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/658af936fdd04cd2661e253b4fe78d769aef8534","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/658af936fdd04cd2661e253b4fe78d769aef8534"}]},{"sha":"658af936fdd04cd2661e253b4fe78d769aef8534","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDY1OGFmOTM2ZmRkMDRjZDI2NjFlMjUzYjRmZTc4ZDc2OWFlZjg1MzQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T03:07:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T03:07:06Z"},"message":"[codex] Add token budget context feature (#27438)\n\n## Why\n\nThe model should be able to see bounded context-window budget metadata\nwhen the `token_budget` feature is enabled. The full-window message is\nonly injected with full context, while normal turns get a smaller\nfollow-up only when reported usage first crosses a budget threshold.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added the `TokenBudget` feature flag.\n- Added `<token_budget>` developer fragments for full context-window\nmetadata and current-window remaining tokens.\n- Inserted the threshold message during normal turn handling by\ncomparing token usage before and after sampling, avoiding persistent\nthreshold bookkeeping.\n- Added core integration coverage for full-context-only metadata and\n25/50/75 percent threshold messages.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-core token_budget`\n- `git diff --check`","tree":{"sha":"d9f3685cd1bb2fe727b61d598b0e6bfbca2c02aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d9f3685cd1bb2fe727b61d598b0e6bfbca2c02aa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/658af936fdd04cd2661e253b4fe78d769aef8534","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKiZaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6YIQAKkSeR263nNGp1hri59ixg9f\n+sJ/XdDWzEE4YiAbdNbNA642/MKjN/Z1fpDyJn+evLqWh6QS55YIweB+gA1v36/5\nxoJBYnKzyI2eQ9bTOELq5c1H17IPJkQM1PdEptS0y1QKRwp9q2NtSM7rHfBUP6Xj\nqo7jv5mREfMOS8KGdktmI99bhJboQyrb33L2CIaNmP41KL0qXHumE/qggiBCfMIx\nu+LqCtANka36e0NjuuaBam3oGJa9wMMik1Hjc4M/RPhKptSPotCVRcysJQBKTg/b\n/BYzDzLXKUx0gRsPLpm9WqIl/KwB+4DhwxJJFZDAvIymxOwTRmEptQ/GR5R+Pcjh\nIts+v9Z7b+hN++3ohnN5PUdDA2CKga7yMr81QTaxdzLDn5cCi8JFZo/K4yQu/QqP\nQJZJRYqvrp/lXUzipDya6UlOeMYwBBiBll3PR0GV8gkNimPThjhmBa4wjmUnQ3W9\nH/VSDt2pMbxeSiBKGJRNiAOZx8oKcdouhFKm0T1smD7ksLEcL6Boh5AfbTqE6A+l\n7HnlTvng+4U0JcA+lTz1Dl9grR4fMDwdQqNBdoFbIffUGZrG4819fEXWDfzIIoUV\nydMenRRUPhLUNni4IQT/PHka+YjRRL3cC0HoefGtBA0b86dMF1K0DVLXALA93Le9\nRpGH/ODQ+d3Ij9Xcvcvs\n=KQHW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d9f3685cd1bb2fe727b61d598b0e6bfbca2c02aa\nparent ab4ce40042498d82854c4005ab5f10fe00317981\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1781147226 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781147226 -0700\n\n[codex] Add token budget context feature (#27438)\n\n## Why\n\nThe model should be able to see bounded context-window budget metadata\nwhen the `token_budget` feature is enabled. The full-window message is\nonly injected with full context, while normal turns get a smaller\nfollow-up only when reported usage first crosses a budget threshold.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added the `TokenBudget` feature flag.\n- Added `<token_budget>` developer fragments for full context-window\nmetadata and current-window remaining tokens.\n- Inserted the threshold message during normal turn handling by\ncomparing token usage before and after sampling, avoiding persistent\nthreshold bookkeeping.\n- Added core integration coverage for full-context-only metadata and\n25/50/75 percent threshold messages.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-core token_budget`\n- `git diff --check`","verified_at":"2026-06-11T03:07:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/658af936fdd04cd2661e253b4fe78d769aef8534","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/658af936fdd04cd2661e253b4fe78d769aef8534","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/658af936fdd04cd2661e253b4fe78d769aef8534/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ab4ce40042498d82854c4005ab5f10fe00317981","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ab4ce40042498d82854c4005ab5f10fe00317981","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ab4ce40042498d82854c4005ab5f10fe00317981"}]},{"sha":"ab4ce40042498d82854c4005ab5f10fe00317981","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGFiNGNlNDAwNDI0OThkODI4NTRjNDAwNWFiNWYxMGZlMDAzMTc5ODE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T02:50:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T02:50:57Z"},"message":"Trim TUI legacy telemetry and migration dependencies (#27487)\n\n## Why\n\nThe TUI still reached through `codex-app-server-client::legacy_core` for\nprocess telemetry setup and personality migration, exposing core-only\ndetails after the TUI moved onto the app-server layer.\n\nThis is part of our ongoing efforts to whittle away at the legacy_core\nshim that was left over after migrating the TUI to the app server.\n\nThis change is just a refactor/rename and should be behavior-neutral and\nlow risk.\n\n## What changed\n\n- expose OTEL provider construction through the app-server client and\nkeep the small process/SQLite telemetry adapters local to the TUI\n- collapse personality migration results to the config-reload decision\nthe TUI needs\n- remove the `legacy_core::otel_init` and\n`legacy_core::personality_migration` subnamespaces","tree":{"sha":"21081cbd72aa5c15069708ce567fbd3571f80a84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/21081cbd72aa5c15069708ce567fbd3571f80a84"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/ab4ce40042498d82854c4005ab5f10fe00317981","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKiKRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfEEQAIUC93W0zf79ZrjavBkoqQAm\nLaGC7iX0+IqxA07Yk3EMSxnLT43A6KhGQo2I0GNrCAL5N5Em+r0Vrup451D/7hsD\nR7b2rW0PANG7JxTLmPdIpgjAhXpwcOGUOsSCr9QTvaydLmtwas1HAi+kDEUnSQ1l\nzdh/egmMunj1Efsw8l4sAaKaXTl9ycB2sOdTxumVOqE/onQ34ocqJMhBDXlz6fGD\nMMvh/5iliwdpT+xx8lruBk3hs0QNHNDSajZQT0MSxVWP/eB3YveCYG44emnTHRzt\nhMq41VIJGFvWbZI1il4V3WKtROJYMJ/iOHMozitpbrxt1Ydl/ouHV7qmsoxiuf2g\nPU+27NGIVvICFCBUFFxVeAZOdeirDfkSt3sVxebmlYqKpSxdO3xKhYm/qJgkiehS\n58xEAuib0Rsp2oZ6YIF0HWVh4RnOWAp1Z85RQ0Ica128xpVlLhdJaGpoTfE8kowb\nyUApyi4wVl3QMhanv/KqA/rFnn7PjwykLh6DmWkPxDP229LiiNAt45MIg+LrjgXX\nIPW/sGKsE3nfZfiPwZbQ2oPx3Ondq6OC4AjLCOBnUpWjFY8upJ/dktiDPloECld4\nIJrnbgvl+qDBByAuVdOZ83sSFLb+ILsWuJIoUGAso6vkABiQ6VAFYfAnvLwhC6iW\nDnlkPwJlrFR/MOfvFbMy\n=U/vN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 21081cbd72aa5c15069708ce567fbd3571f80a84\nparent a6f435ea94e8a8ff516cdaf8f5fe5a5bdafee449\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1781146257 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781146257 -0700\n\nTrim TUI legacy telemetry and migration dependencies (#27487)\n\n## Why\n\nThe TUI still reached through `codex-app-server-client::legacy_core` for\nprocess telemetry setup and personality migration, exposing core-only\ndetails after the TUI moved onto the app-server layer.\n\nThis is part of our ongoing efforts to whittle away at the legacy_core\nshim that was left over after migrating the TUI to the app server.\n\nThis change is just a refactor/rename and should be behavior-neutral and\nlow risk.\n\n## What changed\n\n- expose OTEL provider construction through the app-server client and\nkeep the small process/SQLite telemetry adapters local to the TUI\n- collapse personality migration results to the config-reload decision\nthe TUI needs\n- remove the `legacy_core::otel_init` and\n`legacy_core::personality_migration` subnamespaces","verified_at":"2026-06-11T02:50:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ab4ce40042498d82854c4005ab5f10fe00317981","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ab4ce40042498d82854c4005ab5f10fe00317981","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ab4ce40042498d82854c4005ab5f10fe00317981/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a6f435ea94e8a8ff516cdaf8f5fe5a5bdafee449","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a6f435ea94e8a8ff516cdaf8f5fe5a5bdafee449","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a6f435ea94e8a8ff516cdaf8f5fe5a5bdafee449"}]},{"sha":"a6f435ea94e8a8ff516cdaf8f5fe5a5bdafee449","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGE2ZjQzNWVhOTRlOGE4ZmY1MTZjZGFmOGY1ZmU1YTViZGFmZWU0NDk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Curtis 'Fjord' Hawthorne","email":"fjord@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T02:21:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T02:21:24Z"},"message":"core: resize all history images behind a feature flag (#27247)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds complete client-side image preparation behind the default-off\n`resize_all_images` feature flag.\n\nWhen enabled, local image producers defer decoding and resizing. Images\nare prepared centrally before insertion into conversation history,\ncovering user input, `view_image`, and structured tool-output images.\n\n## Behavior\n\n- Processes base64 `data:` images in messages and function/custom tool\noutputs.\n- Leaves non-data URLs, including HTTP(S) URLs, unchanged.\n- Applies image-detail budgets:\n  - `high` and omitted: 2048px maximum dimension and 2.5K 32px patches.\n  - `original`: 6000px maximum dimension and 10K 32px patches.\n  - `auto`: uses the same 2048px / 2.5K-patch budget as high.\n  - `low`: unsupported and replaced with an actionable placeholder.\n- Preserves original image bytes when no resize or format conversion is\nneeded.\n- Enforces the shared 1 GiB encoded and decoded data-URL sanity limits.\n- Replaces only an image that fails preparation, preserving sibling\ncontent and tool-output metadata.\n- Uses bounded placeholders distinguishing generic processing failures,\noversized images, and unsupported `low` detail.\n- Prepares resumed and forked history before installing it as live\nhistory without modifying persisted rollouts.\n\n## Flag-Off Behavior\n\nWhen `resize_all_images` is disabled:\n\n- Existing local user-input and `view_image` processing remains\nunchanged.\n- Existing decoding and error behavior remains unchanged.\n- Arbitrary tool-output images are not processed.\n- HTTP(S) image URLs continue to be forwarded unchanged.\n\n\n#### [git stack](https://github.com/magus/git-stack-cli)\n- ✅ `1` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27245\n- 👉 `2` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27247\n- ⏳ `3` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27246\n- ⏳ `4` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27266","tree":{"sha":"4deab2021b56652f5e3e6a15713c01f5ca6ee08d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/4deab2021b56652f5e3e6a15713c01f5ca6ee08d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a6f435ea94e8a8ff516cdaf8f5fe5a5bdafee449","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKhukCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVZoQAFDfTIc63FJrNUdU2nDwu+ag\nOhnN3gS/VaC1dK2T12pi2MgIYKDXKwemQjqYxBAtQI3agd9Fx3ewy9PgIEWkaIN3\n16ZFieDa8xoMPoT/Lg+Yhc52B/45bTcBWVRl8mM/ygrCOMTbuaRE4n2KOMd+ELXg\nH2Vd1SSDdKPuommuE4fp5W0bMeOe2fpWDxhzhxMwLx8kzVHx3QSfIuQPI7oaWcG3\nGzOo1vmOSl6o+/JkSQ67LabUz6uujyZyq/AIZKRwmhXXjLR248AyozGL1deGdZTE\nj2z6fOeHd8dRemxIXsc8JwKPu0WUYGGz9kn7EYgJZuHaVbdzcvGsr8E6FRSS6tSG\nXC+N/H8tkqsZo7beAuHxiXOpLk5y7pR+AB+hXmWu21DIh3WcGlhE2vKjhHM3NO+P\nalxRNhK0E269kkbm6BS1OEnUAS8Nk5/VGzgEuIpX4moCw0Wv9wsS7TUZ44O1C1jb\nE3S09tojigJ7DzVZEfCrmhw75QZ/XY7uwINhf1wwGe1pt7llj7Fgu0CEsnrlRfxc\nN+e8iEpVJgrIell35tASZ86SMrDtifkg2n+IUSRmDSTG0C3+EEv8XqGcCPpHvBO9\nbjzQRpWhsfiIu7UNi2beUzGyv3cy87UDznAU7C8kKYwLSoX42JHb//+yOYnqeBvV\nhrgjU05ioPRvLyXfwBU8\n=ESLE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4deab2021b56652f5e3e6a15713c01f5ca6ee08d\nparent 9d87b771cebd0f80e4637e80c93b0d66b10d86c0\nauthor Curtis 'Fjord' Hawthorne <fjord@openai.com> 1781144484 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781144484 -0700\n\ncore: resize all history images behind a feature flag (#27247)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds complete client-side image preparation behind the default-off\n`resize_all_images` feature flag.\n\nWhen enabled, local image producers defer decoding and resizing. Images\nare prepared centrally before insertion into conversation history,\ncovering user input, `view_image`, and structured tool-output images.\n\n## Behavior\n\n- Processes base64 `data:` images in messages and function/custom tool\noutputs.\n- Leaves non-data URLs, including HTTP(S) URLs, unchanged.\n- Applies image-detail budgets:\n  - `high` and omitted: 2048px maximum dimension and 2.5K 32px patches.\n  - `original`: 6000px maximum dimension and 10K 32px patches.\n  - `auto`: uses the same 2048px / 2.5K-patch budget as high.\n  - `low`: unsupported and replaced with an actionable placeholder.\n- Preserves original image bytes when no resize or format conversion is\nneeded.\n- Enforces the shared 1 GiB encoded and decoded data-URL sanity limits.\n- Replaces only an image that fails preparation, preserving sibling\ncontent and tool-output metadata.\n- Uses bounded placeholders distinguishing generic processing failures,\noversized images, and unsupported `low` detail.\n- Prepares resumed and forked history before installing it as live\nhistory without modifying persisted rollouts.\n\n## Flag-Off Behavior\n\nWhen `resize_all_images` is disabled:\n\n- Existing local user-input and `view_image` processing remains\nunchanged.\n- Existing decoding and error behavior remains unchanged.\n- Arbitrary tool-output images are not processed.\n- HTTP(S) image URLs continue to be forwarded unchanged.\n\n\n#### [git stack](https://github.com/magus/git-stack-cli)\n- ✅ `1` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27245\n- 👉 `2` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27247\n- ⏳ `3` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27246\n- ⏳ `4` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27266","verified_at":"2026-06-11T02:21:25Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a6f435ea94e8a8ff516cdaf8f5fe5a5bdafee449","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a6f435ea94e8a8ff516cdaf8f5fe5a5bdafee449","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a6f435ea94e8a8ff516cdaf8f5fe5a5bdafee449/comments","author":{"login":"fjord-oai","id":240979671,"node_id":"U_kgDODl0O1w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240979671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/fjord-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9d87b771cebd0f80e4637e80c93b0d66b10d86c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9d87b771cebd0f80e4637e80c93b0d66b10d86c0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9d87b771cebd0f80e4637e80c93b0d66b10d86c0"}]},{"sha":"9d87b771cebd0f80e4637e80c93b0d66b10d86c0","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDlkODdiNzcxY2ViZDBmODBlNDYzN2U4MGM5M2IwZDY2YjEwZDg2YzA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T01:04:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T01:04:02Z"},"message":"Add session delete commands in CLI and TUI (#27476)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe app server exposes `thread/delete`, but users cannot invoke it from\nthe CLI or TUI. Because deletion is irreversible, the user-facing\ncommands need deliberate confirmation and safer handling of name-based\ntargets.\n\n- Add `codex delete <SESSION>` with interactive confirmation,\nrestricting `--force` to UUID targets.\n- Resolve exact names across active and archived sessions, including\nrenamed sessions, and validate prompted UUID targets before\nconfirmation.\n- Add a `/delete` command with a confirmation popup that warns the\ncurrent session and its subagent threads will be permanently deleted.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- Deleted by UUID with `--force` and verified the rollout, session-index\nentry, and database row were removed.\n- Exercised name-based confirmation for both cancellation and\naffirmative deletion; cancellation preserved the session and\nconfirmation removed it.\n- Verified deletion refuses to proceed without `--force`, while\n`--force` rejects names, including duplicate names.\n- Verified duplicate-name confirmation displays the concrete UUID\nselected.\n- Deleted an archived session by name.\n- Verified an already-missing UUID fails before displaying a\nconfirmation prompt.\n- Exercised `/delete` in the TUI: the popup defaults to No, cancellation\npreserves the session, and confirmation deletes the session and exits.\n- Verified that `codex delete` works for both archived and non-archived\nsessions.","tree":{"sha":"41994f223d257ca21c5997ea5e5c7f55824f8665","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/41994f223d257ca21c5997ea5e5c7f55824f8665"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/9d87b771cebd0f80e4637e80c93b0d66b10d86c0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKgmCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgNYQALBCjMsLZbWIA9leEGFJry4M\n2EY4eTFVqDSLV3LqXnoL7FaJSjCSuHZCHEkCJlu/Y3wj8LGuBu5hCNJ9xGZjOT3V\nvyxF4V/9kEIVVdq2bUie65AcB+2GhCz3Er6A+YgtheN5mZTqlZN2ipC5cc9i0bVv\nevJFx91zWrDhKl7PxM/6hxbE2D0mjYsz7mFV0E1Prfwf/NPJlDNyW7NqWdwtTis6\nBh7H/6ZGXN5pOuHG4oHCGsUXV8V0HaLPJYp0uV7IE4EnroRQhl+KBxngfy6HiskJ\nuj0XjrROuI9Rkvr5zrmEHlhrY4ZgTUIDtgXx5106L8tVq34izRoX9OjQg4GLp+8c\nFmxguSncoPMYhJDr8DK1xleaRKZLE0V+ObbwXRYUlh0eUCb63Q/DWZAx7l0SEhjz\nAHcnPogP5uRYvOJo7EDrRGsFLrUc1isGzZxoHZE5tMDR8/IpMglNWAdlRh4CzGwp\nL7P3c6Hlh8B+Rq2WLnmKN0cpA6A//LMQSHY18nsJCLcF1SsePrHl/uGGA/kT8MM8\nyfvgFZRiafKf5pvNm7XVEDttQ+KZ2kDeXXxd3xyQudgVkz9xbgNY2h/2wCxfnjhO\nMk3Xu8I30tps/b1Mg/+Dj5JYpTZJ5BrRUizdoEAot/a3yahq5rdkYAK9K07zTBk6\nbIy/UEjU4pUmjg9DKaO3\n=JHe7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 41994f223d257ca21c5997ea5e5c7f55824f8665\nparent 36fc79c6f4122a39b2dc10073d7e38706385675e\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1781139842 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781139842 -0700\n\nAdd session delete commands in CLI and TUI (#27476)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe app server exposes `thread/delete`, but users cannot invoke it from\nthe CLI or TUI. Because deletion is irreversible, the user-facing\ncommands need deliberate confirmation and safer handling of name-based\ntargets.\n\n- Add `codex delete <SESSION>` with interactive confirmation,\nrestricting `--force` to UUID targets.\n- Resolve exact names across active and archived sessions, including\nrenamed sessions, and validate prompted UUID targets before\nconfirmation.\n- Add a `/delete` command with a confirmation popup that warns the\ncurrent session and its subagent threads will be permanently deleted.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- Deleted by UUID with `--force` and verified the rollout, session-index\nentry, and database row were removed.\n- Exercised name-based confirmation for both cancellation and\naffirmative deletion; cancellation preserved the session and\nconfirmation removed it.\n- Verified deletion refuses to proceed without `--force`, while\n`--force` rejects names, including duplicate names.\n- Verified duplicate-name confirmation displays the concrete UUID\nselected.\n- Deleted an archived session by name.\n- Verified an already-missing UUID fails before displaying a\nconfirmation prompt.\n- Exercised `/delete` in the TUI: the popup defaults to No, cancellation\npreserves the session, and confirmation deletes the session and exits.\n- Verified that `codex delete` works for both archived and non-archived\nsessions.","verified_at":"2026-06-11T01:04:03Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9d87b771cebd0f80e4637e80c93b0d66b10d86c0","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9d87b771cebd0f80e4637e80c93b0d66b10d86c0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9d87b771cebd0f80e4637e80c93b0d66b10d86c0/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"36fc79c6f4122a39b2dc10073d7e38706385675e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/36fc79c6f4122a39b2dc10073d7e38706385675e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/36fc79c6f4122a39b2dc10073d7e38706385675e"}]},{"sha":"36fc79c6f4122a39b2dc10073d7e38706385675e","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDM2ZmM3OWM2ZjQxMjJhMzliMmRjMTAwNzNkN2UzODcwNjM4NTY3NWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T00:55:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T00:55:49Z"},"message":"Remove TUI legacy core test_support dependencies (#27484)\n\n## Why\n\nThe TUI now sits on the app-server layer, but\n`app-server-client::legacy_core` still exposed core test helpers solely\nfor TUI tests. We've been whittling away the remaining dependencies.\nThis is the next step on that journey.\n\nThere is no functional change — just a refactor, and this affects only\ntest code, so it should be low risk.\n\n## What changed\n\n- remove the `legacy_core::test_support` re-export and call\nmodel-manager test helpers directly\n- keep the bundled model-preset cache local to TUI test support\n- import constraint types directly from `codex-config`","tree":{"sha":"cd942a20b9dd07f78d50e6f1fd755ffe6a91ead4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/cd942a20b9dd07f78d50e6f1fd755ffe6a91ead4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/36fc79c6f4122a39b2dc10073d7e38706385675e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKgeVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUeMQAFBX4avKrA3/eovWhKpsQVu2\ndJi0kSaAEFUl2Xbpg8b7gSvI8cbkw1N7Z7bIapE6QzOmQLntB3nR3/DRLujvWxJG\nHo8G0SU1+uYBrxnyXppOpz1qElW0XY6sX+h6QFDLYbygj5LUtk2BcZBQoFD5XkCW\nr2tr1WkJFHoEJFHjYglnkCXvtxv4TwtI/emJF/uml2F1CtvgeYm1+66/zu/LD8Er\n86xRrcsE+CYCcKI586s4giIxbekr1rhBODnA/4svRvG6zImGLqhYJTVh5JRImN4j\nm/FT3qNgyTNiK/Qgo5vlQZ0G1vOa0QpGFzlRNnOrJ3nynwuADY5EmUv8RBoutI2o\niJdXIITKZ2U1Ndj3Zwv15LEdOTRDJMDBwQLn5RW8uS7NGyOowSsnetXjnBRtXWUb\npSx8PSwEUIzEyLgsJ4ciyuSRZxM1QPZ/SC/47/t/cBTfrvKlVw8r4G6MMV6bfp3g\nexU9VcRIZH3ws9Pt5qght5qOtdoko840W3djVFRmI8CLFEgQTuDVnHCRPu0PuPNG\nDrm0zzMhrKDmYJDRfxwN11ASjyiqa5yM6s+ucRGzZ2DShFRFB3P9mXq/qvk9IJhp\nT1PPC3N3N2NhwYmaanVvywDSQ8qqYs+GDmjK0uzD+Xzu3nDj2NrkIN04pSoGLVen\npplso/Fv016xV5c7mbIg\n=F5A2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree cd942a20b9dd07f78d50e6f1fd755ffe6a91ead4\nparent 1a9efd473b2cccfc7c82d442d5557be6974db133\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1781139349 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781139349 -0700\n\nRemove TUI legacy core test_support dependencies (#27484)\n\n## Why\n\nThe TUI now sits on the app-server layer, but\n`app-server-client::legacy_core` still exposed core test helpers solely\nfor TUI tests. We've been whittling away the remaining dependencies.\nThis is the next step on that journey.\n\nThere is no functional change — just a refactor, and this affects only\ntest code, so it should be low risk.\n\n## What changed\n\n- remove the `legacy_core::test_support` re-export and call\nmodel-manager test helpers directly\n- keep the bundled model-preset cache local to TUI test support\n- import constraint types directly from `codex-config`","verified_at":"2026-06-11T00:55:49Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/36fc79c6f4122a39b2dc10073d7e38706385675e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/36fc79c6f4122a39b2dc10073d7e38706385675e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/36fc79c6f4122a39b2dc10073d7e38706385675e/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1a9efd473b2cccfc7c82d442d5557be6974db133","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1a9efd473b2cccfc7c82d442d5557be6974db133","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1a9efd473b2cccfc7c82d442d5557be6974db133"}]},{"sha":"1a9efd473b2cccfc7c82d442d5557be6974db133","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDFhOWVmZDQ3M2IyY2NjZmM3YzgyZDQ0MmQ1NTU3YmU2OTc0ZGIxMzM","commit":{"author":{"name":"xl-openai","email":"xl@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T00:33:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T00:33:56Z"},"message":"[codex] Remove redundant plugin app auth state (#27465)\n\n## Summary\n\n- remove the redundant `needsAuth` field from `AppSummary` and generated\napp-server schemas\n- stop `plugin/read` from querying Apps MCP solely to hydrate unused\nconnector auth state\n- preserve `plugin/install.appsNeedingAuth` membership and\n`app/list.isAccessible` as the authentication signals\n\n## Why\n\nCodex App and TUI do not consume `plugin/read.plugin.apps[].needsAuth`.\nHydrating it could establish an Apps MCP connection and discover tools\non a cold `plugin/read` request, adding avoidable latency. The plugin\nAPIs are still marked under development, so removing this wire field is\npreferable to retaining a misleading default.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just write-app-server-schema`\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nplugin_install_uses_remote_apps_needing_auth_response`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nplugin_install_returns_apps_needing_auth`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nplugin_read_returns_plugin_details_with_bundle_contents`\n- `just test -p codex-tui\nplugin_detail_popup_snapshot_shows_install_actions_and_capability_summaries`\n- `$xin-build` simplify and debug reviews","tree":{"sha":"b394ca0d4a7aa7ceaac229e2eb585effb347aabb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/b394ca0d4a7aa7ceaac229e2eb585effb347aabb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/1a9efd473b2cccfc7c82d442d5557be6974db133","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKgJ0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABBcQAA62nJSZbhWnEIp3xqbeLb8E\ncRLIOIi/sY9iB+YQt6xc1OMveIPtYgMl7CQDmcUtbZ3ry+zoQ/8wFvsmyxc+OgFr\nyMkb5wTUCABkR3sg4yLxLiMAAwfOl15vn/qkXsiHvSzhGimfY+5L8g673NDWotfu\n/h8L0AvOckbjqpLAR37xI9C5XTvb2EKElqxeHTv6eyTqTVhLXeuyLB9j5ao+VhFo\nIzs4/+a5U5v9gtSjtH7wp+cRtWnsWArGPAn+yF/Xnl5bec2JoRljs3eklbnbbRWy\nqL3Kvz3QRDchHtwCcW093NVd7bGNILI44I8T0wppUxy6hA4aRLgM5imp+avUKxzF\n2Gqlnq97iUOH3a0NuvsL7r0Gzz0gomLx84QHqE9l4fU0sq1AzemUvpkbT0dOlQNE\nyQrB6uQ8VIQyWyDdRvhKzBeYka5UopUJ0FR6jvAI6Su4cO1Eus7eTSvqhNzbi4pE\nrRsM5bsRX73P6XkEhOpL5M9pheywWs9mb3EvuBcOUJ+o70en8RpINd3QJYXHgsBB\nBaAamP010u7z0WToVFOo/Q19BhS0BflqXqHlNEl1Rn1UBgRscBha+AovzAyy9GTJ\nSW/Ul10jZgIk4zoFwVObeVmybixHjSos5e6OPqx+joqc0r+KUTn6jnLtXr7I//PZ\n/mRElhirwMpNtg5bHSNK\n=Zwjz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b394ca0d4a7aa7ceaac229e2eb585effb347aabb\nparent b389b950e1855b9707197234ead11ef71e4edc0d\nauthor xl-openai <xl@openai.com> 1781138036 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781138036 -0700\n\n[codex] Remove redundant plugin app auth state (#27465)\n\n## Summary\n\n- remove the redundant `needsAuth` field from `AppSummary` and generated\napp-server schemas\n- stop `plugin/read` from querying Apps MCP solely to hydrate unused\nconnector auth state\n- preserve `plugin/install.appsNeedingAuth` membership and\n`app/list.isAccessible` as the authentication signals\n\n## Why\n\nCodex App and TUI do not consume `plugin/read.plugin.apps[].needsAuth`.\nHydrating it could establish an Apps MCP connection and discover tools\non a cold `plugin/read` request, adding avoidable latency. The plugin\nAPIs are still marked under development, so removing this wire field is\npreferable to retaining a misleading default.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just write-app-server-schema`\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nplugin_install_uses_remote_apps_needing_auth_response`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nplugin_install_returns_apps_needing_auth`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nplugin_read_returns_plugin_details_with_bundle_contents`\n- `just test -p codex-tui\nplugin_detail_popup_snapshot_shows_install_actions_and_capability_summaries`\n- `$xin-build` simplify and debug reviews","verified_at":"2026-06-11T00:33:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1a9efd473b2cccfc7c82d442d5557be6974db133","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1a9efd473b2cccfc7c82d442d5557be6974db133","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1a9efd473b2cccfc7c82d442d5557be6974db133/comments","author":{"login":"xl-openai","id":184293535,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvwYnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184293535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/xl-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b389b950e1855b9707197234ead11ef71e4edc0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b389b950e1855b9707197234ead11ef71e4edc0d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b389b950e1855b9707197234ead11ef71e4edc0d"}]},{"sha":"b389b950e1855b9707197234ead11ef71e4edc0d","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGIzODliOTUwZTE4NTViOTcwNzE5NzIzNGVhZDExZWY3MWU0ZWRjMGQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jeremy Rose","email":"172423086+nornagon-openai@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-11T00:17:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T00:17:44Z"},"message":"core: cache turn diff rendering (#27489)\n\n## Summary\n\nTurn diff updates repeatedly rendered and serialized the entire\naccumulated diff after every `apply_patch`. The event path also rendered\nonce before updating the tracker solely to test whether a diff existed.\nIn production feedback CODEX-20PW, 2,589 patches across 72 paths\nproduced 401 notifications totaling 441 MB, with the hottest paths\npatched 518 and 495 times.\n\nThis change:\n\n- replaces the pre-update render with a cheap cached-state check\n- caches each rendered file diff by path and content revision, so an\nupdate only invokes Myers for affected paths\n- caches the deterministic aggregate diff so event emission and turn\ncompletion reuse it without recomputation\n- preserves invalidation and net-zero clear notifications\n- applies a 100 ms per-file `similar` timeout; ordinary files complete\nfar below this threshold, while pathological rewrites fall back to a\ncoarse unified hunk that still represents the exact final contents\n\nThe 100 ms deadline bounds synchronous tool-completion latency while\nleaving substantial headroom for normal diffs. The regression test\napplies the fallback diff through the repository's patch parser and\nverifies byte-for-byte final contents.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo test -p codex-core turn_diff_tracker::tests` (14 passed)\n- `cargo test -p codex-core tools::events::tests` (4 passed)\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fmt`\n\nFocused coverage verifies that 42 updates across two files perform 42\nfile renders rather than repeatedly rendering the accumulated set,\nunchanged paths are not re-diffed, clear events remain correct, and a\n48,000-line near-total rewrite returns promptly and applies to the exact\nexpected result. The full `codex-core` suite was not used as the final\ngate because an unrelated existing multi-agent test hit a stack overflow\nwhen run during investigation.\n\n## Bug context\n\n- Sentry feedback: CODEX-20PW\n- Correlation IDs: `019eb2a9-13d2-74e0-b690-27ee224ffb6d`,\n`019e9ad7-09c3-7cb2-b728-ee3acba103ab`","tree":{"sha":"8300b28ed7d945474345319fd7c9c37da557908f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/8300b28ed7d945474345319fd7c9c37da557908f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/b389b950e1855b9707197234ead11ef71e4edc0d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKf6oCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXEkQADguJspTFAqdN63xdJyr8mlo\nLy6PNVq7YMP053qonIsJGMyrzHsPmiL0AgjzNznHzxV2yiiBu086w5KNEvzA3glm\nEV6H+Ad8Hm2n2+gGetlR+ZVnTxlOaSJbiaShSavkcD51hOVMigyHDR2WgwClbkLD\nWiKj0vST1lUqMHWVRe95YAqnkJSfrlRbRgfg80n7N9fbCTlHqkGEDj48f2+Ap1dH\n3w0y3FhD2PWRsjd646UN7nRBy3UzSdtWqJiGw/y56l4/ZzmW14ZL/zUXalkMULu3\nJZnLzqX+0WEiPgWSws4uw89ZEKcXBakmdxlTRyYDD/Mb59t1vro8ZyZ7G6/Jq0Rx\nkai8tnqNG5jMPZvLUzqReNINRGCxpypI5OLe7/xVdhU8ZzRz6KGXu+hXPrqoS8WC\n3fCKWoifguRhsgtJDfCy2Q8TFNgkbPKSlR3E+KncWcXanI+3woOwLKYmjk3VTvAg\nXwYmXgiMkIV1sib3hbFU60cH05quHzlM2oU63v3YCC97S93Cm/B+rdMrYoNg8oKg\n10l6QNxKG43WnlXGDcCd752Uss8FTg6aa9kSzkNJEiCK13ZbMQLfdClH3PSfL/b8\nI7qPqfoc4QjxWvQCjWPD0SSjmh06Zd6HAIDAd0ZptMtAK6o0dKs1mByM6c3dHRqK\nN4CD6P4O+3jW0lzwsKQO\n=AEBT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8300b28ed7d945474345319fd7c9c37da557908f\nparent ac9c534c219d76eb69a730c999920025414296af\nauthor Jeremy Rose <172423086+nornagon-openai@users.noreply.github.com> 1781137064 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781137064 -0700\n\ncore: cache turn diff rendering (#27489)\n\n## Summary\n\nTurn diff updates repeatedly rendered and serialized the entire\naccumulated diff after every `apply_patch`. The event path also rendered\nonce before updating the tracker solely to test whether a diff existed.\nIn production feedback CODEX-20PW, 2,589 patches across 72 paths\nproduced 401 notifications totaling 441 MB, with the hottest paths\npatched 518 and 495 times.\n\nThis change:\n\n- replaces the pre-update render with a cheap cached-state check\n- caches each rendered file diff by path and content revision, so an\nupdate only invokes Myers for affected paths\n- caches the deterministic aggregate diff so event emission and turn\ncompletion reuse it without recomputation\n- preserves invalidation and net-zero clear notifications\n- applies a 100 ms per-file `similar` timeout; ordinary files complete\nfar below this threshold, while pathological rewrites fall back to a\ncoarse unified hunk that still represents the exact final contents\n\nThe 100 ms deadline bounds synchronous tool-completion latency while\nleaving substantial headroom for normal diffs. The regression test\napplies the fallback diff through the repository's patch parser and\nverifies byte-for-byte final contents.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo test -p codex-core turn_diff_tracker::tests` (14 passed)\n- `cargo test -p codex-core tools::events::tests` (4 passed)\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fmt`\n\nFocused coverage verifies that 42 updates across two files perform 42\nfile renders rather than repeatedly rendering the accumulated set,\nunchanged paths are not re-diffed, clear events remain correct, and a\n48,000-line near-total rewrite returns promptly and applies to the exact\nexpected result. The full `codex-core` suite was not used as the final\ngate because an unrelated existing multi-agent test hit a stack overflow\nwhen run during investigation.\n\n## Bug context\n\n- Sentry feedback: CODEX-20PW\n- Correlation IDs: `019eb2a9-13d2-74e0-b690-27ee224ffb6d`,\n`019e9ad7-09c3-7cb2-b728-ee3acba103ab`","verified_at":"2026-06-11T00:17:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b389b950e1855b9707197234ead11ef71e4edc0d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b389b950e1855b9707197234ead11ef71e4edc0d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b389b950e1855b9707197234ead11ef71e4edc0d/comments","author":{"login":"nornagon-openai","id":172423086,"node_id":"U_kgDOCkb3rg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/172423086?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/nornagon-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nornagon-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ac9c534c219d76eb69a730c999920025414296af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ac9c534c219d76eb69a730c999920025414296af","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ac9c534c219d76eb69a730c999920025414296af"}]},{"sha":"ac9c534c219d76eb69a730c999920025414296af","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGFjOWM1MzRjMjE5ZDc2ZWI2OWE3MzBjOTk5OTIwMDI1NDE0Mjk2YWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-11T00:08:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-11T00:08:35Z"},"message":"[codex] Preserve build-script dependencies in rules_rs annotations (#27322)\n\n## Why\n\nBazel compiles Cargo build scripts in the exec configuration. For\n`openssl-sys`, that means the target-specific optional `openssl-src`\ndependency can disappear when producing musl release binaries, even\nthough the build script still needs the vendored source crate.\n\n## What changed\n\nPatch `rules_rs` to expose its existing unconditional\n`build_script_deps` input through `crate.annotation`, then annotate\n`openssl-sys` with the pinned `openssl-src` target. Target-derived build\ndependencies continue to use the existing selected dependency path.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n\nStack: 2 of 6. Follows #27321.","tree":{"sha":"80b55337e9474a4fbd7580fde1cc96b3b148ec08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/80b55337e9474a4fbd7580fde1cc96b3b148ec08"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/ac9c534c219d76eb69a730c999920025414296af","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKfyDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsOwQABOY69WCfv4DRi+ZzNAY9tk6\nlcwL+LxFIcm6E+w/EVdgdKcvz2ebdbezFMgQlGqe2UEfWTGYFVn523haDJM1afuJ\n6e/8oW8Obu9ED5XsapPPfleYLyxH1n+63aufeiW0IbPdt/XdOUEjewhL1A4QSusg\nR2gTQC28tZgDYZz1REq9rduKSQKviKIrFNP/fCAMGJnSAfGjQLA7MJiAIWNtp3ai\nRf4t7hlwglaFgebBqZ5610hDcFpMtadGLfVtDLZU2C9+sLZFqvtvNCV7/MVNiOSU\ngLKrIVZ6htdSm1IguSzzfphoP6AjVgDk8PpGuBYu+i9YVSSyTfroBdAD6KYg+CG4\n05cwBovzegCVg9/L+Vzllve9VKNP1rExvGv/fy74ox4IMCISSwJbb4gwsVUI7d3K\nXNZk1X2SuF+MkKSIV9Ljn09WM22CrqOmtLWgtuIvhiAjJMyAbnWa69KDL3gq4Ba/\nGCVC1i43IFwc3kuuPmOsoNajhwvzI3cYaVQ37i8kY9XCoPWeHNnhCarTmbYOOOzM\nnOaUesFrrifpfcWButoPyozih2+6VIvJlcZCji0dPQgi2VQOJ74ciyEGkoHPR9J0\nzLfqhtME4Bb53kFPYrhlZ3SLWTxM6X5tJ+rhQ7ie0VsFh5xgt4fq65nYbRhC8mdt\n0sCjupvnFIUyL5aVCBXn\n=/+57\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 80b55337e9474a4fbd7580fde1cc96b3b148ec08\nparent b39f943a634a6e7ba86c3d6e8cf6d5f35e612566\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1781136515 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781136515 -0700\n\n[codex] Preserve build-script dependencies in rules_rs annotations (#27322)\n\n## Why\n\nBazel compiles Cargo build scripts in the exec configuration. For\n`openssl-sys`, that means the target-specific optional `openssl-src`\ndependency can disappear when producing musl release binaries, even\nthough the build script still needs the vendored source crate.\n\n## What changed\n\nPatch `rules_rs` to expose its existing unconditional\n`build_script_deps` input through `crate.annotation`, then annotate\n`openssl-sys` with the pinned `openssl-src` target. Target-derived build\ndependencies continue to use the existing selected dependency path.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n\nStack: 2 of 6. Follows #27321.","verified_at":"2026-06-11T00:08:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ac9c534c219d76eb69a730c999920025414296af","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ac9c534c219d76eb69a730c999920025414296af","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ac9c534c219d76eb69a730c999920025414296af/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b39f943a634a6e7ba86c3d6e8cf6d5f35e612566","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b39f943a634a6e7ba86c3d6e8cf6d5f35e612566","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b39f943a634a6e7ba86c3d6e8cf6d5f35e612566"}]},{"sha":"b39f943a634a6e7ba86c3d6e8cf6d5f35e612566","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGIzOWY5NDNhNjM0YTZlN2JhODZjM2Q2ZThjZjZkNWYzNWU2MTI1NjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"marksteinbrick-oai","email":"mark.steinbrick@openai.com","date":"2026-06-10T22:35:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T22:35:41Z"},"message":"[codex-analytics] emit internally started turn events (#27392)\n\n## Why\nCurrently, the analytics reducer omits `codex_turn_event` for internally\nstarted subagent turns\n- It uses `TurnState.connection_id` to select app-server client and\nruntime metadata\n- `turn/start` sets this field for client-started turns, while internal\nsubagent turns bypass that path\n- Spawned child threads inherit the correct connection, but turn\nemission does not use thread state\n\n## What Changed\n- Keeps explicit `TurnState.connection_id` authoritative for\nclient-started turns\n- Falls back to the matching thread’s inherited connection when the turn\nconnection is absent\n- Preserves completeness gates, event schema, and post-emission state\nremoval\n- Extends subagent lifecycle test coverage\n\n## Verification\n- `just test -p codex-analytics` (71 tests passed)\n- `just fix -p codex-analytics`\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"93390834707455f49079265b99874ef5588489e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/93390834707455f49079265b99874ef5588489e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/b39f943a634a6e7ba86c3d6e8cf6d5f35e612566","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKea9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGvUQAENlSXzPVI5a8uzPYWhdaTLh\nqZazdSBFFo7b87rONicl/By2y94AptUbKuwLJN59Fkb0/CZ9qY5o5jc1iFoPMhdA\nzlsXIBI+iM/wdlQIf+Zx0QudPl5zlGswwo5q/Mpbop/cbvFT++VYNku5894M/oiS\nEwtfAsrujTmzzyyrE0HG1bPV1myFjddTjlKafyTSthI39VUxc106G8GNwKbqwAy1\nOvnVlpvwjDXxCatgp0oALcH1CBwikQAXQmlsXFCwoJI640RB/aWLj50iAEqMfkX6\n6sJewjN7wcfqvdgz71fwJPdNR2Wtk31C3BjCbeUPAO5c0uJtKLnLU7TfMe1kdIEu\nNn+YvfoyBRYkvQ0dEGbP4toodz0l3YbIe9TtvR9TGP6N8ojMFuUMd4u8RrNjBF5I\n6zBEt7T/u4nZnSdrT7FN2gpSNRjea+euQdGNdCS24Nj2h2bybbd4AJAOKrQoEORr\ny22OewUJcVLYgFsvoefUIOeCgLEhR2ZaZ6oFINGX5ZMUnJHJpcma6QV/454fLdCG\nkxQAPHDpbPFKA453/TZ4/1MVTlKVMCP6YTCGJBNTzFsI9Fyd2vZm1LtmwKDPh4Jj\neyZ83liiJa3H9aR+nI8aGkRA4blksT+ZNT1IXWPLrQhElBnymLplQ4xEE0+A0wRi\n3cettwhjW79SFEbMhxc1\n=z8Ea\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 93390834707455f49079265b99874ef5588489e1\nparent c72205239f83f5f6162c7464c8e373a81cb62785\nauthor marksteinbrick-oai <mark.steinbrick@openai.com> 1781130941 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781130941 -0700\n\n[codex-analytics] emit internally started turn events (#27392)\n\n## Why\nCurrently, the analytics reducer omits `codex_turn_event` for internally\nstarted subagent turns\n- It uses `TurnState.connection_id` to select app-server client and\nruntime metadata\n- `turn/start` sets this field for client-started turns, while internal\nsubagent turns bypass that path\n- Spawned child threads inherit the correct connection, but turn\nemission does not use thread state\n\n## What Changed\n- Keeps explicit `TurnState.connection_id` authoritative for\nclient-started turns\n- Falls back to the matching thread’s inherited connection when the turn\nconnection is absent\n- Preserves completeness gates, event schema, and post-emission state\nremoval\n- Extends subagent lifecycle test coverage\n\n## Verification\n- `just test -p codex-analytics` (71 tests passed)\n- `just fix -p codex-analytics`\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-10T22:35:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b39f943a634a6e7ba86c3d6e8cf6d5f35e612566","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b39f943a634a6e7ba86c3d6e8cf6d5f35e612566","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b39f943a634a6e7ba86c3d6e8cf6d5f35e612566/comments","author":{"login":"marksteinbrick-oai","id":219906558,"node_id":"U_kgDODRuB_g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219906558?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marksteinbrick-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/marksteinbrick-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marksteinbrick-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marksteinbrick-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marksteinbrick-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marksteinbrick-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marksteinbrick-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marksteinbrick-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marksteinbrick-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marksteinbrick-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marksteinbrick-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c72205239f83f5f6162c7464c8e373a81cb62785","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c72205239f83f5f6162c7464c8e373a81cb62785","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c72205239f83f5f6162c7464c8e373a81cb62785"}]},{"sha":"c72205239f83f5f6162c7464c8e373a81cb62785","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGM3MjIwNTIzOWY4M2Y1ZjYxNjJjNzQ2NGM4ZTM3M2E4MWNiNjI3ODU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Curtis 'Fjord' Hawthorne","email":"fjord@openai.com","date":"2026-06-10T22:27:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T22:27:34Z"},"message":"image: add shared data URL preparation utilities (#27245)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdd shared image-processing primitives needed for centralized image\npreparation in a follow-up PR.\n\n- Add `load_data_url_for_prompt` for decoding and preparing base64 image\ndata URLs.\n- Add configurable maximum-dimension and 32px patch-budget resizing.\n- Enforce a 1 GiB sanity limit on both encoded and decoded data-URL\nrepresentations.\n- Preserve original PNG, JPEG, and WebP bytes when resizing is\nunnecessary.\n- Preserve the existing GIF-to-PNG behavior.\n- Move image utility tests into the existing sidecar test module.\n\n## Behavior\n\nThis PR is intended to be runtime behavior-preserving.\n\nExisting production callers continue using\n`PromptImageMode::ResizeToFit` and `PromptImageMode::Original` with\ntheir existing semantics. The new data-URL entrypoint and configurable\nresize mode have no production callers in this PR; they are used by the\nnext PR in the stack.\n\nThis PR does not change user-input handling, `view_image`, history\ninsertion, request construction, HTTP image URL forwarding, or\napp-server behavior.\n\n\n#### [git stack](https://github.com/magus/git-stack-cli)\n- 👉 `1` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27245\n- ⏳ `2` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27247\n- ⏳ `3` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27246\n- ⏳ `4` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27266","tree":{"sha":"27ee528c53c524faf6c3f5442e669cbc81d161a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/27ee528c53c524faf6c3f5442e669cbc81d161a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c72205239f83f5f6162c7464c8e373a81cb62785","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKeTXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvvUQACiIgntGm0SFiRvRO5qR8vwP\nffQWmyCcaWT6hVr+e+z8Zjbdha/xfdFcppVAIXC7rqT3GZJpkaNYgWd5qaBoyb8i\n86z8HYApBftJfpJ3v4h96e0ay9xdUqotg3m1fcY7ETS0H7PEGu7UYhnSPWoqxoyX\ngfkFcz/UilU2R0zVNBn7Vvp3lsFDxeSb5Iapnf2r03oMN0VtpcVkRUS23FJjKC7A\nsBB3O1H8MLgz2pDzj6ZHtPcXvZBUzMBsXJ/x8GC7Ni86mfDBfDLtElptqra2pAOo\nXK+1T8Upw56B8r5m0zfDMCcukw4nGghfXXE/Pbeo4g6/D2YRWuBPbQT/X5oZnkO0\nVRs7t4K5DU0CHwHqoT0HL77ambwrA1Ru16LLWoRnzJFbD2l9F83Thz12mpOITHWA\nKItbNky9yKBUN8hl60eCAkf4+sq1tu2A8z8J13gpaZN4Oxogb19ZFztWII396SCm\nrPUb7z0+IWXVCCcY0GHxcDnJ7MG62wbdwq9Yvw5cRdrAcGCNXiTXyy5kGphcYe/R\nU4yLthQsUSb4JXWq3cCr9yXCXuF+tGAtHi0H7DrT7Pr0VnNi3ssYIC75F7yxnHkV\n22MOGmbdgPHHs6Es2MoTvAgjE9cA4He4Nu0cG7t34jrrDy2ZaWtgDKImCKcS1Kfk\nTm1GZPACye4IY4VN1C1a\n=YpU6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 27ee528c53c524faf6c3f5442e669cbc81d161a1\nparent 7e5e41daea443bac9df2af36d86a5332efa7b4d7\nauthor Curtis 'Fjord' Hawthorne <fjord@openai.com> 1781130454 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781130454 -0700\n\nimage: add shared data URL preparation utilities (#27245)\n\n## Summary\n\nAdd shared image-processing primitives needed for centralized image\npreparation in a follow-up PR.\n\n- Add `load_data_url_for_prompt` for decoding and preparing base64 image\ndata URLs.\n- Add configurable maximum-dimension and 32px patch-budget resizing.\n- Enforce a 1 GiB sanity limit on both encoded and decoded data-URL\nrepresentations.\n- Preserve original PNG, JPEG, and WebP bytes when resizing is\nunnecessary.\n- Preserve the existing GIF-to-PNG behavior.\n- Move image utility tests into the existing sidecar test module.\n\n## Behavior\n\nThis PR is intended to be runtime behavior-preserving.\n\nExisting production callers continue using\n`PromptImageMode::ResizeToFit` and `PromptImageMode::Original` with\ntheir existing semantics. The new data-URL entrypoint and configurable\nresize mode have no production callers in this PR; they are used by the\nnext PR in the stack.\n\nThis PR does not change user-input handling, `view_image`, history\ninsertion, request construction, HTTP image URL forwarding, or\napp-server behavior.\n\n\n#### [git stack](https://github.com/magus/git-stack-cli)\n- 👉 `1` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27245\n- ⏳ `2` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27247\n- ⏳ `3` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27246\n- ⏳ `4` https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27266","verified_at":"2026-06-10T22:27:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c72205239f83f5f6162c7464c8e373a81cb62785","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c72205239f83f5f6162c7464c8e373a81cb62785","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c72205239f83f5f6162c7464c8e373a81cb62785/comments","author":{"login":"fjord-oai","id":240979671,"node_id":"U_kgDODl0O1w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240979671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/fjord-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fjord-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7e5e41daea443bac9df2af36d86a5332efa7b4d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7e5e41daea443bac9df2af36d86a5332efa7b4d7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7e5e41daea443bac9df2af36d86a5332efa7b4d7"}]},{"sha":"7e5e41daea443bac9df2af36d86a5332efa7b4d7","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDdlNWU0MWRhZWE0NDNiYWM5ZGYyYWYzNmQ4NmE1MzMyZWZhN2I0ZDc","commit":{"author":{"name":"richardopenai","email":"richardlee@openai.com","date":"2026-06-10T21:36:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T21:36:38Z"},"message":"[codex] Add reusable OTEL gauge instruments (#27057)\n\n## Why\n\nExec-server observability needs current-value measurements in addition\nto counters. The reusable OTEL client should expose that primitive\nwithout coupling it to exec-server runtime behavior.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Adds integer gauge instruments, with optional descriptions.\n- Caches gauges by name and description so instrument metadata remains\npart of the declaration identity.\n- Covers gauge values, descriptions, merged attributes, and OTLP HTTP\nexport.\n\nThis PR only adds the gauge primitive. It does not add second-based\nduration histograms or exec-server adoption.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. #26091: counter descriptions\n2. **#27057: gauge instruments**\n3. #27058: second-based duration histograms\n\nRelated independent coverage: #27059 tests OTLP HTTP log and trace event\nexport.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-otel`\n- `just fix -p codex-otel`\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"56a4535ddc3d82af61d23b3bca6b108b204c49d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/56a4535ddc3d82af61d23b3bca6b108b204c49d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/7e5e41daea443bac9df2af36d86a5332efa7b4d7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKdjmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnX0QAK38jpFqZ22GoHxK7H1JRzBb\nhTaVZc9WM6jpGtjatjOrwm4gB7A5Wjey0IZfCgkUsESCbednlI/jybTaMVK6b022\n8dJPIkc/dzu704iwHZNsXO7hycCD7OQlmGBlIAEdHlkiF7ZT4k2bFJy1hmU1eXV/\ndLydhS00KfEoR0Ahto9O/iSUjgSV8u6jN9neO/Z9Udf2XSofzVZwp4wvoMfzTefd\nXf8gkSjWuE57DjTOud9lGk9YiXK6zTyAzrJdEpYIrfhf26OmGs6et1t6muBefzgo\nmOlCqY5iiGn7pIbUfGZwxFT0oE3FcChVhsNcrUUezFB42bW/rkIS6JJvRQTehM/M\n83lkiM+6tUapotE4mDdLQvgbdVbWRL3NTdJo/6CdEuCbMAEHUVo0ASTJDrOOWb8v\n9oODrVqxPuR99x/Ld2corBx6GALKN7yokfUF07EhwYvKrDnCsSkwGqySXxLL/n3H\nhsaWeXO9BXaB+REJbzk4fG3LBI9yR/HQRK1qOBOjTIqQ5TsarhvnT4RESrXTKu/0\nED1hVqhOkDGjMOnQquatpHeYiD8doGc5F7oGrR0UUFTjOXevGDDAxGYEB7jFQwzs\nmsXzkmWj6LxUYN9LR6dSsvD0Gf/U1VfoS3EiedipyJz/hC9c5JhGzh6ptSESpKZR\n8iqa5i04NlUGYLUdpYUC\n=zUyT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 56a4535ddc3d82af61d23b3bca6b108b204c49d2\nparent 22dd6ebc7d3abe50d8aa40be3025eccd9c166418\nauthor richardopenai <richardlee@openai.com> 1781127398 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781127398 +0000\n\n[codex] Add reusable OTEL gauge instruments (#27057)\n\n## Why\n\nExec-server observability needs current-value measurements in addition\nto counters. The reusable OTEL client should expose that primitive\nwithout coupling it to exec-server runtime behavior.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Adds integer gauge instruments, with optional descriptions.\n- Caches gauges by name and description so instrument metadata remains\npart of the declaration identity.\n- Covers gauge values, descriptions, merged attributes, and OTLP HTTP\nexport.\n\nThis PR only adds the gauge primitive. It does not add second-based\nduration histograms or exec-server adoption.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. #26091: counter descriptions\n2. **#27057: gauge instruments**\n3. #27058: second-based duration histograms\n\nRelated independent coverage: #27059 tests OTLP HTTP log and trace event\nexport.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-otel`\n- `just fix -p codex-otel`\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-10T21:36:39Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7e5e41daea443bac9df2af36d86a5332efa7b4d7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7e5e41daea443bac9df2af36d86a5332efa7b4d7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7e5e41daea443bac9df2af36d86a5332efa7b4d7/comments","author":{"login":"richardopenai","id":272641442,"node_id":"U_kgDOEEAtog","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272641442?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai","html_url":"https://github.com/richardopenai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"22dd6ebc7d3abe50d8aa40be3025eccd9c166418","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/22dd6ebc7d3abe50d8aa40be3025eccd9c166418","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/22dd6ebc7d3abe50d8aa40be3025eccd9c166418"}]},{"sha":"22dd6ebc7d3abe50d8aa40be3025eccd9c166418","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDIyZGQ2ZWJjN2QzYWJlNTBkOGFhNDBiZTMwMjVlY2NkOWMxNjY0MTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"guinness-oai","email":"guinness@openai.com","date":"2026-06-10T21:32:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T21:32:29Z"},"message":"Forward standalone assistant output to realtime (#27319)\n\n## Why\n\nWhen a realtime session is open without an active frontend-model\nhandoff, completed Codex assistant messages are currently dropped. That\nprevents the frontend model from hearing orchestrator preambles and\nfinal responses produced by typed turns or other non-handoff work, which\nmakes the two models present as disconnected personas.\n\nActive handoffs already forward each completed assistant message,\nincluding preambles. This change leaves those V1 and V2 paths intact and\nfills only the no-active-handoff gap.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Send standalone V1 assistant messages through\n`conversation.handoff.append` with a stable synthetic handoff ID\n- Send standalone V2 assistant messages as normal `[BACKEND]`\n`conversation.item.create` message items, then enqueue `response.create`\nso the frontend model responds\n- Preserve the existing active V1 and V2 transport and completion\nbehavior\n- Continue excluding user messages from realtime mirroring\n- Skip empty output and cap each complete context injection, including\nits V2 prefix, at 1,000 tokens\n- Add end-to-end coverage for both wire formats, V2 response creation,\npreambles, final responses, and truncation\n\n## Test plan\n\n- CI","tree":{"sha":"05a8a50cb04be4501228f33ba9a3733155ebfdbb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/05a8a50cb04be4501228f33ba9a3733155ebfdbb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/22dd6ebc7d3abe50d8aa40be3025eccd9c166418","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKdftCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEPQQACePnM7yEe34IcwKw15d5bTv\nPTCyqap6yecmFZQhM+It0mPCQtXcYVLNmiriw9TfOmCXlo3LgNsBjRaWqJbOcDuj\nebE/2Ebw5pc8BMU8LkloA2okIrGxCUXL40L/K1oSxbO597vkbnmV/1/mZkhtiyPN\nmAA0FQej04S/WwBkswwh0wdYVOPFKJJsuw4DYBKaRW9lMEzaUZbHylnmcEH8ytO/\nOq7iutIJvKQZhqbR3R8GZMuQJLXRpKOH4ws+e/03/exoZu5Z8/Z0fgvCbM9pvKsr\nAjlgZrh94CYzB0xDwM+F0zbW9Gi21HpcLRYsF8i4auxbQ3+xlzvoIexu1MfX8kax\n4zW27NNeL/zR1Mkk0b0k4tLekFJQwwsgga8lfRGp0eWMJ7IaFo1OvnZdHllkyHjH\nFKKO/Q/Dzfswodz6UYKjv7EnWHyzapV8vIUsQPwt28PSWXunGk0SE+v2pjxQGRDs\n+Mg4+mTfx4Tg1OAkOgrVERjU7zhQDdcTu3yIYxf/B7fFUERkrjd7IJCAEAmiSVm7\nzkz8Vs0hgmEZ7M0ebR/eOl9v/vXCGq7pM1qmjBlj1bcWPYdORq3WSQjmF2stEuae\njx+jnGNDnaSI0ZoP9Pabbqa8AbOLPDtk8vM5OHSpQeDXUq58a4JQdLMbcZqOXRpi\nuGXEp+tgNSgCWHK2eulf\n=Nle5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 05a8a50cb04be4501228f33ba9a3733155ebfdbb\nparent 387adc6c4bc484aefb658a6006ad0a26fc45c79b\nauthor guinness-oai <guinness@openai.com> 1781127149 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781127149 +0000\n\nForward standalone assistant output to realtime (#27319)\n\n## Why\n\nWhen a realtime session is open without an active frontend-model\nhandoff, completed Codex assistant messages are currently dropped. That\nprevents the frontend model from hearing orchestrator preambles and\nfinal responses produced by typed turns or other non-handoff work, which\nmakes the two models present as disconnected personas.\n\nActive handoffs already forward each completed assistant message,\nincluding preambles. This change leaves those V1 and V2 paths intact and\nfills only the no-active-handoff gap.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Send standalone V1 assistant messages through\n`conversation.handoff.append` with a stable synthetic handoff ID\n- Send standalone V2 assistant messages as normal `[BACKEND]`\n`conversation.item.create` message items, then enqueue `response.create`\nso the frontend model responds\n- Preserve the existing active V1 and V2 transport and completion\nbehavior\n- Continue excluding user messages from realtime mirroring\n- Skip empty output and cap each complete context injection, including\nits V2 prefix, at 1,000 tokens\n- Add end-to-end coverage for both wire formats, V2 response creation,\npreambles, final responses, and truncation\n\n## Test plan\n\n- CI","verified_at":"2026-06-10T21:32:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/22dd6ebc7d3abe50d8aa40be3025eccd9c166418","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/22dd6ebc7d3abe50d8aa40be3025eccd9c166418","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/22dd6ebc7d3abe50d8aa40be3025eccd9c166418/comments","author":{"login":"guinness-oai","id":254771997,"node_id":"U_kgDODy-DHQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/254771997?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/guinness-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guinness-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"387adc6c4bc484aefb658a6006ad0a26fc45c79b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/387adc6c4bc484aefb658a6006ad0a26fc45c79b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/387adc6c4bc484aefb658a6006ad0a26fc45c79b"}]},{"sha":"387adc6c4bc484aefb658a6006ad0a26fc45c79b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDM4N2FkYzZjNGJjNDg0YWVmYjY1OGE2MDA2YWQwYTI2ZmM0NWM3OWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Tamir Duberstein","email":"tamird@openai.com","date":"2026-06-10T20:15:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T20:15:43Z"},"message":"[codex] reuse release artifacts for npm staging (#27312)\n\nThe release job already downloads every workflow artifact into `dist`,\nbut npm staging creates a new cache and downloads the six target\nartifacts again.\n\nReuse `dist` as the staging script's artifact cache while preserving the\nexisting download fallback for missing artifacts and standalone callers.\nThe script retains ownership of temporary caches but does not delete a\ncaller-provided directory.\n\nIn https://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/27242495616, the\nduplicate\ndownload transferred 3.3 GiB and took 4 minutes 13 seconds. This should\nreduce total release time by about 4 minutes.","tree":{"sha":"0f62f4a040bf3aa6cd5f0cfcc12e3b0939df053d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/0f62f4a040bf3aa6cd5f0cfcc12e3b0939df053d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/387adc6c4bc484aefb658a6006ad0a26fc45c79b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKcXvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3tIQALBUKreUw8E1/8o2gRjNahSa\nHbaCf8XBFQmT7L23VcpqWQWWz5IKrATbiZ0riUPmx9uf3CHn9S2qnE/T9A0z4ls8\n6XHP/Xr7+D7KUXJMEVdJXYkNIiMx3OzWtcxwBlBDGreFXu8rvyH1PvxWIsEpTaLI\ns7195E7hgBXR1s/JQmT1fH6AFV0zMeen8omsjIcxiKVeZ123DjpuzzZXkuSc3sTd\n0GakJRbsRPF6YKjw5JNesiSdVmKGQjT7i6+yW0BYT+i/gHsMInDU8TKdO93HGJlb\nPOVx2t8m02b2RV9Hx6ca41fNW4EzwUEjSgl3+HHqXTC8me1h/Okb/s0PKaEdza/J\nmjzE9lmSBLucy9C9htWKEgSnQrgc6UrOX/mdBZeq/Ift1zGol9KpKU25OMAeXhhu\neRM7ZUYmCP4Wx4OXXgL0AYJHZMomMYXG7hTWzHIsioNEgo7B2zdYcgrA9z0fqomo\nn9LWa6aCI02BAYQm1gtcyqMp5iLkXGYusKTLjA+/hhChsD2eq9nWZvK9PLpJCOtF\nuwnNvuQKHO/j01Sc8xIuX324YTnSKkJGNm+Cj1XCE3aHLngcI3PtOl9j+BLMhfNf\n3dSDXgpp/Pa6bVXyZh5muwdotcIakIFPbIy6JuGD8Pw8AXfAXyc3x4Ymvx0uvxPt\nAisJ8TJzMSubNXA/ep9X\n=SocN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0f62f4a040bf3aa6cd5f0cfcc12e3b0939df053d\nparent 980f60b6641c5907c16db3c39f36ac113e15c93d\nauthor Tamir Duberstein <tamird@openai.com> 1781122543 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781122543 -0700\n\n[codex] reuse release artifacts for npm staging (#27312)\n\nThe release job already downloads every workflow artifact into `dist`,\nbut npm staging creates a new cache and downloads the six target\nartifacts again.\n\nReuse `dist` as the staging script's artifact cache while preserving the\nexisting download fallback for missing artifacts and standalone callers.\nThe script retains ownership of temporary caches but does not delete a\ncaller-provided directory.\n\nIn https://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/27242495616, the\nduplicate\ndownload transferred 3.3 GiB and took 4 minutes 13 seconds. This should\nreduce total release time by about 4 minutes.","verified_at":"2026-06-10T20:15:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/387adc6c4bc484aefb658a6006ad0a26fc45c79b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/387adc6c4bc484aefb658a6006ad0a26fc45c79b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/387adc6c4bc484aefb658a6006ad0a26fc45c79b/comments","author":{"login":"tamird","id":1535036,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MzUwMzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1535036?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird","html_url":"https://github.com/tamird","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tamird/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"980f60b6641c5907c16db3c39f36ac113e15c93d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/980f60b6641c5907c16db3c39f36ac113e15c93d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/980f60b6641c5907c16db3c39f36ac113e15c93d"}]},{"sha":"980f60b6641c5907c16db3c39f36ac113e15c93d","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDk4MGY2MGI2NjQxYzU5MDdjMTZkYjNjMzlmMzZhYzExM2UxNWM5M2Q","commit":{"author":{"name":"e-provencher","email":"eprovencher@openai.com","date":"2026-06-10T20:11:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T20:11:20Z"},"message":"[codex] Preserve disabled MCP servers across runtime overlays (#27414)\n\n## Why\n\nRecent MCP runtime overlay changes replace same-name configured server\nentries with compatibility or extension-provided configs. Those\nreplacement configs default to enabled, so an MCP server explicitly\nconfigured with `enabled = false` could be initialized anyway.\n\nThe connection manager still filters disabled servers correctly, but the\nconfigured disabled state was lost before initialization reached that\nfilter.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Remember MCP servers that are disabled in the configured view before\napplying runtime fallbacks and extension overlays.\n- Restore `enabled = false` for those servers after overlays, while\nleaving all other overlay fields and `Remove` precedence unchanged.\n- Add focused extension-backed regression coverage for a disabled\n`codex_apps` server.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-mcp-extension`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fix -p codex-mcp-extension`\n\nThe full workspace `just test` suite was not run.","tree":{"sha":"1d6f9b5fee6a2848e7c69201a76037adeb0a9f2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/1d6f9b5fee6a2848e7c69201a76037adeb0a9f2c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/980f60b6641c5907c16db3c39f36ac113e15c93d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKcToCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAApkEQAH+ZqSdgemzYuclREW8obxzo\nNmv8hdlDmm9QW3vnvKXIT7BXjZXdD5gQN17/nJ676vH5zhPnWZx188qAtOP3I+0c\nphJ4xcxMYyyW2I+gLKStY2MYlJQpFqt1xANw0ZamRuaxX2DxaSWt4OqyspB/l/Vx\nqLovHMd6DpxaFK/aUU/JCAqLHR72oPdxZd9zEuxSCpItz/tvZ84HS2WxI8XNRGg6\ncIYIYgwnm1pe1OO3X5Nl1rRFlsDJdzO9NbjppZUQ8CUdYxsdxDtA1+sUgxW5xefE\n+LyU+VCouWxlbjdmIvDsjiN3UHO9ouOo/4xCudGb+UGuZdCI4zOkhJb7RhuvsiNV\nKamqUQ0EEaiELV08aYejfMJjPKapFlGU6ptmp4g6YbyWH/n47soZ6HlSQf0ryeKW\n7BIdR+x1diuMeINxiDS/M2ZhuT5a53NqQVu/WUCDTRTMBsmUgMazMdlwdG23IFdp\nqMWUdyIy9caie04U0detQjL/GQqh7M/pglytB+Fb6dPbJEkOjAaqVvlIVhxsBkwB\n4dHpHDPiTe+C81hVj6n9NSmTwvk8HHc6szOdv4nLBdcQ0+OjbmBeG2c/o9Q4hEOR\n+IXuRPznGjsBdN0aFOnGLkrzrB38xW7uNsoKsGhIiH0Le5UeEgqjYmjUSnvTJ7MS\nhHmeliu8WtfDtR3c4ssg\n=D9Ys\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1d6f9b5fee6a2848e7c69201a76037adeb0a9f2c\nparent 7011044c1c0f51185eee007b45f0f42140fa794c\nauthor e-provencher <eprovencher@openai.com> 1781122280 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781122280 -0400\n\n[codex] Preserve disabled MCP servers across runtime overlays (#27414)\n\n## Why\n\nRecent MCP runtime overlay changes replace same-name configured server\nentries with compatibility or extension-provided configs. Those\nreplacement configs default to enabled, so an MCP server explicitly\nconfigured with `enabled = false` could be initialized anyway.\n\nThe connection manager still filters disabled servers correctly, but the\nconfigured disabled state was lost before initialization reached that\nfilter.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Remember MCP servers that are disabled in the configured view before\napplying runtime fallbacks and extension overlays.\n- Restore `enabled = false` for those servers after overlays, while\nleaving all other overlay fields and `Remove` precedence unchanged.\n- Add focused extension-backed regression coverage for a disabled\n`codex_apps` server.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-mcp-extension`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fix -p codex-mcp-extension`\n\nThe full workspace `just test` suite was not run.","verified_at":"2026-06-10T20:11:21Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/980f60b6641c5907c16db3c39f36ac113e15c93d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/980f60b6641c5907c16db3c39f36ac113e15c93d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/980f60b6641c5907c16db3c39f36ac113e15c93d/comments","author":{"login":"provencher-oai","id":288160983,"node_id":"U_kgDOESz81w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/288160983?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/provencher-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/provencher-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/provencher-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/provencher-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/provencher-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/provencher-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/provencher-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/provencher-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/provencher-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/provencher-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/provencher-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7011044c1c0f51185eee007b45f0f42140fa794c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7011044c1c0f51185eee007b45f0f42140fa794c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7011044c1c0f51185eee007b45f0f42140fa794c"}]},{"sha":"7011044c1c0f51185eee007b45f0f42140fa794c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDcwMTEwNDRjMWMwZjUxMTg1ZWVlMDA3YjQ1ZjBmNDIxNDBmYTc5NGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"xl-openai","email":"xl@openai.com","date":"2026-06-10T20:11:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T20:11:09Z"},"message":"[codex] Skip local curated discovery for remote plugins (#27311)\n\n## Summary\n\n- skip the local `openai-curated` marketplace before marketplace loading\nwhen tool-suggest discovery uses remote plugins\n- preserve existing marketplace listing behavior for all other callers\nand when remote plugins are disabled\n- add regression coverage proving the curated marketplace is excluded\nbefore its malformed manifest can be read\n\n## Why\n\nTool-suggest discovery previously loaded every local `openai-curated`\nplugin manifest and only discarded that marketplace afterward when\nremote plugins were enabled. The remote catalog is used in that mode, so\nthe local scan consumed CPU without contributing discoverable plugins.\n\n## Impact\n\nRemote-plugin tool suggestion discovery no longer reads the local\ncurated marketplace and its plugin manifests. `openai-bundled`,\nconfigured marketplaces, normal `plugin/list` behavior, and local\ncurated discovery when remote plugins are disabled are unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins\nlist_marketplaces_can_skip_openai_curated_before_loading`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nlist_tool_suggest_discoverable_plugins_omits_openai_curated_when_remote_enabled`\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`","tree":{"sha":"c32def629b58684984e199bacebf5cc4034c4190","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c32def629b58684984e199bacebf5cc4034c4190"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/7011044c1c0f51185eee007b45f0f42140fa794c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKcTdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALF8QAAOmCZ9fdC1NUiDKsVEdD36w\niMnUT/7zFt70EeP+J+QIYgiSkIqfIGEMYgU62+VQcxRU+A/wHZaqIPXE/lc9YHBJ\nnPMOTpuU6tdZDulIY+A063NPqyAsksndUdnoufkFoM5hcwDrJEWWSWzPpPSWHw+0\n69NPhrYE17HKO4UG8/L39dDC9cvb6fpf/W6UVK3uUORlgrPmhOZIHku9P51+Gc0M\nCqexqvgEh2oSeOypHoRUZnyiUpWAKxZvi08mUu1DoDY10lpQn2e2yClXv0gY8WsJ\nnL8teKFkCLaKVIMAArwWIKVyid/S+uTZuZf2B0w5AO8SC7AZVWZe7DS+dblq1Z++\nbbpy6y3S4hlIF267NfZodXikorvIPvVen7BTwHFntFDskNSicSVZGW5mg6QCaWVx\nZp7n3Yc6aWedsh0uR3Ta49RDIgGTrbB/FZYVKZYtIKhaFvmICNHqCP2qd1jsgSnJ\nHPnXEjfsnbgwNkq0PZoBpo5CWq+xfutl2CdtKKLK8b2yuHHPkzi5xdSjRUnY7V2n\nB29zFEccKFPBeuwSYbXLUNvYj/voO4QyNI1/TY8TOrcfIKLgoLDohnVgampUy+Us\n0iTsaOuTrRBtjUD0zFd/GZLUrQTSocpbaxfoRCdKBsX8dtx/C+ITva6v1+EZoQgQ\nNPBWPz8TdejwxqavDPoa\n=9rY/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c32def629b58684984e199bacebf5cc4034c4190\nparent b4445f275838981bfd22429c5c41f2c5be0bde7a\nauthor xl-openai <xl@openai.com> 1781122269 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781122269 -0700\n\n[codex] Skip local curated discovery for remote plugins (#27311)\n\n## Summary\n\n- skip the local `openai-curated` marketplace before marketplace loading\nwhen tool-suggest discovery uses remote plugins\n- preserve existing marketplace listing behavior for all other callers\nand when remote plugins are disabled\n- add regression coverage proving the curated marketplace is excluded\nbefore its malformed manifest can be read\n\n## Why\n\nTool-suggest discovery previously loaded every local `openai-curated`\nplugin manifest and only discarded that marketplace afterward when\nremote plugins were enabled. The remote catalog is used in that mode, so\nthe local scan consumed CPU without contributing discoverable plugins.\n\n## Impact\n\nRemote-plugin tool suggestion discovery no longer reads the local\ncurated marketplace and its plugin manifests. `openai-bundled`,\nconfigured marketplaces, normal `plugin/list` behavior, and local\ncurated discovery when remote plugins are disabled are unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins\nlist_marketplaces_can_skip_openai_curated_before_loading`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nlist_tool_suggest_discoverable_plugins_omits_openai_curated_when_remote_enabled`\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`","verified_at":"2026-06-10T20:11:09Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7011044c1c0f51185eee007b45f0f42140fa794c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7011044c1c0f51185eee007b45f0f42140fa794c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7011044c1c0f51185eee007b45f0f42140fa794c/comments","author":{"login":"xl-openai","id":184293535,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvwYnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184293535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/xl-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b4445f275838981bfd22429c5c41f2c5be0bde7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b4445f275838981bfd22429c5c41f2c5be0bde7a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b4445f275838981bfd22429c5c41f2c5be0bde7a"}]},{"sha":"b4445f275838981bfd22429c5c41f2c5be0bde7a","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGI0NDQ1ZjI3NTgzODk4MWJmZDIyNDI5YzVjNDFmMmM1YmUwYmRlN2E","commit":{"author":{"name":"stefanstokic-oai","email":"stefanstokic@openai.com","date":"2026-06-10T19:53:15Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T19:53:15Z"},"message":"[codex] add /import for external agents (#27071)\n\n## Why\n\nExternal-agent import should be discoverable and deliberate without\nblocking startup or claiming the public `codex [PROMPT]` CLI namespace.\nThe slash command keeps the flow local to the interactive TUI and reuses\nthe existing app-server import API.\n\n## What changed\n\n- add the user-facing `/import` slash command\n- detect external-agent importable items only when the command is\ninvoked\n- run imports through the embedded local app-server\n- show start and completion messages, refresh configuration, and block\nduplicate imports while one is pending\n- reject the flow for unsupported remote and local-daemon sessions\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-tui external_agent_config_migration` (10 passed)\n- manually exercised an isolated TUI fixture with existing\nexternal-agent setup and session data using a fresh `CODEX_HOME`\n- verified picker customization, plugin and session detection, import\ncompletion, repeated invocation, and imported-session resume context\n- the broader `just test -p codex-tui` run passed 2,805 tests, with 2\nunrelated guardian feature-flag failures and 4 skipped tests\n\n## Draft follow-ups\n\n- review whether completion messaging should remain attached to the\ninitiating chat if the user switches chats during an import\n- review shutdown semantics for an in-progress background import\n\n## Stack\n\n1. [#27064](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27064): remove the\nstartup migration flow\n2. [#27065](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27065): extract the\npicker renderer\n3. [#27070](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27070): add the\nexternal-agent import picker UX\n4. [#27071](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27071): expose the flow\nthrough `/import`\n\n**This PR is stack item 4.** Draft while the lower stack dependencies\nare reviewed.","tree":{"sha":"08e210df7daa58a9033e7ff6b7105b57237f7929","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/08e210df7daa58a9033e7ff6b7105b57237f7929"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/b4445f275838981bfd22429c5c41f2c5be0bde7a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKcCrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYIwQAAWTuK/FsmLUQukG5z2hDhB3\ng9KSz4NmCxKulaYXp+/sFUdUIIHi4gvlP4PDIc6igO+hJl1c2KtJ0UAwom5Oj2DH\ncLXuGiAClrb8CN/Rnv8utDYndJX/qH5jyBD5n9SR+EiUiLCJVSTQ/I8L5gMO0W2I\n7YYT8ta2zfZU0w5ZnRZqa0Ol5nkqUZ6bSxyGDRktGNAjUvgJ6TnX73Xq4gN0cTtW\nc9JVuK5/13/m5KGjSOWcxpGDpsZsUHv16gb2CUaLJDvI32psVimRoH/n2jO5PAVW\n8R7cyAFUQFf8LP5U76iHKYT6Q4wtMpna9Mjb5sqxyxigVzYtRenQpJWRb9vcGlfM\nGc6EbDg2fRYV3/j2bqRRR041c4Xe6EcfqYxE/EgLfRE/0B8U8TilecZlW60TkvZh\nqLQ6zoTVu95GrG1nHXCVRKWTWvbp1Rxqd8ivRRUBwLjzkZeEYgwdXiKxkYhwDEqE\ndmW3CGTieAVolz3E7keeK57kXTd4PUQGrDqb3mazwtfmmmzSoTgTX54suRiemRJT\naz5OqAkOPZ2OrZAJIZw/X71w6oJh67s1EROMjShNeIfE2iNt+xJFDENLiv9dWgMS\nM39mup+6BWE/XDIhWOF4ugnh4foxegObwqHOiNDNTwcaOl/sYVIUmUjneIuF+2b4\n8So+z3jkeSyrCZA4LLEx\n=GM3s\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 08e210df7daa58a9033e7ff6b7105b57237f7929\nparent 1deae7bd4a1212f94ec5b877fc4c9d7edea644f1\nauthor stefanstokic-oai <stefanstokic@openai.com> 1781121195 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781121195 -0400\n\n[codex] add /import for external agents (#27071)\n\n## Why\n\nExternal-agent import should be discoverable and deliberate without\nblocking startup or claiming the public `codex [PROMPT]` CLI namespace.\nThe slash command keeps the flow local to the interactive TUI and reuses\nthe existing app-server import API.\n\n## What changed\n\n- add the user-facing `/import` slash command\n- detect external-agent importable items only when the command is\ninvoked\n- run imports through the embedded local app-server\n- show start and completion messages, refresh configuration, and block\nduplicate imports while one is pending\n- reject the flow for unsupported remote and local-daemon sessions\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-tui external_agent_config_migration` (10 passed)\n- manually exercised an isolated TUI fixture with existing\nexternal-agent setup and session data using a fresh `CODEX_HOME`\n- verified picker customization, plugin and session detection, import\ncompletion, repeated invocation, and imported-session resume context\n- the broader `just test -p codex-tui` run passed 2,805 tests, with 2\nunrelated guardian feature-flag failures and 4 skipped tests\n\n## Draft follow-ups\n\n- review whether completion messaging should remain attached to the\ninitiating chat if the user switches chats during an import\n- review shutdown semantics for an in-progress background import\n\n## Stack\n\n1. [#27064](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27064): remove the\nstartup migration flow\n2. [#27065](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27065): extract the\npicker renderer\n3. [#27070](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27070): add the\nexternal-agent import picker UX\n4. [#27071](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27071): expose the flow\nthrough `/import`\n\n**This PR is stack item 4.** Draft while the lower stack dependencies\nare reviewed.","verified_at":"2026-06-10T19:53:16Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b4445f275838981bfd22429c5c41f2c5be0bde7a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b4445f275838981bfd22429c5c41f2c5be0bde7a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b4445f275838981bfd22429c5c41f2c5be0bde7a/comments","author":{"login":"stefanstokic-oai","id":278208182,"node_id":"U_kgDOEJUetg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/278208182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/stefanstokic-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1deae7bd4a1212f94ec5b877fc4c9d7edea644f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1deae7bd4a1212f94ec5b877fc4c9d7edea644f1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1deae7bd4a1212f94ec5b877fc4c9d7edea644f1"}]},{"sha":"1deae7bd4a1212f94ec5b877fc4c9d7edea644f1","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDFkZWFlN2JkNGExMjEyZjk0ZWM1Yjg3N2ZjNGM5ZDdlZGVhNjQ0ZjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-10T19:45:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T19:45:29Z"},"message":"[codex] Move release platform rules into bazel package (#27321)\n\n## Intent\n\nKeep release-specific Bazel helpers out of the shared Rust crate\ndefinitions and colocate them with Bazel platform configuration.\n\n## Implementation\n\nMoves `multiplatform_binaries` and its platform list from `defs.bzl`\ninto `bazel/platforms/release_binaries.bzl` and updates the CLI load\nsite. Behavior is unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `bazel query //codex-rs/cli:release_binaries`\n\nStack: 1 of 6.","tree":{"sha":"6aa98c11699c8cb44a4aa79c98f96232e69a6cf4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6aa98c11699c8cb44a4aa79c98f96232e69a6cf4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/1deae7bd4a1212f94ec5b877fc4c9d7edea644f1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKb7ZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAt4IQAFChS52cwzhYlNZji5WWQ4Kh\nWXna7sEA8Y4JNqk0Eho+gy3S8HOwkTcWKU6W7Ov/h5vwSkb1EG3Q5AGafQokAH4v\n6leINvc8WAEUbvv2pVNPUEYBA4QnD/BegY0UnNm/oJytUAWFAJyJCu0Tev2BjeuJ\nuQzaP+jJfHxPAgG1C32mS295gxcxmh1PiEvzJsv6eZhHKhemM9CjgdHdzZWgikMS\nAEk+Bh9mzQ5pH2rwjeqcLvwsq+cTy6hhB6XgBAibsRi+3VStrzBJVNiHUCT2+Vmx\nh8mAm7LvYfzgt2AT4VDV6NHhb1FRMYOu2h2I4E5TKOLJOB3OKd8hd7lj851ul9bF\nqIHsxpCuUvn4hgKGkwLscVj065zpE99eu3NhQkr4biMoSmOlsTXq/fqZkhkcyKCy\nTojZJHGCdfUWYDJzllyWIqhSjtkE35fnJ6SxzQrHitD45vYeCZWsuODcVQ+f+ls/\njWp2O5b0ioktDzdCkv6VrOg5aIHiZZmiuzfgWo9e2O0EZZv8/kPzGw19q59fIj1l\nBYCehledypEwo5s5rMfpFxNgnN1p+abTc9bL48M0dZJcOMNATsRar3tZRvUFn6Vb\nDIfV7tX7GFetPl61IT/nPs9m14Q7cE2LrlFsRQhucnnruPBmo/2YytOexkna9lLs\ngl2XoowAMXtyam6Bl1jc\n=814Q\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6aa98c11699c8cb44a4aa79c98f96232e69a6cf4\nparent e3528434cdfb9b822057095c7edbf4c99363f709\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1781120729 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781120729 +0000\n\n[codex] Move release platform rules into bazel package (#27321)\n\n## Intent\n\nKeep release-specific Bazel helpers out of the shared Rust crate\ndefinitions and colocate them with Bazel platform configuration.\n\n## Implementation\n\nMoves `multiplatform_binaries` and its platform list from `defs.bzl`\ninto `bazel/platforms/release_binaries.bzl` and updates the CLI load\nsite. Behavior is unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `bazel query //codex-rs/cli:release_binaries`\n\nStack: 1 of 6.","verified_at":"2026-06-10T19:45:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1deae7bd4a1212f94ec5b877fc4c9d7edea644f1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1deae7bd4a1212f94ec5b877fc4c9d7edea644f1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1deae7bd4a1212f94ec5b877fc4c9d7edea644f1/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e3528434cdfb9b822057095c7edbf4c99363f709","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e3528434cdfb9b822057095c7edbf4c99363f709","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e3528434cdfb9b822057095c7edbf4c99363f709"}]},{"sha":"e3528434cdfb9b822057095c7edbf4c99363f709","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGUzNTI4NDM0Y2RmYjliODIyMDU3MDk1YzdlZGJmNGM5OTM2M2Y3MDk","commit":{"author":{"name":"stefanstokic-oai","email":"stefanstokic@openai.com","date":"2026-06-10T19:19:37Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T19:19:37Z"},"message":"[codex] add external agent import picker UX (#27070)\n\n## Why\n\nUsers need to understand what external-agent data Codex detected, what\nis selected, and how to proceed before an import begins. The updated\npicker makes focus, selection state, and the submission path explicit\nwhile preserving the existing import backend.\n\n## What changed\n\n- replace the old migration prompt with a two-step external-agent import\npicker\n- add a customize view with explicit item focus, selection state,\ncounts, and a review action\n- separate detected import data into a view model\n- add Unix and Windows snapshots for prompt, item-focus, and\naction-focus states\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-tui external_agent_config_migration` (10 passed)\n- manually exercised an isolated TUI fixture covering customization,\nselection toggles, review, import, repeated invocation, and session\nresume\n- the broader `just test -p codex-tui` run passed 2,805 tests, with 2\nunrelated guardian feature-flag failures and 4 skipped tests\n\n## Review note\n\nThis is the largest layer in the stack because the interaction state,\nrendering changes, and required snapshots move together. It remains a\ndraft in case reviewers prefer a further presentation/state split.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. [#27064](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27064): remove the\nstartup migration flow\n2. [#27065](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27065): extract the\npicker renderer\n3. [#27070](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27070): add the\nexternal-agent import picker UX\n4. [#27071](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27071): expose the flow\nthrough `/import`\n\n**This PR is stack item 3.** Draft while the lower stack dependencies\nare reviewed.","tree":{"sha":"1efda847b9a48ae1008892bea83bb3b2bfef62cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/1efda847b9a48ae1008892bea83bb3b2bfef62cf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e3528434cdfb9b822057095c7edbf4c99363f709","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKbjKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7HIQAHJmt9vKIj2pl0dOiy7HfVtU\n3ohl833SFh/zxKaGUc6LMR2HDTzzd5lL7jRU5s8VGEdtxa8sGJBplHuwiTk/Zmwe\njYc6y+x/Oky/xpd93WkAmDMeM9p941XkQQTRhDNLU1qfC5IFXlRHmA0dopzCkEO1\nNMRHqIg096ePXbRmLUnymH8G1WtRaqZk8utObygelSzQqxTo33uc1/jZovtu/nqq\nrcWQ5svrlg5Dc4EC4OQQCtnZW0oDcb9A1jJaQjaNXUyD+aWkFnui9xqPK08ZxYR+\n8xfkZFkZT0vOwytbveOlDEDyqL4qVpQqvio3ouv4WMzMmLU8T7lv21TCdyT6R8QS\nOwHh6Qm3PsDIbC2l/nUtaZR0ZTAPNVv0Hod1Rrwb7XBObUNv8L9iQc9aUbfkLWRX\n1fcsi7PESbMJPkVvjm6KMo5xscPXokwps7yZxK78u18sdY0NeTGPMu/rC7D5C2Qu\nwqBwDe3k2ve7eA8K0+APKQHBGpb9L8itI8O6GZZDo+BRMZ73ylbaTWwXhgiXxHHS\nMu0MgxPN8bFJ62yO1pwrH1HbxhtnsZiJOrIrbjt4UYZRei0fXzY8/RXGTzPKNbuX\nQS2kwCqr1uD1ESZnOR1kZr+bsDc9FmUw0BfR2M3XPNtHTMyLLCjXMMlw1998ZYJ4\nky6JGXSgb0TJqz/qJUM7\n=k81o\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1efda847b9a48ae1008892bea83bb3b2bfef62cf\nparent 13468115fc6443970b8bf521927fceaf58ad35c1\nauthor stefanstokic-oai <stefanstokic@openai.com> 1781119177 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781119177 -0400\n\n[codex] add external agent import picker UX (#27070)\n\n## Why\n\nUsers need to understand what external-agent data Codex detected, what\nis selected, and how to proceed before an import begins. The updated\npicker makes focus, selection state, and the submission path explicit\nwhile preserving the existing import backend.\n\n## What changed\n\n- replace the old migration prompt with a two-step external-agent import\npicker\n- add a customize view with explicit item focus, selection state,\ncounts, and a review action\n- separate detected import data into a view model\n- add Unix and Windows snapshots for prompt, item-focus, and\naction-focus states\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-tui external_agent_config_migration` (10 passed)\n- manually exercised an isolated TUI fixture covering customization,\nselection toggles, review, import, repeated invocation, and session\nresume\n- the broader `just test -p codex-tui` run passed 2,805 tests, with 2\nunrelated guardian feature-flag failures and 4 skipped tests\n\n## Review note\n\nThis is the largest layer in the stack because the interaction state,\nrendering changes, and required snapshots move together. It remains a\ndraft in case reviewers prefer a further presentation/state split.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. [#27064](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27064): remove the\nstartup migration flow\n2. [#27065](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27065): extract the\npicker renderer\n3. [#27070](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27070): add the\nexternal-agent import picker UX\n4. [#27071](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27071): expose the flow\nthrough `/import`\n\n**This PR is stack item 3.** Draft while the lower stack dependencies\nare reviewed.","verified_at":"2026-06-10T19:19:38Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e3528434cdfb9b822057095c7edbf4c99363f709","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e3528434cdfb9b822057095c7edbf4c99363f709","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e3528434cdfb9b822057095c7edbf4c99363f709/comments","author":{"login":"stefanstokic-oai","id":278208182,"node_id":"U_kgDOEJUetg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/278208182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/stefanstokic-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"13468115fc6443970b8bf521927fceaf58ad35c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/13468115fc6443970b8bf521927fceaf58ad35c1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/13468115fc6443970b8bf521927fceaf58ad35c1"}]},{"sha":"13468115fc6443970b8bf521927fceaf58ad35c1","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDEzNDY4MTE1ZmM2NDQzOTcwYjhiZjUyMTkyN2ZjZWFmNThhZDM1YzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Eric Traut","email":"etraut@openai.com","date":"2026-06-10T19:19:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T19:19:26Z"},"message":"Guard core test subprocess cleanup (#27343)\n\n## Why\n\nLocal integration-heavy `codex-core` CLI tests can time out or be\ninterrupted after spawning `codex exec`. Stopping only the direct child\nis not enough: `codex exec` can leave grandchildren behind, including\n`python3`/`python3.12` processes that get reparented to PID 1 and keep\nrunning after the test is gone.\n\nThis PR fixes that failure mode directly for the affected CLI\nintegration tests, without changing production code or reducing local\ntest concurrency.\n\n## What\n\n- Run the `cli_stream` `codex exec` subprocesses through a small private\nwrapper in `core/tests/suite/cli_stream.rs`.\n- Spawn those subprocesses in their own process group before execution.\n- Keep `.output()`-style stdout/stderr capture and the existing\n30-second timeout behavior.\n- Own each spawned process with a drop guard that kills the whole\nprocess group on success, timeout, panic, or other early return.\n\nThe switch from `assert_cmd::Command` to `std::process::Command` is only\nfor these subprocess launches; `assert_cmd` does not expose a pre-spawn\nhook for setting the process group.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-core --test all responses_mode_stream_cli`\n\nThis is limited to core integration tests; it does not change production\n`src` code paths.","tree":{"sha":"f1697926b437207661f1d3982c378b86dc7a099c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f1697926b437207661f1d3982c378b86dc7a099c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/13468115fc6443970b8bf521927fceaf58ad35c1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKbi+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0B8QAEojBrCXoHiCbaGLcWdsVnlT\nlDPNQsZLQ7gk1pFOF68mBPg7BBD9jT7Ef33I5wlJ2il7u57PO7exNcziP5ODJpg4\nm4B6anb5/vElpbLsJI66E0tHrc8BEosTXZZ0sFy4aZcbloUohbozckLuo+WP/3bV\noBRl93osDpGZ51/TGRJ+aRvXurfAT0TyvvlG46KP9DKoBHxrmJHp1jID0+9EC3dO\nsktEIz8hzzqxtP0DL/QXakFJbQk8sOno2UpL6Kj17I4wdOTNt9UN9aT+SQPU/QLe\n+Vb9tFK893Our48ggcxNoVq8kiHhzj9HtYs0iBxggUczpTL/GMZTBtJg0VGm9Uai\nbgWkwBjmc3Ohl9gTj3gBLnHL4VaQcs/V2A9GsRAhbMqh0jUKKa22Q8Bm9+jUzg7Z\nCYOheN/SbrWfuCpBtj0RmG/l7q2FqZxuLL6yMi4Kuh1uMFQw4A2HXe/1gQA7Z6G3\n9cn401Nu47O6RvzGzVLePNy8xajKlu/fCgY0tmAIFXcJVV4Lqw8HQujV8eSD9ZsE\np/66zUQcxmfwbrmVga8JonvxQy1D3JPGY7QHTnpfMQZ3Qwci5vtVULpIh0wg96kj\nmwx92m1IYHNiHVPqXV/sj5YbYS8eA8nRxUJ9O0ggEDNIW2P9+QngZa98OTXyHWQN\nblmLRDJq4PJXIjzTvTno\n=LYLj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f1697926b437207661f1d3982c378b86dc7a099c\nparent 2e377ce5e5bc3da1ca2b133496cbccab3a3d2c01\nauthor Eric Traut <etraut@openai.com> 1781119166 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781119166 -0700\n\nGuard core test subprocess cleanup (#27343)\n\n## Why\n\nLocal integration-heavy `codex-core` CLI tests can time out or be\ninterrupted after spawning `codex exec`. Stopping only the direct child\nis not enough: `codex exec` can leave grandchildren behind, including\n`python3`/`python3.12` processes that get reparented to PID 1 and keep\nrunning after the test is gone.\n\nThis PR fixes that failure mode directly for the affected CLI\nintegration tests, without changing production code or reducing local\ntest concurrency.\n\n## What\n\n- Run the `cli_stream` `codex exec` subprocesses through a small private\nwrapper in `core/tests/suite/cli_stream.rs`.\n- Spawn those subprocesses in their own process group before execution.\n- Keep `.output()`-style stdout/stderr capture and the existing\n30-second timeout behavior.\n- Own each spawned process with a drop guard that kills the whole\nprocess group on success, timeout, panic, or other early return.\n\nThe switch from `assert_cmd::Command` to `std::process::Command` is only\nfor these subprocess launches; `assert_cmd` does not expose a pre-spawn\nhook for setting the process group.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-core --test all responses_mode_stream_cli`\n\nThis is limited to core integration tests; it does not change production\n`src` code paths.","verified_at":"2026-06-10T19:19:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/13468115fc6443970b8bf521927fceaf58ad35c1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/13468115fc6443970b8bf521927fceaf58ad35c1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/13468115fc6443970b8bf521927fceaf58ad35c1/comments","author":{"login":"etraut-openai","id":223546144,"node_id":"U_kgDODVMLIA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/223546144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/etraut-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/etraut-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2e377ce5e5bc3da1ca2b133496cbccab3a3d2c01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2e377ce5e5bc3da1ca2b133496cbccab3a3d2c01","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2e377ce5e5bc3da1ca2b133496cbccab3a3d2c01"}]},{"sha":"2e377ce5e5bc3da1ca2b133496cbccab3a3d2c01","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDJlMzc3Y2U1ZTViYzNkYTFjYTJiMTMzNDk2Y2JjY2FiM2EzZDJjMDE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-10T19:17:15Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T19:17:15Z"},"message":"feat: make ThreadStore available on ThreadExtensionDependencies (#27439)\n\nGenerally useful for extensions.","tree":{"sha":"8efb626425e8deda9e423f83b5d98228fe0c2d63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/8efb626425e8deda9e423f83b5d98228fe0c2d63"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/2e377ce5e5bc3da1ca2b133496cbccab3a3d2c01","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKbg7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyhAQAKU7HUkV4sjKr/o+GAsnXbBb\nEILp0BJIHTgn9xSQLuYG5Vwh9bZjpzX5VNiMALbCiHWagZw8EiDhVBd8j1TkbHxa\n5bBkTNpEfcqCeRBPSIclQ6CQI7SvM88PWHaorM4rfDg6tPUm0y42AgTAjJCAVe9L\nJBZ0lxAvD/oUvVagUoq7CwBXGeDCH8ziHh5jg9a+oEgDFH+gUNKQSu7Td5MQNIZO\nTV7spLdF7Hd1AeGZjpTqaX1naTNCDMTQIn8fJ4zjwp323E4mc0l9cYwVmPpVLIiF\nTQMHBTx76pfIPbo9kdAUlqFma2W0OcwxnfCw0eDsRrBo2hHPcVXkdPVBwIwjj+1v\n0kHMv8jrdiKFZ3TZ3C40vHp3P/flVKi8INr1RydpgBYYxmSSOZ8ZjahdOAGuCA4K\nE1hDCuXrepud6h5VLaqfmdN4CBGDXKKgoPmiLxnRWLsGxf2MRyiDTDYXdwo9UIhV\njFPRPZV+xRHqE3EeeMXxz7QFJp2/Jnw1IAezIknZbeeEm/ePfo7Yf1NNuqBnNAsq\ntI0kHQpT8xn2eM/Pu9ZJLbHDrwJzWDHV4ARCaODUIA5uI7BHWPeoGlo0Cjb6liqK\nyRK62xs66rkxA/PFQ4iwYXtflVoNlSGpbgvDk0S2yQod0sGRNg0t40S34C72u2hr\nq/1J713VfvXp8vZD2iG3\n=Q0TM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8efb626425e8deda9e423f83b5d98228fe0c2d63\nparent 020bf49346efa6c781726c86eda2a59ff415a712\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1781119035 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781119035 -0400\n\nfeat: make ThreadStore available on ThreadExtensionDependencies (#27439)\n\nGenerally useful for extensions.","verified_at":"2026-06-10T19:17:16Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2e377ce5e5bc3da1ca2b133496cbccab3a3d2c01","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2e377ce5e5bc3da1ca2b133496cbccab3a3d2c01","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2e377ce5e5bc3da1ca2b133496cbccab3a3d2c01/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"020bf49346efa6c781726c86eda2a59ff415a712","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/020bf49346efa6c781726c86eda2a59ff415a712","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/020bf49346efa6c781726c86eda2a59ff415a712"}]},{"sha":"020bf49346efa6c781726c86eda2a59ff415a712","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDAyMGJmNDkzNDZlZmE2Yzc4MTcyNmM4NmVkYTJhNTlmZjQxNWE3MTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Alex Daley","email":"adaley@openai.com","date":"2026-06-10T19:01:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T19:01:03Z"},"message":"[plugins] Inject remote_plugin_id into install elicitations (#26409)\n\nSummary\n- Propagate cached remote plugin IDs through Codex plugin discovery.\n- Inject `remote_plugin_id` and connector IDs into\n`request_plugin_install` elicitation `_meta` from the resolved plugin.\n- Keep the remote plugin ID out of the model-facing tool schema,\narguments, and result.\n\nValidation\n- `just test -p codex-tools`\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nlist_tool_suggest_discoverable_plugins_includes_cached_remote_global_plugins`\n- `just fix -p codex-tools`\n- `just fix -p codex-core-plugins`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `just test -p codex-core` was also attempted: 2,581 passed, 55 failed,\nand 1 timed out across unrelated sandbox/environment-sensitive\nintegration tests.","tree":{"sha":"a5fcdfbf495687002e30767db71ea55cfe6c35ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a5fcdfbf495687002e30767db71ea55cfe6c35ba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/020bf49346efa6c781726c86eda2a59ff415a712","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKbRvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkfsQAJo1kD+YfmFfDhlMfaxfiI19\nR9QujoHuoTJUFmFRG/jhLIGiViOLFKtjTK/1OJOjc6irIIBy4gtOu8+/2HAYBrbv\ntPJ3vC8F0G98sESjQB//SHJHbNy3X95p2nDSQVax7djGNuZIVfHTNor8QxpKCVGm\nnAZKqZsWpg/ygkrnNEp2WzG2AKTSU85kSYZ8l9usbwYZecQTmsFeGzEUJqdHAtxX\nBWh7Oxm2/yOwezzPZx/TgnIHJFsNmvrELlHDJg5DcYm4BCljWD8LY4kllAPGngjO\ng7NqGuPsKUNuoTN0UNFawhWKaroFEqlMkhAg73a/78rpOtPrskXxof22Gz9AePJt\nYMiehmvtskRoAblnpjyr+upVqxV2tBmyBejHdn0DtiMJkWVD3x2DMjE6j4IK90dd\nPPxO4m5683EEbHyN0mxO09712JGuUqmTqjEW6xOJ5vZeRg/LPgI3sX2QSwKdShxv\nclgJ1V0BQsDYNwuXr9tBWp+z1JMPoLzZ6lgK8RfBFYvoXUyNs/2ZOFw2CYgPKOFK\nvabVT3EwLiV67i0J5Y0XSqKMXs7MlP+E/pE8+5K7uovwQvuOTaBCkUyC0126OXbU\nrzdr3FcLgX6VtLsF9z1eGeVB5DaI6SbVwAwcRLbPV5tuVfEfHwhhm/xRde0eKAnI\nswgTqInqGLaNmDFPivuI\n=vJ6a\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a5fcdfbf495687002e30767db71ea55cfe6c35ba\nparent 72667f4f41ec5515096ea5676b09cd3c01e6c866\nauthor Alex Daley <adaley@openai.com> 1781118063 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781118063 -0700\n\n[plugins] Inject remote_plugin_id into install elicitations (#26409)\n\nSummary\n- Propagate cached remote plugin IDs through Codex plugin discovery.\n- Inject `remote_plugin_id` and connector IDs into\n`request_plugin_install` elicitation `_meta` from the resolved plugin.\n- Keep the remote plugin ID out of the model-facing tool schema,\narguments, and result.\n\nValidation\n- `just test -p codex-tools`\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nlist_tool_suggest_discoverable_plugins_includes_cached_remote_global_plugins`\n- `just fix -p codex-tools`\n- `just fix -p codex-core-plugins`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `just test -p codex-core` was also attempted: 2,581 passed, 55 failed,\nand 1 timed out across unrelated sandbox/environment-sensitive\nintegration tests.","verified_at":"2026-06-10T19:01:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/020bf49346efa6c781726c86eda2a59ff415a712","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/020bf49346efa6c781726c86eda2a59ff415a712","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/020bf49346efa6c781726c86eda2a59ff415a712/comments","author":{"login":"adaley-openai","id":192042180,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3JUxA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192042180?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/adaley-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adaley-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"72667f4f41ec5515096ea5676b09cd3c01e6c866","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/72667f4f41ec5515096ea5676b09cd3c01e6c866","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/72667f4f41ec5515096ea5676b09cd3c01e6c866"}]},{"sha":"72667f4f41ec5515096ea5676b09cd3c01e6c866","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDcyNjY3ZjRmNDFlYzU1MTUwOTZlYTU2NzZiMDljZDNjMDFlNmM4NjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"stefanstokic-oai","email":"stefanstokic@openai.com","date":"2026-06-10T18:48:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T18:48:30Z"},"message":"[codex] extract external agent import picker renderer (#27065)\n\n## Why\n\nThe external-agent import picker is easier to review when its rendering\nrefactor lands separately from new state and interaction behavior. This\nlayer is intended to be behavior-neutral.\n\n## What changed\n\n- extract external-agent migration rendering into a dedicated `render`\nmodule\n- preserve existing behavior while separating presentation from\ninteraction logic\n- establish a smaller foundation for the import picker UX in the next PR\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-tui external_agent_config_migration` (10 passed)\n\n## Stack\n\n1. [#27064](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27064): remove the\nstartup migration flow\n2. [#27065](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27065): extract the\npicker renderer\n3. [#27070](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27070): add the\nexternal-agent import picker UX\n4. [#27071](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27071): expose the flow\nthrough `/import`\n\n**This PR is stack item 2.** Draft while the lower stack dependency is\nreviewed.","tree":{"sha":"b12e67519867b646e81b0192c26e9892b23ae63f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/b12e67519867b646e81b0192c26e9892b23ae63f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/72667f4f41ec5515096ea5676b09cd3c01e6c866","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKbF+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAN+kQAHJfSQN7D7taIx2UxkN70ECj\nrLHvaW0El/ENRQMPSNtT3TAzrXVSqkWxDH1mv7Tl7Jm35o1887xbMWnUnPnyy4wn\nBBAzsirHJd2Nidy4dlEkd/B6LYZZEYk3pvVmZWgKY633IwkN2i+UeUdQGy+z3CG5\nnTXPGQO02Z2wiOUubPBk/OfRcKxoqiZeT8c4raYjJpH+WaqMM+PJU3SzsAA4OGSJ\nGMlI5fRcdi/MtcBT95dmffVRjGMpJ8QTtJx8yBHl3XdBTEWleFLpduLZ9tkXHkUG\n7M5+FVmY6rqbKrS7Tq4eev0iZXCfk/EMg8aM20OmT2i15noPtp1iU16+AzFj8Qj8\nYRyBJdeDDrTkk/fTIDMncXRIhiGpdw5uzIHQQLnIg0THfXlFzIu7EGSfwUXQgrIx\nTVSmRWEdXqltzrKiNp7j7+Fff1LA4gQ4KA1xYIrtGlQWk4Vu+veKcKOaJLa0AWTT\nbfZ6i+GWoL/3ZwbnH//864Q2yHR5nh6CFfnZId4BZ73Q1jctx1ESffYaBE7D5VYq\nTmba2Ip6IoR/xRaD/iD4LVjpcYKEUbZ22pZv8vfvGzofImm64LaN76zYAEioSOl/\n/YEaW4HzO7JuH+DiyAqnb4+beWrxZdBzbgCa9+yLe1l8khecaQXzHLxRwzRLRHDb\nBlj3bRSXKcGiAeaM25qQ\n=3T6q\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b12e67519867b646e81b0192c26e9892b23ae63f\nparent ccf1a185180428727cffbdd9bd4eaaab2dc218ef\nauthor stefanstokic-oai <stefanstokic@openai.com> 1781117310 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781117310 -0400\n\n[codex] extract external agent import picker renderer (#27065)\n\n## Why\n\nThe external-agent import picker is easier to review when its rendering\nrefactor lands separately from new state and interaction behavior. This\nlayer is intended to be behavior-neutral.\n\n## What changed\n\n- extract external-agent migration rendering into a dedicated `render`\nmodule\n- preserve existing behavior while separating presentation from\ninteraction logic\n- establish a smaller foundation for the import picker UX in the next PR\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-tui external_agent_config_migration` (10 passed)\n\n## Stack\n\n1. [#27064](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27064): remove the\nstartup migration flow\n2. [#27065](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27065): extract the\npicker renderer\n3. [#27070](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27070): add the\nexternal-agent import picker UX\n4. [#27071](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/27071): expose the flow\nthrough `/import`\n\n**This PR is stack item 2.** Draft while the lower stack dependency is\nreviewed.","verified_at":"2026-06-10T18:48:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/72667f4f41ec5515096ea5676b09cd3c01e6c866","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/72667f4f41ec5515096ea5676b09cd3c01e6c866","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/72667f4f41ec5515096ea5676b09cd3c01e6c866/comments","author":{"login":"stefanstokic-oai","id":278208182,"node_id":"U_kgDOEJUetg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/278208182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/stefanstokic-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stefanstokic-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ccf1a185180428727cffbdd9bd4eaaab2dc218ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ccf1a185180428727cffbdd9bd4eaaab2dc218ef","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ccf1a185180428727cffbdd9bd4eaaab2dc218ef"}]},{"sha":"ccf1a185180428727cffbdd9bd4eaaab2dc218ef","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGNjZjFhMTg1MTgwNDI4NzI3Y2ZmYmRkOWJkNGVhYWFiMmRjMjE4ZWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"kbazzi","email":"kbazzi@openai.com","date":"2026-06-10T18:46:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-10T18:46:57Z"},"message":"[codex] Retry transient Guardian review failures (#27062)\n\n## Background\n\nCodex can use **Auto Review** for permission requests. Instead of asking\nthe user immediately, Codex starts a separate locked-down reviewer\nsession called **Guardian**, which returns a structured `allow` or\n`deny` assessment.\n\nThe Guardian reviewer is itself a Codex session, so its model request\ncan fail for transient infrastructure reasons such as model overload,\nHTTP connection failure, or response-stream disconnect. Today, any such\nfailure immediately ends the Auto Review attempt and blocks the action.\n\nThis PR adds bounded retries for failures that the existing protocol\nexplicitly identifies as transient.\n\nLinear context:\n[CA-539](https://linear.app/openai/issue/CA-539/retry-auto-review-infrastructure-failures-and-fall-back-to-manual)\n\n## What changes\n\nA Guardian review can now make at most **three total attempts**:\n\n1. Run the review normally.\n2. Retry after a jittered delay of roughly 180–220 ms if the first\nattempt fails with an eligible error.\n3. Retry after a jittered delay of roughly 360–440 ms if the second\nattempt also fails with an eligible error.\n\nAll attempts share the original review deadline. Jitter spreads retries\nfrom concurrent clients to reduce synchronized load during broader\noutages. The retries do not reset the user's maximum wait time, and the\nbackoff waits terminate early if the review is cancelled or the deadline\nexpires.\n\nBefore retrying, the existing Guardian session lifecycle decides whether\nthe session remains usable. Healthy trunks are reused, broken trunks are\nremoved by the existing cleanup path, and ephemeral sessions continue to\nclean themselves up.\n\nThe review still emits one logical lifecycle to clients. Recoverable\nintermediate failures do not produce warnings or terminal events.\n\n## Retry policy\n\n### Retried up to twice\n\n- model/server overload\n- HTTP connection failure\n- response-stream connection failure\n- response-stream disconnect\n- internal server error\n- a final reviewer message that cannot be parsed as the required\nGuardian assessment\n\n### Not retried\n\n- bad or invalid requests\n- authentication failures\n- usage limits\n- cyber-policy failures\n- errors without a structured category\n- a request that already exhausted the lower-level Responses retry\nbudget\n- a completed Guardian turn with no assessment payload\n- prompt-construction failures\n- Guardian review timeout\n- cancellation or abort\n- a valid `deny` assessment\n\nThe session-error classification uses `ErrorEvent.codex_error_info`; it\ndoes not inspect error-message strings.\n\n## Implementation notes\n\n- `wait_for_guardian_review` preserves the complete `ErrorEvent`,\nincluding structured `codex_error_info`.\n- Guardian session failures preserve the original message and optional\nstructured `CodexErrorInfo`.\n- The retry policy classifies the explicitly transient `CodexErrorInfo`\nvariants; unknown, absent, and deterministic categories are not retried.\n- The Guardian session manager receives the caller's deadline rather\nthan creating a new timeout per attempt.\n- Analytics record the final `attempt_count`.\n- Retry orchestration does not add a separate session-cleanup protocol;\nit relies on the existing trunk and ephemeral lifecycle decisions.\n\n## Automated testing\n\nFocused Guardian coverage verifies:\n\n- every supported transient `CodexErrorInfo` is classified as retryable,\nwhile absent and non-transient categories are not;\n- structured transient session failure -> retry -> approval with the\nhealthy trunk reused;\n- two invalid Guardian responses -> third attempt -> approval, with\nexactly three requests;\n- three invalid responses -> existing fail-closed result, with exactly\nthree requests and one terminal lifecycle;\n- valid denial, missing payload, invalid request, timeout, cancellation,\nand prompt/session construction failures are not retried;\n- retry eligibility ends after the third attempt;\n- retry delays use the shared exponential backoff helper and remain\nwithin the expected jitter bounds;\n- cancellation and deadline expiry interrupt the backoff wait;\n- healthy trunks are reused across retryable failures;\n- broken event streams remove the trunk through the existing lifecycle\ncleanup;\n- an ephemeral retry does not disturb a concurrent trunk review.\n\nValidation performed:\n\n- `just test -p codex-core guardian_review_\nguardian_ephemeral_retry_preserves_parallel_trunk_and_fork_history\nrun_review_removes_trunk_when_event_stream_is_broken` — **42 passed**;\n- `just test -p codex-analytics` — **71 passed**;\n- scoped Clippy fixes for `codex-core` and `codex-analytics` passed.\n\nA prior full `codex-core` run had unrelated environment-sensitive\nfailures outside Guardian coverage.\n\n## Manual QA\n\nThe focused integration tests use the local mock Responses server to\ninspect exact request counts and emitted lifecycle events. They confirm\nthat retries are internal, a successful later attempt supplies the final\ndecision, non-retryable failures issue only one request, and exhausted\nretries emit only one terminal result.","tree":{"sha":"9ca2c3c0ed6072b50035262f1160f2b9faa0f721","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/9ca2c3c0ed6072b50035262f1160f2b9faa0f721"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/ccf1a185180428727cffbdd9bd4eaaab2dc218ef","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqKbEiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2WUQABxUCM015JpgZgWM/D6tNvQH\nJ8GmPv7Usu3kBLQoRUYH0JA8205we4++UTepXIzqWrDSMDubVYCxJcRw5Hb0lzdi\npXC34buzMi21JRVAMNpexW5c9oPrSDfMiMv70aQrTrqh4is1Mw6lAqJ3dvNbmB1D\nvBFpOlOa8gbBJ1XO5z9pH/ke+hS8sV06Y07mcUbbA2LZ/aNdqAo4fsBxoEidqNUd\nVboTc+7uFhP1SwNC5g6dSLo8D42gK/X1WrA2LtMFrsJ/SH8xcxurei0tdGF6Fgyo\n2fgL+JeqUZs9B7sAltvuzsXaqpNwYckSIsQ1GLVeJYFwgUakvS8H1TArAFp3v9DE\njl+fWriPZbYdLgB+DHAi16fwAq68i2T1N0DEYXxsy+hEupFWK2tubJ68QtLojvOz\nXNzoK4Qww6hKFoupuoMGwK6aFQ9xzKvxlkx9Pdosmyi4tbLXBq+bgCsxOY5S7mje\necImD6WVswMYX/EBcp/W4nSOqvYGgg3o1gaWSNG6gDoL3ftJCdtcMOmCHsjhZzZI\n5pvYUnxTcPjC007IM4eXTiDf1q+zxNEnLIe4TF+cav2pBpIjYnXncBbAKV6aldgV\nrFpQ2Ehmpbjx/od2oEeXq2yJRbu6pFVhgitodFdWjnj24F3ja3A/Ty/I5F/C63if\nOhw0slVTyovZX3RlGuia\n=b3xm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9ca2c3c0ed6072b50035262f1160f2b9faa0f721\nparent 42415443d036c374eb848caec69b5714e9681b35\nauthor kbazzi <kbazzi@openai.com> 1781117217 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781117217 -0700\n\n[codex] Retry transient Guardian review failures (#27062)\n\n## Background\n\nCodex can use **Auto Review** for permission requests. Instead of asking\nthe user immediately, Codex starts a separate locked-down reviewer\nsession called **Guardian**, which returns a structured `allow` or\n`deny` assessment.\n\nThe Guardian reviewer is itself a Codex session, so its model request\ncan fail for transient infrastructure reasons such as model overload,\nHTTP connection failure, or response-stream disconnect. Today, any such\nfailure immediately ends the Auto Review attempt and blocks the action.\n\nThis PR adds bounded retries for failures that the existing protocol\nexplicitly identifies as transient.\n\nLinear context:\n[CA-539](https://linear.app/openai/issue/CA-539/retry-auto-review-infrastructure-failures-and-fall-back-to-manual)\n\n## What changes\n\nA Guardian review can now make at most **three total attempts**:\n\n1. Run the review normally.\n2. Retry after a jittered delay of roughly 180–220 ms if the first\nattempt fails with an eligible error.\n3. Retry after a jittered delay of roughly 360–440 ms if the second\nattempt also fails with an eligible error.\n\nAll attempts share the original review deadline. Jitter spreads retries\nfrom concurrent clients to reduce synchronized load during broader\noutages. The retries do not reset the user's maximum wait time, and the\nbackoff waits terminate early if the review is cancelled or the deadline\nexpires.\n\nBefore retrying, the existing Guardian session lifecycle decides whether\nthe session remains usable. Healthy trunks are reused, broken trunks are\nremoved by the existing cleanup path, and ephemeral sessions continue to\nclean themselves up.\n\nThe review still emits one logical lifecycle to clients. Recoverable\nintermediate failures do not produce warnings or terminal events.\n\n## Retry policy\n\n### Retried up to twice\n\n- model/server overload\n- HTTP connection failure\n- response-stream connection failure\n- response-stream disconnect\n- internal server error\n- a final reviewer message that cannot be parsed as the required\nGuardian assessment\n\n### Not retried\n\n- bad or invalid requests\n- authentication failures\n- usage limits\n- cyber-policy failures\n- errors without a structured category\n- a request that already exhausted the lower-level Responses retry\nbudget\n- a completed Guardian turn with no assessment payload\n- prompt-construction failures\n- Guardian review timeout\n- cancellation or abort\n- a valid `deny` assessment\n\nThe session-error classification uses `ErrorEvent.codex_error_info`; it\ndoes not inspect error-message strings.\n\n## Implementation notes\n\n- `wait_for_guardian_review` preserves the complete `ErrorEvent`,\nincluding structured `codex_error_info`.\n- Guardian session failures preserve the original message and optional\nstructured `CodexErrorInfo`.\n- The retry policy classifies the explicitly transient `CodexErrorInfo`\nvariants; unknown, absent, and deterministic categories are not retried.\n- The Guardian session manager receives the caller's deadline rather\nthan creating a new timeout per attempt.\n- Analytics record the final `attempt_count`.\n- Retry orchestration does not add a separate session-cleanup protocol;\nit relies on the existing trunk and ephemeral lifecycle decisions.\n\n## Automated testing\n\nFocused Guardian coverage verifies:\n\n- every supported transient `CodexErrorInfo` is classified as retryable,\nwhile absent and non-transient categories are not;\n- structured transient session failure -> retry -> approval with the\nhealthy trunk reused;\n- two invalid Guardian responses -> third attempt -> approval, with\nexactly three requests;\n- three invalid responses -> existing fail-closed result, with exactly\nthree requests and one terminal lifecycle;\n- valid denial, missing payload, invalid request, timeout, cancellation,\nand prompt/session construction failures are not retried;\n- retry eligibility ends after the third attempt;\n- retry delays use the shared exponential backoff helper and remain\nwithin the expected jitter bounds;\n- cancellation and deadline expiry interrupt the backoff wait;\n- healthy trunks are reused across retryable failures;\n- broken event streams remove the trunk through the existing lifecycle\ncleanup;\n- an ephemeral retry does not disturb a concurrent trunk review.\n\nValidation performed:\n\n- `just test -p codex-core guardian_review_\nguardian_ephemeral_retry_preserves_parallel_trunk_and_fork_history\nrun_review_removes_trunk_when_event_stream_is_broken` — **42 passed**;\n- `just test -p codex-analytics` — **71 passed**;\n- scoped Clippy fixes for `codex-core` and `codex-analytics` passed.\n\nA prior full `codex-core` run had unrelated environment-sensitive\nfailures outside Guardian coverage.\n\n## Manual QA\n\nThe focused integration tests use the local mock Responses server to\ninspect exact request counts and emitted lifecycle events. They confirm\nthat retries are internal, a successful later attempt supplies the final\ndecision, non-retryable failures issue only one request, and exhausted\nretries emit only one terminal result.","verified_at":"2026-06-10T18:46:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ccf1a185180428727cffbdd9bd4eaaab2dc218ef","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ccf1a185180428727cffbdd9bd4eaaab2dc218ef","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ccf1a185180428727cffbdd9bd4eaaab2dc218ef/comments","author":{"login":"kbazzi","id":289796993,"node_id":"U_kgDOEUXzgQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/289796993?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi","html_url":"https://github.com/kbazzi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbazzi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"42415443d036c374eb848caec69b5714e9681b35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/42415443d036c374eb848caec69b5714e9681b35","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/42415443d036c374eb848caec69b5714e9681b35"}]}]